irst-group-of-ten-stone-formations-place_m9NrjzE.jpg','First group of ten stone formations, placed within the Mandir, are regarded as sacred and are linked to the site’s origin story. (Source: CKA Archives)','First group of ten stone formations, placed within the Mandir, are regarded as sacred and are linked to the site’s origin story. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8950,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/second-group-of-the-peculiar-ten-stone-fo_CsibZfc.jpg','Second group of the peculiar ten stone formations, forming part of the original discovery that led to the establishment of the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','Second group of the peculiar ten stone formations, forming part of the original discovery that led to the establishment of the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8952,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/surrounding-greenery-near-the-jambhaljai-_PfbLwSk.jpg','Surrounding greenery near the Jambhaljai Mata Mandir, which is usually used as grazing space for livestock and serves as a resting point for travellers. (Source: CKA Archives)','Surrounding greenery near the Jambhaljai Mata Mandir, which is usually used as grazing space for livestock and serves as a resting point for travellers. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8954,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/front-view-of-the-jangli-maharaj-mandir-i_TNuprT3.png','Front view of the Jangli Maharaj Mandir in Shivaji Nagar, Pune.[24]','Front view of the Jangli Maharaj Mandir in Shivaji Nagar, Pune.[24]',NULL),(8958,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/a-view-of-jivdhan-fort-in-junnar-pune-sou_Ho2arwA.jpg','A view of Jivdhan Fort in Junnar, Pune (Source: CKA Archives)','A view of Jivdhan Fort in Junnar, Pune (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8960,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/vanarlingi-pinnacle-located-on-the-same-h_dzrvJ98.jpg','Vanarlingi Pinnacle, located on the same hill as Jivdhan Fort. The fort’s elevated position provided strategic oversight of the Naneghat Pass. (Source: CKA Archives)','Vanarlingi Pinnacle, located on the same hill as Jivdhan Fort. The fort’s elevated position provided strategic oversight of the Naneghat Pass. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8963,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/bhau-joshi-l-created-a-permanent-museum-f_a19jnzH.jpg','Bhau Joshi (L) created a permanent museum for miniature railway models after the success of his initial exhibitions in Pune and Mumbai.[25]','Bhau Joshi (L) created a permanent museum for miniature railway models after the success of his initial exhibitions in Pune and Mumbai.[25]',NULL),(8965,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-joshis-museum-of-miniature-railways-i_6nf1weo.jpg','The Joshi’s Museum of Miniature Railways in Kothrud showcases detail oriented miniatures forming an entire city.[26]','The Joshi’s Museum of Miniature Railways in Kothrud showcases detail oriented miniatures forming an entire city.[26]',NULL),(8969,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-chaityagriha-of-karla-caves-lonavala-_2qVSKaD.png','The chaityagriha of Karla Caves, Lonavala, Pune district, which is considered by many to be among the finest and best-preserved examples of its kind in India.[27]','The chaityagriha of Karla Caves, Lonavala, Pune district, which is considered by many to be among the finest and best-preserved examples of its kind in India.[27]',NULL),(8971,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/carvings-in-the-karla-caves-near-lonavala_2VbNMeA.jpg','Carvings in the Karla Caves near Lonavala. (Source: Vignesh Jaiswal)','Carvings in the Karla Caves near Lonavala. (Source: Vignesh Jaiswal)',NULL),(8974,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/exterior-of-kasba-ganpati-mandir-located-_g5L1UD3.jpg','Exterior of Kasba Ganpati Mandir, located in Kasba Peth and regarded as the gramdevta Mandir of Pune. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior of Kasba Ganpati Mandir, located in Kasba Peth and regarded as the gramdevta 