ne/cultural-sites/a-tile-plaque-near-the-entrance-displays-_ZlUSdhv.jpg','A tile plaque near the entrance displays Tilak leading Ganpati celebrations in Pune with passionate drumming beats and onlookers getting energised by this celebration. (Source: CKA Archives)','A tile plaque near the entrance displays Tilak leading Ganpati celebrations in Pune with passionate drumming beats and onlookers getting energised by this celebration. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8987,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-ganesh-murti-enshrined-by-lokmanya-ti_Askn23E.jpg','The Ganesh murti enshrined by Lokmanya Tilak in 1893, recognised as the “Manacha Pachva Ganpati” (the fifth respected Ganpati) among Pune’s Manache Ganpati. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Ganesh murti enshrined by Lokmanya Tilak in 1893, recognised as the “Manacha Pachva Ganpati” (the fifth respected Ganpati) among Pune’s Manache Ganpati. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8989,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-magnificent-tilak-statue-with-the-kes_Qj9i9gJ.jpg','The magnificent Tilak statue with the Kesari Wada Ganpati in the front. A noticeable feature is the background depicting several figures from India’s freedom movement like Dadabhai Naoroji, Gopal Krishna Gokhale, Justice Mahadeo Govind Ranade, Gopal Ganesh Agarkar, Lala Lajpat Rai, Bipin Chandra Pal, Sri Aurobindo Ghose, Vinayak Damodar Savarkar, and others. (Source: CKA Archives)','The magnificent Tilak statue with the Kesari Wada Ganpati in the front. A noticeable feature is the background depicting several figures from India’s freedom movement like Dadabhai Naoroji, Gopal Krishna Gokhale, Justice Mahadeo Govind Ranade, Gopal Ganesh Agarkar, Lala Lajpat Rai, Bipin Chandra Pal, Sri Aurobindo Ghose, Vinayak Damodar Savarkar, and others. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8991,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-eastern-wing-of-the-kesari-wada-as-me_s6D13OY.jpg','The eastern wing of the Kesari Wada, as mentioned above, served as Tilak’s residence. Preserved to reflect its original layout, the space offers a glimpse into the private life of one of India’s foremost nationalist leaders. (Source: CKA Archives)','The eastern wing of the Kesari Wada, as mentioned above, served as Tilak’s residence. Preserved to reflect its original layout, the space offers a glimpse into the private life of one of India’s foremost nationalist leaders. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(8994,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/front-view-of-the-khunya-murlidhar-mandir_igFXJk4.png','Front view of the Khunya Murlidhar Mandir, Sadashiv Peth, Pune.[28]','Front view of the Khunya Murlidhar Mandir, Sadashiv Peth, Pune.[28]',NULL),(8998,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-staircase-believed-to-have-once-led-t_46YVUF7.png','The staircase believed to have once led to the western gate of Killa-e-Hissar, known as Konkan Darwaja. Though now paved, historians note that the alignment and layout remain largely unchanged. These steps are thought to have been used for centuries, connecting the fort to surrounding settlements that eventually formed Kasabe Pune, what is now Kasba Peth.[29]','The staircase believed to have once led to the western gate of Killa-e-Hissar, known as Konkan Darwaja. Though now paved, historians note that the alignment and layout remain largely unchanged. These steps are thought to have been used for centuries, connecting the fort to surrounding settlements that eventually formed Kasabe Pune, what is now Kasba Peth.[29]',NULL),(9002,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/an-archival-photograph-of-dr-br-ambedkar-_G3dn7H8.png','An archival photograph of Dr. B.R. Ambedkar at Bhima Koregaon, Pune. Dr. Ambedkar visited the Koregaon Ranstambh annually on 1 January to honour the Mahar soldiers who fought in the 1818 battle. His visits transformed the site into a place of collective memory and a symbol of resistance against caste-based oppression.[30]','An archival photograph of Dr. B.R. Ambedkar at Bhima Koregaon, Pune. Dr. Ambedkar visited the Koregaon Ranstambh annually on 1 January to honour the Mahar soldiers who fought in the 1818 battle. His visits transformed the site into a place of collective memory and a symbol of resistance against caste-based oppression.[30]',NULL),(9006,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-anterior-of-lal-mahal-at-kasba-peth-p_SVrLHBd.jpg','The anterior of Lal Mahal at Kasba Peth, Pune.[31]','The anterior of Lal Mahal at Kasba Peth, Pune.[31]',NULL),(9007,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-wooden-panels-of-lal-mahal-source-cka_Qd3pqQX.jpg','The wooden panels of Lal Mahal. (Source: CKA Archives)','The wooden panels of Lal Mahal. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(9008,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-bust-of-rajmata-jijabai-within-lal-ma_YImdGrJ.jpg','The bust of Rajmata Jijabai within Lal Mahal.[32]','The bust of Rajmata Jijabai within Lal Mahal.[32]',NULL),(9010,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/the-oil-painting-at-lal-mahal-depicting-s_IInR7VG.png','The oil painting at Lal Mahal depicting Shaista Khan’s narrow escape from Shivaji Maharaj.[33]','The oil painting at Lal Mahal depicting Shaista Khan’s narrow escape from Shivaji Maharaj.[33]',NULL),(9012,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/a-view-of-lal-mahal-from-the-boundary-wal_X6HcaRe.jpg','A view of Lal Mahal from the boundary walls of Shaniwar Wada. (Source: CKA Archives)','A view of Lal Mahal from the boundary walls of Shaniwar Wada. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(9014,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/limbraj-maharaj-vitthal-mandir-budhwar-pe_0JiW7Hq.png','Limbraj Maharaj Vitthal Mandir, Budhwar Peth, Pune.[34]','Limbraj Maharaj Vitthal Mandir, Budhwar Peth, Pune.[34]',NULL),(9018,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/cultural-sites/a-bronze-statue-of-maharshi-dhondo-keshav_skXioPn.jpg','A bronze statue of Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve in the middle of his samadhi.[35]