dpanthi style and facing north. (Source: Purattatva)[1]',''),(10424,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-entrance-of-the-mahadev-mandir-featuri_jNTBqCs.jpg','The entrance of the Mahadev Mandir, featuring a brick and mortar wall (a later addition) painted in a faded pink color. (Source: YouTube @/RJ Dipak Wankhade)','The entrance of the Mahadev Mandir, featuring a brick and mortar wall (a later addition) painted in a faded pink color. (Source: YouTube @/RJ Dipak Wankhade)',''),(10428,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/moreshwar-mandir-in-barshi-takli-highlight_rx4GE2Q.jpg','Moreshwar Mandir in Barshi Takli, highlighted in vibrant yellow, green, red, orange, and pink colors, blending Hemadpanthi form with a masjid-like exterior. (Source: CKA Archives)','Moreshwar Mandir in Barshi Takli, highlighted in vibrant yellow, green, red, orange, and pink colors, blending Hemadpanthi form with a masjid-like exterior. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10431,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-balapur-chhatri-stands-on-a-high-platf_1OHMgt2.jpg','The Balapur Chhatri stands on a high platform by the river, with five domes supported by twenty pillars and is built in a Rajputana style. (Source: Akola City Word Press)[2]','The Balapur Chhatri stands on a high platform by the river, with five domes supported by twenty pillars and is built in a Rajputana style. (Source: Akola City Word Press)[2]',''),(10435,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/a-gateway-leading-into-balapur-fort-reflec_2kkPb1a.jpg','A gateway leading into Balapur Fort, reflecting Indo-Islamic architectural elements. (Source: CKA Archives)','A gateway leading into Balapur Fort, reflecting Indo-Islamic architectural elements. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10441,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-large-door-of-the-house-has-a-space-wh_1KWTEnm.jpg','The large door of the house has a space where vegetable vendors sit and sell vegetables. The devlis on the left side of the door, provide much-needed light in the evenings for the vendors. (Source: CKA Archives)','The large door of the house has a space where vegetable vendors sit and sell vegetables. The devlis on the left side of the door, provide much-needed light in the evenings for the vendors. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10443,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-intricately-designed-entrance-door-of-_xBqFY4R.jpg','The intricately designed entrance door of an old structure, showcasing traditional stone masonry and detailed carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)','The intricately designed entrance door of an old structure, showcasing traditional stone masonry and detailed carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10444,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-house-features-several-exterior-doors-_lB5oJ5F.jpg','The house features several exterior doors, each with its own detailing. One such door is flanked by ‘Konades’ on either side. Konades are small niches used to place lamps at night. (Source: CKA Archives)','The house features several exterior doors, each with its own detailing. One such door is flanked by ‘Konades’ on either side. Konades are small niches used to place lamps at night. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10445,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/these-doors-at-the-exteriors-feature-a-dis_Tij5CQB.jpg','These doors at the exteriors feature a distinct panelled design that open differently from the typical double-leaf doors elsewhere in the house. Their construction appears more utilitarian, likely tailored for commercial access rather than domestic use. (Source: CKA Archives)','These doors at the exteriors feature a distinct panelled design that open differently from the typical double-leaf doors elsewhere in the house. Their construction appears more utilitarian, likely tailored for commercial access rather than domestic use. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10447,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/a-window-decorated-with-an-arched-brick-fr_LBScUeh.jpg','A window decorated with an arched brick frame, showcasing local masonry skills of the time. (Source: CKA Archives)','A window decorated with an arched brick frame, showcasing local masonry skills of the time. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10449,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/street-view-of-the-balcony-railings-source_pR9b2bN.jpg','Street view of the balcony railings. (Source: CKA Archives)','Street view of the balcony railings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10450,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/view-of-the-balcony-railings-from-the-insi_nKemxzX.jpg','View of the balcony railings from the inside. (Source: CKA Archives)','View of the balcony railings from the inside. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10452,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/a-traditional-roshandan-originally-designe_jMaHUNw.jpg','A traditional roshandan, originally designed for ventilation and natural light, placed high on the wall to support airflow in upper levels. In this home, as with many homes in the area, it has been subtly repurposed to accommodate electrical wiring.(Source: CKA Archives)','A traditional roshandan, originally designed for ventilation and natural light, placed high on the wall to support airflow in upper levels. In this home, as with many homes in the area, it has been subtly repurposed to accommodate electrical wiring.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10454,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/old-haud-which-is-now-covered-with-cement-_bAMzpPE.jpg','Old Haud which is now covered with cement. (Source: CKA Archives)','Old Haud which is now covered with cement. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10456,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/the-old-waste-waterway-used-for-drainage-a_wFmcQ4h.jpg','The old waste waterway, used for drainage and possibly to water a traditional Parasbaug (kitchen garden). This system was common in older homes. (Source: CKA Archives)','The old waste waterway, used for drainage and possibly to water a traditional Parasbaug (kitchen garden). This system was common in older homes. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10458,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/traditional-kitchen-spaces-with-provision-_idX04xo.jpg','Traditional kitchen spaces with provision for LPG Gas. (Source: CKA Archives)','Traditional kitchen spaces with provision for LPG Gas. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10459,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/chul-claystove-historically-used-for-cooki_4RZtIyO.jpg','‘Chul’ (Claystove) historically used for cooking. (Source: CKA Archives)','‘Chul’ (Claystove) historically used for cooking. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10462,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/front-view-of-the-house-the-front-door-is-_vhKH3Kr.jpg','Front view of the house. The front door is decorated with beautiful embellishments. (Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the house. The front door is decorated with beautiful embellishments. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10464,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/wooden-door-featuring-intricate-carvings-s_6xo9psx.jpg','Wooden door featuring intricate carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden door featuring intricate carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10465,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/interior-doors-made-up-of-plywood-finished_zV5I1s9.jpg','Interior doors made up of plywood, finished with printed laminate. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior doors made up of plywood, finished with printed laminate. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10467,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/tall-window-near-the-staircase-notice-how-_xEaMy8U.jpg','Tall window near the staircase. Notice how the tall arched window illuminates the staircase. (Source: CKA Archives)','Tall window near the staircase. Notice how the tall arched window illuminates the staircase. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10468,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/window-with-ms-grills-and-aluminium-slidin_whqKPSP.jpg','Window with MS grills and aluminium sliding doors. This window is in stark contrast with the decorative windows used in other houses. (Source: CKA Archives)','Window with MS grills and aluminium sliding doors. This window is in stark contrast with the decorative windows used in other houses. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10470,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/a-clerestory-window-positioned-high-on-the_m9TiJsu.jpg','A Clerestory window positioned high on the wall for ventilation which is similar in function and placement to traditional roshandans, though constructed with contemporary materials. (Source: CKA Archives)','A Clerestory window positioned high on the wall for ventilation which is similar in function and placement to traditional roshandans, though constructed with contemporary materials. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10471,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/architecture/exterior-view-of-the-clerestory-window-sho_6rDBnD2.jpg','Exterior view of the clerestory window, showing its high placement for airflow. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior view of the clerestory window, showing its high placement for airflow. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10483,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/artforms/a-member-of-the-warkari-community-carrying-an-_Mb3kkPc.png','A member of the Warkari community carrying an ektari performs Bhajan and Kirtan.[1]','A member of the Warkari community carrying an ektari performs Bhajan and Kirtan.[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warkari'),(10486,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/artforms/a-pingala-artist-dressed-in-their-traditional-_kt2Zf52.jpg','A Pingala artist, dressed in their traditional attire[2]','A Pingala artist, dressed in their traditional attire[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A4%AA%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%B3%E0%A4%BE.jpg'),(10492,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/artforms/dawali-a-bamboo-basket-used-for-storing-rotis3_ywenB3P.png','Dawali, a bamboo basket used for storing rotis[3]','Dawali, a