aj_Cnnon_Narnala_fort.jpg'),(10570,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/patur-caves-that-are-said-to-have-been-c_xATd2Ch.jpg','Patur Caves that are said to have been carved out by the Vakatakas[13]','Patur Caves that are said to have been carved out by the Vakatakas[13]','https://maharashtratourism.gov.in/tourist-intrests/caves/'),(10572,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/petikashirsha-brahmi-inscriptions-source_fF9k5Tn.jpg','Petikashirsha Brahmi inscriptions (Source: CKA Archives)','Petikashirsha Brahmi inscriptions (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10575,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/the-siddeshwar-mandir-at-kothali-source-_Hu1fIta.jpg','The Siddeshwar Mandir at Kothali (Source: CKA Archives)','The Siddeshwar Mandir at Kothali (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10578,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/sundarabai-khandelwal-tower-stands-tall-_hVbQIWa.jpg','Sundarabai Khandelwal Tower stands tall in the city of Akola (Source: CKA Archives)','Sundarabai Khandelwal Tower stands tall in the city of Akola (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10581,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/a-gateway-on-the-bhairavgad-fort14-c966b3d8.jpg','A gateway on the Bhairavgad Fort[14]','A gateway on the Bhairavgad Fort[14]','https://gunjan282.wordpress.com/2019/11/10/wari-bhairaogad-fort-on-the-bank-of-wan-river/'),(10583,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/a-wall-on-the-bhairavgad-fort15-e5899a6f.jpg','A wall on the Bhairavgad Fort[15]','A wall on the Bhairavgad Fort[15]','https://gunjan282.wordpress.com/2019/11/10/wari-bhairaogad-fort-on-the-bank-of-wan-river/'),(10584,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/cultural-sites/a-wall-at-the-fort-one-can-notice-the-br_JGwuzc8.jpg','A wall at the fort, one can notice the brick walls[16]','A wall at the fort, one can notice the brick walls[16]','https://gunjan282.wordpress.com/2019/11/10/wari-bhairaogad-fort-on-the-bank-of-wan-river/'),(10603,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/festivals-fairs/nandi-bail-facing-shiv-bhagwaan-with-a-_WHtUD1c.png','Nandi Bail facing Shiv Bhagwaan, with a Shivlinga beside them[1]','Nandi Bail facing Shiv Bhagwaan, with a Shivlinga beside them[1]','https://media.assettype.com/esakal%2F2024-08-18%2Fid98x2wt%2FRushikesh%20Salvi%20Esakal%20(33).jpg?w=1024&auto=format%2Ccompress&fit=max'),(10606,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/festivals-fairs/rajeshwar-yatra2-252638fb.png','Rajeshwar Yatra[2]','Rajeshwar Yatra[2]','https://www.esakal.com/akola/this-time-too-there-is-no-yatra-coronavirus-curfew-on-rajeshwar-temple-procession-route-akola-news-nad86'),(10609,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/festivals-fairs/sakharam-maharaj-yatrautsav3-27b74251.png','Sakharam Maharaj Yatrautsav[3]','Sakharam Maharaj Yatrautsav[3]','https://www.esakal.com/jalgaon/palkhi-procession-of-sant-sakharam-maharaj-was-carried-out-on-buddha-purnima-jalgaon-news-gbp00'),(10642,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/markets/jainam-fashion-jewellery-gandhi-market-road1-8d3a42a5.png','Jainam Fashion Jewellery, Gandhi Market Road[1]','Jainam Fashion Jewellery, Gandhi Market Road[1]','https://www.justdial.com/Akola/Jainam-Fashion-Jewellery-Akola-Gandhi-Chowk/9999PX724-X724-210213103752-Q4W2_BZDET'),(10649,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/markets/shree-mall-murtizapur-road2-500e9bdd.png','Shree Mall, Murtizapur Road[2]','Shree Mall, Murtizapur Road[2]','https://www.justdial.com/Akola/Electronic-Goods-Showrooms-in-Murtizapur/nct-10185144'),(10650,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/markets/vegetable-wholesalersmurtizapur-road3-89f2d125.png','Vegetable WholesalersMurtizapur Road[3]','Vegetable WholesalersMurtizapur Road[3]','https://www.justdial.com/Akola/Vegetable-Wholesalers-in-Murtizapur/nct-10516820/page-4'),(10658,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/markets/shri-vishwakarma-glass-in-tilak-road-akola4-2a52c405.png','Shri Vishwakarma Glass in Tilak Road, Akola[4]','Shri Vishwakarma Glass in Tilak Road, Akola[4]','https://www.justdial.com/Akola/Shri-Vishwakarma-Glass-Near-Manik-Talkies-Tilak-Road/9999PX724-X724-191126170106-N9X6_BZDET'),(10665,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/kabaddi-known-locally-as-hututu-is-one-of-_11Kk5FN.jpg','Kabaddi, known locally as Hututu, is one of the oldest and most beloved traditional games in Akola. Originating from ancient times, this game is played on local soil without the need for expensive equipment, making it accessible to everyone (Source: CKA Archives).','Kabaddi, known locally as Hututu, is one of the oldest and most beloved traditional games in Akola. Originating from ancient times, this game is played on local soil without the need for expensive equipment, making it accessible to everyone (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10670,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/champol-is-another-traditional-game-played_WshVXhv.jpg','Champol is another traditional game played in villages, often referred to as a local version of the board game Ludo. (Source: CKA Archives)','Champol is another traditional game played in villages, often referred to as a local version of the board game Ludo. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10676,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/in-the-lagori-game-a-ball-made-of-plastic-_VWHR1xq.jpg','In the Lagori game, a ball made of plastic or rubber and seven flat stones or discs are used (Source: CKA Archives).','In the Lagori game, a ball made of plastic or rubber and seven flat stones or discs are used (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10679,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/kancha-is-a-traditional-game-played-with-g_pEZSRyE.jpg','Kancha is a traditional game played with glass marbles, which are inexpensive and commonly available. For just one rupee, one can get 4 marbles (Source: CKA Archives).','Kancha is a traditional game played with glass marbles, which are inexpensive and commonly available. For just one rupee, one can get 4 marbles (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10682,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/children-playingpakhani-also-known-as-gara_bPJK4OZ.jpg','Children PlayingPakhani, also known as Garadya,(Source: CKA Archives).','Children PlayingPakhani, also known as Garadya,(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10686,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/sticker-is-a-game-played-using-the-colorfu_zWfcjJr.jpg','Sticker is a game played using the colorful cards found inside matchboxes, such as those from brands like Kuber-Khajana, Panjah, and Camel (Source: CKA Archives).','Sticker is a game played using the colorful cards found inside matchboxes, such as those from brands like Kuber-Khajana, Panjah, and Camel (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10689,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/khade-is-a-traditional-game-played-with-a-_bdQw7g6.jpg','Khade is a traditional game played with a small stone. To begin the game, players take the stone and throw it up, catching it on the dorsal side of the hand. They continue by throwing the stone up again and catching it with the dorsal side of the hand. The stones are then placed in a corner, and the player throws them up once more, attempting to catch as many stones as possible. If a player fails to catch the stone, they are out, and it is the next player\'s turn (Source: CKA Archives).','Khade is a traditional game played with a small stone. To begin the game, players take the stone and throw it up, catching it on the dorsal side of the hand. They continue by throwing the stone up again and catching it with the dorsal side of the hand. The stones are then placed in a corner, and the player throws them up once more, attempting to catch as many stones as possible. If a player fails to catch the stone, they are out, and it is the next player\'s turn (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10692,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/a-spinningbhovarasource-cka-archives-17532be3.jpg','A SpinningBhovara,(Source: CKA Archives).','A SpinningBhovara,(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10695,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/on-the-occasion-of-makar-sankranti-a-kite-_YlLtNDF.jpg','On the occasion of Makar Sankranti, a kite competition is held where participants use cotton thread to fly their kites. People from all over gather on open grounds or in specific areas to fly their kites.[1]','On the occasion of Makar Sankranti, a kite competition is held where participants use cotton thread to fly their kites. People from all over gather on open grounds or in specific areas to fly their kites.[1]','https://images.app.goo.gl/y8ARvim8ZJGgmpmy7'),(10699,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/the-akola-cricket-club2-bf62fe9d.jpg','The Akola Cricket Club[2]','The Akola Cricket Club[2]','https://www.instagram.com/wifaofficial/p/DCCMDmfuxFD/?img_index=2'),(10702,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/the-2024-akola-jr-boys-team-in-theinter-di_wrrl8OK.png','The 2024 Akola Jr. Boys Team in theInter District Football Championship organized by WIFA[3].','The 2024 Akola Jr. Boys Team in theInter District Football Championship organized by WIFA[3].','https://documents.iplt20.com/ipl/IPLHeadshot2025/1001.png'),(10707,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/boxers-in-the-vasant-desai-stadiumsource-c_4B4yme7.jpg','Boxers in the Vasant Desai Stadium(Source: CKA Archives).','Boxers in the Vasant Desai Stadium(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(10711,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/atharva-taide-is-a-cricketer-from-akola-wh_8DwPCtw.jpg','Atharva Taide is a cricketer from Akola who as of 2025 plays for Sunrisers Hyderabad in the IPL[4]','Atharva Taide is a cricketer from Akola who as of 2025 plays for Sunrisers Hyderabad in the IPL[4]','https://www.gujarattitansipl.com/players/darshan-nalkande-67489-profile'),(10714,'culture/images/maharashtra/akola/sports-games/darshan-nalkande-as-of-2025-plays-for-delh_aSgVZJS.png','Darshan Nalkande as of 2025 plays for Delhi Capitals in the IPL[5]','Darshan Nalkande as of 2025 plays for Delhi Capitals in the IPL[5]','https://images.app.goo.gl/y8ARvim8ZJGgmpmy