eled design and signs of aging. (Source: CKA Archives)','Weathered wooden door painted in white, showing a simple paneled design and signs of aging. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(10925,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/architecture/a-horizontal-ventilation-window-painted_HDpovW8.jpg','A horizontal ventilation window painted in the same turquoise color as the wall. It features a simple slatted wooden design, likely for air circulation. The window appears to be recessed into the wall and shows considerable aging. (Source: CKA Archives)','A horizontal ventilation window painted in the same turquoise color as the wall. It features a simple slatted wooden design, likely for air circulation. The window appears to be recessed into the wall and shows considerable aging. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(10926,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/architecture/a-red-painted-wooden-window-with-vertic_VODZ0Ez.jpg','A red-painted wooden window with vertical planks divided into two sections (upper and lower panels), set within a green-painted wall frame. (Source: CKA Archives)','A red-painted wooden window with vertical planks divided into two sections (upper and lower panels), set within a green-painted wall frame. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(10928,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/architecture/interior-view-showing-an-exposed-wooden_nfUSgsd.jpg','Interior view showing an exposed wooden rafter system with horizontal wooden purlins supporting the sheets above. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior view showing an exposed wooden rafter system with horizontal wooden purlins supporting the sheets above. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(10929,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/architecture/wider-view-of-the-same-roofing-structur_57xA8P2.png','Wider view of the same roofing structure with visible framework, featuring a decorative jali ventilation window and household items hung from the beams. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wider view of the same roofing structure with visible framework, featuring a decorative jali ventilation window and household items hung from the beams. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(10945,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/artforms/rangoli-installation-at-jog-stadium-amravat_e4OZqnR.png','Rangoli installation at Jog Stadium, Amravati, a 1,500+ foot-long rangoli created to promote social messages such as “Save the Girl Child” and “Protect Nature.”[1]','Rangoli installation at Jog Stadium, Amravati, a 1,500+ foot-long rangoli created to promote social messages such as “Save the Girl Child” and “Protect Nature.”[1]','https://www.indiabookofrecords.in/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/Madhuri-Satish-Suda.jpg'),(10954,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/artforms/entrance-of-the-nanda-udyan-ganpati-museum-_FIHMsoZ.jpg','Entrance of the Nanda Udyan Ganpati Museum, located on the Paratwada–Chikhaldara road, Amravati district, a unique museum dedicated entirely to Bhagwan Ganesha. This museum houses one of the largest private collections of Ganpati murtis, curated by Pradeep and Deepali Nand. (Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance of the Nanda Udyan Ganpati Museum, located on the Paratwada–Chikhaldara road, Amravati district, a unique museum dedicated entirely to Bhagwan Ganesha. This museum houses one of the largest private collections of Ganpati murtis, curated by Pradeep and Deepali Nand. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10956,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/artforms/central-exhibit-at-the-nanda-udyan-ganpati-_Tli2y2V.jpg','Central exhibit at the Nanda Udyan Ganpati Museum, Amravati featuring a marble sculpture of Lord Shiva, Parvati, and Ganesha, surrounded by a diverse collection of carvings and depictions of Ganesh. (Source: CKA Archives)','Central exhibit at the Nanda Udyan Ganpati Museum, Amravati featuring a marble sculpture of Lord Shiva, Parvati, and Ganesha, surrounded by a diverse collection of carvings and depictions of Ganesh. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10957,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/artforms/murti-making-is-a-well-established-craft-in_b6EOSac.jpg','Murti-making is a well-established craft in Maharashtra, closely linked to religious and cultural traditions. Perhaps reflecting this heritage, the museum displays a diverse collection of handcrafted Ganesha murtis in a variety of artistic forms and styles.(Source: CKA Archives)','Murti-making is a well-established craft in Maharashtra, closely linked to religious and cultural traditions. Perhaps reflecting this heritage, the museum displays a diverse collection of handcrafted Ganesha murtis in a variety of artistic forms and styles.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10980,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/the-ambadevi-mandir-amravati-city-sou_d0t2oGY.jpg','The Ambadevi Mandir, Amravati City. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Ambadevi Mandir, Amravati City. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10982,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/devotees-exit-the-ambadevi-mandir-aft_i3RE7hX.jpg','Devotees exit the Ambadevi Mandir after a darshan. (Source: CKA Archives)','Devotees exit the Ambadevi Mandir after a darshan. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10986,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/atmasiddhi-mahanubhav-mandir-achalpur_IqPomKw.jpg','Atmasiddhi Mahanubhav Mandir, Achalpur.(Source: CKA Archives)','Atmasiddhi Mahanubhav Mandir, Achalpur.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10987,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/talav-lake-near-atmasiddhi-mahanubhav_VmiMDRW.jpg','Talav (lake) near Atmasiddhi Mahanubhav Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','Talav (lake) near Atmasiddhi Mahanubhav Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10991,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/entrance-to-bebah-bagh-ashahi-qabrist_g0noA1T.jpg','Entrance to Bebah Bagh, aShahi Qabristan situated in Achalpur’s Sarmaspura area.(Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance to Bebah Bagh, aShahi Qabristan situated in Achalpur’s Sarmaspura area.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10992,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/the-intricate-carvings-and-latticed-w_yyKKU8R.jpg','The intricate carvings and latticed windows of Bebah Bagh showcase the influence of Persian architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)','The intricate carvings and latticed windows of Bebah Bagh showcase the influence of Persian architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10994,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/arched-doorways-of-bebah-bagh-decorat_BWEde9R.jpg','Arched doorways of Bebah Bagh decorated with intricate carvings demonstrate the site\'s Indo-Islamic architectural style. (Source: CKA Archives)','Arched doorways of Bebah Bagh decorated with intricate carvings demonstrate the site\'s Indo-Islamic architectural style. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10995,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/the-royal-qabar-within-bebah-bagh-tha_JluJXZA.jpg','The royal Qabar within Bebah Bagh that showcases the site’s history as the burial ground of many figures from the Nizam Shahi dynasty. (Source: CKA Archives)','The royal Qabar within Bebah Bagh that showcases the site’s history as the burial ground of many figures from the Nizam Shahi dynasty. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10996,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/the-deteriorating-arched-facades-and-_O6ls8gZ.jpg','The deteriorating arched facades and fallen debris of Bebah Bagh. (Source: CKA Archives)','The deteriorating arched facades and fallen debris of Bebah Bagh. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10997,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/a-long-corridor-featuring-repeated-ar_F0Tc9Rm.jpg','A long corridor featuring repeated arched passages and stone latticework along the walls of Bebah Bagh. (Source: CKA Archives)','A long corridor featuring repeated arched passages and stone latticework along the walls of Bebah Bagh. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(10999,'culture/images/maharashtra/amravati/cultural-sites/the-grand-exterior-of-bebah-bagh-show_T6GxB0C.jpg','The grand exterior of Bebah Bagh, showcasing its architectural grandeur,