-leaves1-58e4d678.png','Gongura Leaves[1]','Gongura Leaves[1]','https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-P0CkyiM-bSg/XeIF0JmLkCI/AAAAAAAAAes/mkv_nLMei3shyHUab0gOjar2_f3iIgGBQCEwYBhgL/s1600/gongura%2Bred%2Bstem.JPG'),(12324,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/gongura-pickle2-76ee84cb.png','Gongura Pickle[2]','Gongura Pickle[2]','https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/shopping?q=tbn:ANd9GcSotMSvt31VZckoMh8onSUfkdICgp6U81wVaZS9Tv4Qu_hjqs-pnt9_x73ttrDTmyBbshH_kJn1fO1QYYAqJHGfDhzBKBCht7kwm7GCyWYm&usqp=CAc'),(12327,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/dalia3-240ff1fd.png','Dalia[3]','Dalia[3]','https://cdn.cdnparenting.com/articles/2018/07/1133889533-H-1024x700.webp'),(12335,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/kharra-supari4-ef007050.png','Kharra Supari[4]','Kharra Supari[4]','https://5.imimg.com/data5/SELLER/Default/2023/5/307883220/GO/WZ/JG/99210375/nuts-500x500.jpeg'),(12339,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/tarri-poha5-774b7870.png','Tarri Poha[5]','Tarri Poha[5]','https://i.ytimg.com/vi/owKJhUbr26I/hq720.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEhCK4FEIIDSFryq4qpAxMIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJD&rs=AOn4CLAkeJnqp1at2qNcmrj9T8HG2x1LSw'),(12342,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/vangyachi-bhaji6-68224fd5.jpg','Vangyachi Bhaji[6]','Vangyachi Bhaji[6]','https://img-global.cpcdn.com/recipes/205d2d8cf7ec6086/680x482cq70/%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%AF%E0%A4%9A-%E0%A4%AD%E0%A4%9C-vangyachi-bhaji-recipe-in-marathi-%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%AA-%E0%A4%9A-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%AF-%E0%A4%AB%E0%A4%9F.jpg'),(12345,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/zinga-fish-source-cka-archives-02fc63c6.jpg','Zinga Fish (Source: CKA Archives)','Zinga Fish (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(12350,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/8ea77080e9284311a06b6aba4d53e9e9-a068b4ce.jpg','','',''),(12354,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/taj-biryani8-5615e180.jpg','Taj Biryani[8]','Taj Biryani[8]','https://www.google.com/imgres?q=chandrapur%20taj%20biryani&imgurl=https%3A%2F%2Fcontent.jdmagicbox.com%2Fcomp%2Fchandrapur%2Fz7%2F9999p7172.7172.160602185131.s5z7%2Fcatalogue%2Ftaj-biryani-center-chandrapur-0briz9tbcf.jpg&imgrefurl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.justdial.com%2FChandrapur%2FTaj-Biryani-Center-Near-Police-Club-Chandrapur-Ho%2F9999P7172-7172-160602185131-S5Z7_BZDET&docid=egkW-bzWL9r-_M&tbnid=jUsmbfn2GmtJuM&vet=12ahUKEwi_ste54aeJAxUVi68BHay1JK0QM3oECBcQAA..i&w=1920&h=1440&hcb=2&ved=2ahUKEwi_ste54aeJAxUVi68BHay1JK0QM3oECBcQAA'),(12357,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/food/madras-cafe9-2ff0dec3.png','Madras Cafe[9]','Madras Cafe[9]','https://www.justdial.com/Chandrapur/Cafe-Madras-Near-Laxmi-Narayan-Mandir-Chandrapur-City/9999P7172-7172-150821170255-J4Z9_BZDET'),(12388,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/markets/anandwan-weekly-market-source-cka-archives_6llpFXR.jpg','Anandwan weekly market (Source: CKA Archives)','Anandwan weekly market (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(12402,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/markets/each-bull-is-evaluated-based-on-its-size-m_B4BjOHh.png','Each bull is evaluated based on its size, muscle structure, hoof condition, teeth (for estimating age), and behavior. Strong, well-fed bulls fetch higher prices, and prices can range from ₹40,000 to over ₹1.5 lakh, depending on the breed and physical quality. Most transactions are made in cash after detailed bargaining. Bulls are brought in using trucks, tractors, or bullock carts, and the market area is typically set up on an open ground with temporary arrangements.[1]','Each bull is evaluated based on its size, muscle structure, hoof condition, teeth (for estimating age), and behavior. Strong, well-fed bulls fetch higher prices, and prices can range from ₹40,000 to over ₹1.5 lakh, depending on the breed and physical quality. Most transactions are made in cash after detailed bargaining. Bulls are brought in using trucks, tractors, or bullock carts, and the market area is typically set up on an open ground with temporary arrangements.[1]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D7hvf7wq_B4'),(12409,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/markets/market-road-source-cka-archives-9832bd6b.jpg','Market Road (Source: CKA Archives)','Market Road (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(12414,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/children-often-craft-spinning-toys-ca_BDQC0iL.jpg','Children often craft spinning toys called \"chakri\" using caps from Coca-Cola, Pepsi, and other soft drinks. (Source: CKA Archives).','Children often craft spinning toys called \"chakri\" using caps from Coca-Cola, Pepsi, and other soft drinks. (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12419,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/d16e0d6bbf804c2788415834ba78cbbc-f478b41c.jpg','','',''),(12422,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/a-rural-version-of-the-common-board-g_BCpAppn.jpg','A rural version of the common board game known as “Saap-Shidi”(Snakes and Ladder) is known as Chaklasta in Chandrapur, Source: CKA Archives.','A rural version of the common board game known as “Saap-Shidi”(Snakes and Ladder) is known as Chaklasta in Chandrapur, Source: CKA Archives.',''),(12427,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/during-the-holi-in-march-the-game-of-_9A6jEzs.png','During the Holi in March, the game of ghanmakad is enjoyed with great enthusiasm by both children and adults. (Source: CKA Archives).','During the Holi in March, the game of ghanmakad is enjoyed with great enthusiasm by both children and adults. (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12432,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/the-game-of-zandi-mundi-starts-four-d_fsEe9vh.png','The game of Zandi Mundi starts four days before the festival of the bullring. (Source: CKA Archives).','The game of Zandi Mundi starts four days before the festival of the bullring. (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12436,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/mahesh-wadhai-is-a-distinguished-mara_s6fql75.jpg','Mahesh Wadhai is a distinguished marathon runner hailing from Chandrapur, India. Mahesh Wadhai completed a full marathon (42 km) with a remarkable personal best time of 2:31:57 at the Vasai Virar Municipal Corporation Marathon held in Mumbai on December 11, 20222. This achievement places him among the elite marathon runners in India.[1]','Mahesh Wadhai is a distinguished marathon runner hailing from Chandrapur, India. Mahesh Wadhai completed a full marathon (42 km) with a remarkable personal best time of 2:31:57 at the Vasai Virar Municipal Corporation Marathon held in Mumbai on December 11, 20222. This achievement places him among the elite marathon runners in India.[1]','https://www.ahmedabadmarathon.com/en/highlights/2019'),(12441,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/the-anandvan-basketball-ground-is-loc_auw22ZV.jpg','The Anandvan Basketball Ground is located in Anandwan, a community rehabilitation center founded by Baba Amte.(Source: CKA Archives).','The Anandvan Basketball Ground is located in Anandwan, a community rehabilitation center founded by Baba Amte.(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12444,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/the-nembaji-shooting-warora-playgroun_AQfyf4y.jpg','The Nembaji (Shooting) Warora Playground (Source: CKA Archives).','The Nembaji (Shooting) Warora Playground (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12447,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/3cd685fc8bae431e9ab9cf05c7d4d9d5-c2160273.jpg','','',''),(12450,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/the-sati-township-stadiumsource-cka-a_DBDe3gh.png','The Sati Township Stadium(Source: CKA Archives).','The Sati Township Stadium(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12454,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/view-from-the-top-of-seven-sisters-hi_ZW6ANez.jpg','View from the top of seven sisters hills, Chandrapur(Source: CKA Archives).','View from the top of seven sisters hills, Chandrapur(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12455,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/nature-walksource-cka-archives-a3aafd6a.jpg','Nature Walk(Source: CKA Archives).','Nature Walk(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12460,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/sports-games/recreational-cricket-clubs-have-gaine_qKVPDD2.png','Recreational cricket clubs have gained popularity in the region. The Ordnance Factory Bhadravati has produced remarkable players, such as Murthy Rajan, who represented Ranji, the zone, and even participated in India camps during that time. Among the cricket grounds, St. Michael\'s School Ground in Chandrapur city is well known for its excellent facilities(Source: CKA Archives).','Recreational cricket clubs have gained popularity in the region. The Ordnance Factory Bhadravati has produced remarkable players, such as Murthy Rajan, who represented Ranji, the zone, and even participated in India camps during that time. Among the cricket grounds, St. Michael\'s School Ground in Chandrapur city is well known for its excellent facilities(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(12464,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/stories/achaleshwar-mandir1-1cb85db8.png','Achaleshwar Mandir[1]','Achaleshwar Mandir[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Anchaleshwar_Temple_Group,_Chandrapur'),(12467,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/stories/chandrapur-mahakali-mandir2-f787cf9a.png','Chandrapur Mahakali Mandir[2]','Chandrapur Mahakali Mandir[2]','https://www.seawatersports.com/places/maharashtra/mahakali-temple'),(12471,'culture/images/maharashtra/chandrapur/stories/seven-sisters-hills3-2e9eb1da.jpg','Seven Sisters Hills[3]','Seven Sisters Hills[3]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perjagadh_Seven_Sisters_Hills_5.jpg'),(12490,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/ajanta-caves-are-an-e_Ud5txSU.png','Ajanta Caves are an example of rock-cut architecture and feature both chaityagrihas and viharas carved into a horseshoe-shaped cliff above the Waghora River.[1]','Ajanta Caves are an example of rock-cut architecture and feature both chaityagrihas and viharas carved into a horseshoe-shaped cliff above the Waghora River.[1]',''),(12492,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/cave-2-at-ajanta-refl_vUZcCLq.png','Cave 2 at Ajanta reflects the later Mahayana phase, with a sculpted Buddha, bodhisattvas, and vibrant tempera murals adorning its intricately carved interiors.[2]','Cave 2 at Ajanta reflects the later Mahayana phase, with a sculpted Buddha, bodhisattvas, and vibrant tempera murals adorning its intricately carved interiors.[2]',''),(12496,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/ellora-caves-follow-a_x7v948X.png','Ellora Caves follow a diverse rock-cut architectural style, carved into the vertical Charanandri hills in a linear north-south alignment.[3]','Ellora Caves follow a diverse rock-cut architectural style, carved into the vertical Charanandri hills in a linear north-south alignment.[3]',''),(12498,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/elloras-buddhist-cave_UFRU1c3.png','Ellora’s Buddhist caves follow the Mahayana rock-cut architectural style, with sculpted Buddha images lining the walls of multi-storeyed viharas.[4]','Ellora’s Buddhist caves follow the Mahayana rock-cut architectural style, with sculpted Buddha images lining the walls of multi-storeyed viharas.[4]',''),(12500,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/elloras-hindu-caves-c_6c1jqs4.png','Ellora’s Hindu caves culminates in a monolithic Kailash Mandir (Cave 16) showcasing a fully carved freestanding shrine hewn from a single rock.[5]','Ellora’s Hindu caves culminates in a monolithic Kailash Mandir (Cave 16) showcasing a fully carved freestanding shrine hewn from a single rock.[5]',''),(12502,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/indra-sabha-cave-32-i_glO5WjR.png','Indra Sabha (Cave 32) in the Jain caves features intricately carved pillars, detailed figural panels, and compact shrines, exemplifying the sect’s focus on both austerity and ornamentation.[6]','Indra Sabha (Cave 32) in the Jain caves features intricately carved pillars, detailed figural panels, and compact shrines, exemplifying the sect’s focus on both austerity and ornamentation.[6]',''),(12506,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/daulatabad-fort-a-rem_ylmjPWn.png','Daulatabad Fort, a remarkable example of medieval military engineering, is entirely carved from basalt rock, showcasing its strategic design and formidable structure.[7]','Daulatabad Fort, a remarkable example of medieval military engineering, is entirely carved from basalt rock, showcasing its strategic design and formidable structure.[7]',''),(12508,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/the-entrance-gates-of_N9lDk0H.png','The entrance gates of Daulatabad Fort are equipped with iron spikes, designed to counter the advance of war elephants during sieges.[8]','The entrance gates of Daulatabad Fort are equipped with iron spikes, designed to counter the advance of war elephants during sieges.[8]',''),(12512,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/bhadkal-darwaza-follo_g9QELBQ.png','Bhadkal Darwaza, following the Indo-Islamic architectural style with Deccan influences, is a two-storey masonry structure built with grey basalt and lime mortar.[9]','Bhadkal Darwaza, following the Indo-Islamic architectural style with Deccan influences, is a two-storey masonry structure built with grey basalt and lime mortar.[9]',''),(12516,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/soneri-mahal-built-in_HaQPRwA.png','Soneri Mahal, built in Rajput architectural style, is a two-storeyed rectangular structure set on a high plinth, surrounded by a large rectangular garden.[10]','Soneri Mahal, built in Rajput architectural style, is a two-storeyed rectangular structure set on a high plinth, surrounded by a large rectangular garden.[10]',''),(12520,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/white-marble-domes-ar_PTeGUX0.png','White marble domes, arched recesses, and symmetrical minarets reflect the late Mughal and Persian influences of Bibi Ka Maqbara’s Indo-Islamic architectural style.[11]','White marble domes, arched recesses, and symmetrical minarets reflect the late Mughal and Persian influences of Bibi Ka Maqbara’s Indo-Islamic architectural style.[11]',''),(12522,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/the-white-marble-dome_IusxhJM.png','The white marble dome of Bibi Ka Maqbara is flanked by four smaller domes and topped with a brass finial.[12]','The white marble dome of Bibi Ka Maqbara is flanked by four smaller domes and topped with a brass finial.[12]',''),(12524,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/architecture/lattice-jali-screens-_kQjBaWM.png','Lattice (jali) screens at Bibi Ka Maqbara showcase intricate geometric patterns and delicate stone carving.[13]','Lattice (jali) screens at Bibi Ka Maqbara showcase intricate geometric patterns and delicate stone carving.[13]',''),(12547,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/a-chaitya-griha-with-a-st_CS04rEI.jpg','A chaitya-griha with a stupa in Cave 9[1]','A chaitya-griha with a stupa in Cave 9[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajanta,_cave_9,_chaitya-griha,_with_stupa_%289842167554%29.jpg'),(12548,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/achaitya-griha-with-an-in_crdcVS1.jpg','Achaitya-griha with an intricately carved stupa in Cave 26[2]','Achaitya-griha with an intricately carved stupa in Cave 26[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajanta,_cave_26,_chaitya-griha,_Buddha_%289841424296%29.jpg'),(12550,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/the-flying-apsara-paintin_7EQETv3.jpg','The Flying Apsara painting[3]','The Flying Apsara painting[3]','http://www.abhijna-emuseum.com/articles/ancient-resonances-the-murals-of-ajanta/'),(12552,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/a-scene-from-the-mahajana_sd5Tfns.jpg','A scene from the ‘Mahajanaka Jataka’[4]','A scene from the ‘Mahajanaka Jataka’[4]','https://www.worldhistory.org/image/4326/jataka-image-in-ajanta/'),(12556,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/cave-15-or-the-dashavatar_RgLxHfg.jpg','Cave 15 or the Dashavatara Cave, a Hindu cave[5]','Cave 15 or the Dashavatara Cave, a Hindu cave[5]','https://mapacademy.io/article/dashavatara-cave-ellora/'),(12557,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/cave-10-or-the-vishwakarm_VOsDRRF.png','Cave 10 or the Vishwakarma Cave, a Buddhist cave[6]','Cave 10 or the Vishwakarma Cave, a Buddhist cave[6]','https://nanchi.blog/2020/05/08/ellora-caves-10-vishwakarma-caves-verul-buddhist-caves-aurangabad/'),(12558,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/cave-31-or-the-indra-sabh_yEVzmnx.jpg','Cave 31 or the Indra Sabha Cave, a Jain cave[7]','Cave 31 or the Indra Sabha Cave, a Jain cave[7]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indra_Sabha_-_Cave_32_at_Ellora.jpg'),(12562,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/an-outside-view-of-the-au_cTrHlS3.png','An outside view of the Aurangabad Caves[8]','An outside view of the Aurangabad Caves[8]','https://aurangabadtourism.in/ajanta-caves-aurangabad'),(12568,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/a-paithani-sari-being-wea_Jn9GF1P.jpg','A Paithani sari being weaved.[9]','A Paithani sari being weaved.[9]','https://www.sahapedia.org/paithani-saree-woven-histories-of-maharashtra'),(12572,'culture/images/maharashtra/chhatrapati-sambhaji-nagar/artforms/a-himroo-garment-being-wo_6n4gRke.jpg','A Himroo garment being woven; source: Himroo Fabrics[10]','A Himroo garment being woven; source: Himroo Fabrics[10]','https://www.vogue.in/fashion/content/paithani-sari-maharashtrian-bridal-sari-history-technique'),(12579,'culture/images/maharashtra/