ricate carvings is displayed at the Ramling Appa Lamture Museum, Ter, Dharashiv. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(12980,'culture/images/maharashtra/dharashiv/cultural-sites/a-wooden-door-from-the-nearby-uttare_uWNmue4.jpg','A wooden door from the nearby Uttareshwar Mandir in Ter is kept on display at the Ramling Appa Lamture Museum. (Source: CKA Archives)','A wooden door from the nearby Uttareshwar Mandir in Ter is kept on display at the Ramling Appa Lamture Museum. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(12984,'culture/images/maharashtra/dharashiv/cultural-sites/the-kunthalgiri-mandir-complex-locat_RlcO7mU.png','The Kunthalgiri Mandir complex, located atop a 175-foot hill in Dharashiv. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Kunthalgiri Mandir complex, located atop a 175-foot hill in Dharashiv. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(12988,'culture/images/maharashtra/dharashiv/cultural-sites/the-majestic-naldurg-fort-dharashiv-_hcAD41l.jpg','The majestic Naldurg Fort, Dharashiv, with the Bori River flowing beside the fort walls as part of a natural defensive trench historically used as a moat. (Source: CKA Archives)','The majestic Naldurg Fort, Dharashiv, with the Bori River flowing beside the fort walls as part of a natural defensive trench historically used as a moat. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(12991,'culture/images/maharashtra/dharashiv/cultural-sites/tofs-cannon-mounts-positioned-along-_B8rcGbc.jpg','Tofs (cannon mounts) positioned along the outer wall, facing former siege routes and rival territories. (Source: CKA Archives)','Tofs (cannon mounts) positioned along the outer wall, facing former siege routes and rival territories. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(12993,'culture/images/maharashtra/dharashiv/cultural-sites/the-unique-design-at-the-mouth-of-th_b8QC7Fm.jpg','The unique design at the mouth of the tof, its presence emphasizing its strategic military function. (Source: CKA Archives)','The unique design at the mouth of the tof, its presence emphasizing its strategic military functio