markets/in-sakri-taluka-dhule-district-farmers-rely-on-_JZlAPdF.png','In Sakri Taluka (Dhule district), farmers rely on a network of local agro-dealer shops and service centres—calledKrishi Seva Kendras—for purchasing critical agricultural inputs such as fertilisers, seeds, and pesticides. Distributed across villages, these centres are monitored by the district Agriculture Department to ensure quality. The region’s farming landscape varies between water-scarce zones and better-rained belts, prompting demand for tailored crop inputs. With cropping patterns shifting and modern techniques slowly adopted, these rural input markets serve as the main conduit through which farmers access supplies and technical guidance.[1]','In Sakri Taluka (Dhule district), farmers rely on a network of local agro-dealer shops and service centres—calledKrishi Seva Kendras—for purchasing critical agricultural inputs such as fertilisers, seeds, and pesticides. Distributed across villages, these centres are monitored by the district Agriculture Department to ensure quality. The region’s farming landscape varies between water-scarce zones and better-rained belts, prompting demand for tailored crop inputs. With cropping patterns shifting and modern techniques slowly adopted, these rural input markets serve as the main conduit through which farmers access supplies and technical guidance.[1]','https://www.esakal.com/uttar-maharashtra/agriculturesakri-private-agriculture-market-growth-farmers-exploitation-political-influence-unregulated-trade-fair-pricing-demand-maharashtra-nmk01'),(13586,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/markets/subhash-nagar-market-in-dhule-city-sells-produc_fzU5rCE.png','Subhash Nagar Market, in Dhule city, sells produce, groceries, and household goods daily from 6:00 am to 8:00 pm. Sixty stalls, including informal setups, offer onions, chilies, and custard apples. Farmers from fifteen villages supply goods. Started in the 1980s, it peaks during festivals with pooja stalls. It closes during heavy rains. Its early hours suit daily shoppers.[2]','Subhash Nagar Market, in Dhule city, sells produce, groceries, and household goods daily from 6:00 am to 8:00 pm. Sixty stalls, including informal setups, offer onions, chilies, and custard apples. Farmers from fifteen villages supply goods. Started in the 1980s, it peaks during festivals with pooja stalls. It closes during heavy rains. Its early hours suit daily shoppers.[2]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HiJV7_97Wdc'),(13604,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/sports-games/the-dhule-stadium-source-cka-archives-9db4fe00.jpg','The Dhule Stadium (Source: CKA Archives)','The Dhule Stadium (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(13608,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/sports-games/hsa-basketball-court-source-cka-archives-8e537d82.jpg','HSA Basketball Court (Source: CKA Archives)','HSA Basketball Court (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(13613,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/sports-games/taluka-krida-sankul-also-known-as-garud-ma_orsRHNm.jpg','Taluka Krida Sankul, also known as Garud Maidan, is a prominent sports facility located in Dhule, (Source: CKA Archives).','Taluka Krida Sankul, also known as Garud Maidan, is a prominent sports facility located in Dhule, (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(13616,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/sports-games/indoor-sports-complex-dhule-source-cka-arc_ZsK36OC.jpg','Indoor Sports Complex, Dhule (Source: CKA Archives).','Indoor Sports Complex, Dhule (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(13618,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/sports-games/in-the-dhule-district-the-practice-of-yoga_RuVUeLB.png','In the Dhule district, the practice of yoga and fitness has gained significant traction, particularly through institutions like Yoga Vidya Dham, which operates in both Shirpur and Dhule. The Shirpur center offers a yoga diploma course and a Master of Arts in Yoga through an open university, promoting health awareness among the community. Dr. Shrikant Wadile, the founder of the organization, conducts monthly yoga sessions both online and offline, providing valuable training to many individuals (Source: CKA Archives).','In the Dhule district, the practice of yoga and fitness has gained significant traction, particularly through institutions like Yoga Vidya Dham, which operates in both Shirpur and Dhule. The Shirpur center offers a yoga diploma course and a Master of Arts in Yoga through an open university, promoting health awareness among the community. Dr. Shrikant Wadile, the founder of the organization, conducts monthly yoga sessions both online and offline, providing valuable training to many individuals (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(13630,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/stories/kanhaiyalal-mandir1-99583e74.png','Kanhaiyalal Mandir[1]','Kanhaiyalal Mandir[1]','https://www.justdial.com/Dhule/Shri-Kanhaiyalal-Maharaj/9999P2562-2562-190331035856-I9V6_BZDET'),(13633,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/stories/cda7f827315a48ddaa97b5fa7e8e4667-2eb39627.png','','',''),(13636,'culture/images/maharashtra/dhule/stories/03320adf79734959b0c9c33ccd3505f3-a0a1fe0e.png','','',''),(13648,'culture/images/maharashtra/gadchiroli/architecture/view-of-the-markandeshwar-mandir-know_LABljQo.png','View of the Markandeshwar Mandir, known as the \'Khajuraho of Vidarbha\', located on the banks of the Wainganga River.[1]','View of the Markandeshwar Mandir, known as the \'Khajuraho of Vidarbha\', located on the banks of the Wainganga River.[1]',''),(13652,'culture/images/maharashtra/gadchiroli/architecture/the-shiv-mandir-at-arttondi-built-in-_Bhq6xiL.png','The Shiv Mandir at Arttondi built in the Hemadpanthi architectural style. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Shiv Mandir at Arttondi built in the Hemadpanthi architectural style. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13654,'culture/images/maharashtra/gadchiroli/architecture/older-steps-carved-in-stone-are-on-th_UgFQYxH.png','Older steps carved in stone are on the right, and newer concrete steps are on the left. (Source: CKA Archives)','Older 