ect level Competition in Aheri(Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(13919,'culture/images/maharashtra/gadchiroli/stories/bhaskar-halami-left1-5e3a0a41.png','Bhaskar Halami (left)[1]','Bhaskar Halami (left)[1]','https://images.tv9hindi.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Bhaskar-Halami.jpg'),(13931,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/remains-of-the-5th-century-nagara-brick-m_05vAZLQ.jpg','Remains of the 5th-century Nagara Brick Mandir, showing its distinctive brick construction.[1]','Remains of the 5th-century Nagara Brick Mandir, showing its distinctive brick construction.[1]','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/0012023_Nagra_Brick_Temple%2C_Chandanitola_Gondia_Maharastra_334.jpg/1920px-0012023_Nagra_Brick_Temple%2C_Chandanitola_Gondia_Maharastra_334.jpg'),(13936,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-doye-wada-in-dongargaon-built-in-the-_nxAmQsy.jpg','The Doye Wada in Dongargaon, built in the early 1900s. Notice its beautiful hexagonal structure and the details that add to its aesthetic. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Doye Wada in Dongargaon, built in the early 1900s. Notice its beautiful hexagonal structure and the details that add to its aesthetic. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13938,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/traditional-wooden-entryway-of-doye-wada-_MJjrDTo.png','Traditional wooden entryway of Doye Wada featuring a triangular gabled roof with latticed woodwork (jali) beneath the eaves. The entrance consists of wooden double doors and symmetrical windows on either side. (Source: CKA Archives)','Traditional wooden entryway of Doye Wada featuring a triangular gabled roof with latticed woodwork (jali) beneath the eaves. The entrance consists of wooden double doors and symmetrical windows on either side. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13939,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/an-elongated-wooden-door-panel-of-the-wad_EZRbl9z.png','An elongated wooden door panel of the Wada which showcases sheds light on the early 20th-century carpentry techniques. The door has rectangular panels with recessed details, set within a plastered archway. The top and bottom panels feature geometric designs, while the middle panel includes a carved motif, possibly a kalash, used in religious rituals. (Source: CKA Archives)','An elongated wooden door panel of the Wada which showcases sheds light on the early 20th-century carpentry techniques. The door has rectangular panels with recessed details, set within a plastered archway. The top and bottom panels feature geometric designs, while the middle panel includes a carved motif, possibly a kalash, used in religious rituals. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13940,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-multilevel-wooden-paneled-door-at-the-w_XlQP7XT.png','A multilevel wooden paneled door at the Wada. Notice the vertical wooden supports and horizontal railings. The exposed structural elements reveal the timber frame construction methodology used throughout the wada. (Source: CKA Archives)','A multilevel wooden paneled door at the Wada. Notice the vertical wooden supports and horizontal railings. The exposed structural elements reveal the timber frame construction methodology used throughout the wada. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13941,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/an-arched-window-with-plaster-surround-fr_fT2F1Fh.png','An arched window with plaster surround from Doye Wada featuring a curved, molded arch (cusped arch design). The window contains wooden muntins dividing the glass panes in a traditional pattern. (Source: CKA Archives)','An arched window with plaster surround from Doye Wada featuring a curved, molded arch (cusped arch design). The window contains wooden muntins dividing the glass panes in a traditional pattern. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13942,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/small-ventilation-window-panels-source-ck_BV1wZwf.png','Small ventilation window panels. (Source: CKA Archives)','Small ventilation window panels. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13943,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/larger-second-floor-windows-featuring-jha_NVVsvbS.jpg','Larger second-floor windows featuring jharokhas (traditional ornamental overhanging balconies which are characteristically seen in Rajput architecture). (Source: CKA Archives)','Larger second-floor windows featuring jharokhas (traditional ornamental overhanging balconies which are characteristically seen in Rajput architecture). (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13945,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-wooden-balcony-structure-which-featur_9RZwkEj.jpg','The wooden balcony structure which features a series of ventilation openings arranged in a uniform pattern along the facade. Below the jharokhas, decorative wooden trim with scalloped edges creates a rhythmic visual element. Notice how these architectural features provided both privacy and ventilation for residents while maintaining visual connection. (Source: CKA Archives)','The wooden balcony structure which features a series of ventilation openings arranged in a uniform pattern along the facade. Below the jharokhas, decorative wooden trim with scalloped edges creates a rhythmic visual element. Notice how these architectural features provided both privacy and ventilation for residents while maintaining visual connection. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13946,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-multi-tiered-terracotta-tile-roofing-_IjQ8Wqg.jpg','The multi-tiered terracotta tile roofing system of Doye Wada showcasing traditional sloped roof construction techniques. The pitched roof design with overlapping clay tiles indicates how the design is oriented to respond to heavy monsoon rainfall, allowing for efficient water drainage. (Source: CKA Archives)','The multi-tiered terracotta tile roofing system of Doye Wada showcasing traditional sloped roof construction techniques. The pitched roof design with overlapping clay tiles indicates how the design is oriented to respond to heavy monsoon rainfall, allowing for efficient water drainage. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13948,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-compound-wall-of-the-wada-notice-the-_k7Wup8q.png','The Compound wall of the Wada. Notice the unique brick masonry here. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Compound wall of the Wada. Notice the unique brick masonry here. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13949,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-street-view-of-the-doye-wada-one-can-se_vdtHPG0.png','A street view of the Doye Wada. One can see the many arches and the structure of the residence hidden within the trees. (Source: CKA Archives)','A street view of the Doye Wada. One can see the many arches and the structure of the residence hidden within the trees. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13950,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/multiple-connecting-arches-create-visual-_mmAaURT.png','Multiple connecting arches create visual rhythm throughout Doye Wada, guiding visitors through the historic residence. (Source: CKA Archives)','Multiple connecting arches create visual rhythm throughout Doye Wada, guiding visitors through the historic residence. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13951,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/this-arch-is-painted-in-a-neutral-white-a_0nOmEVo.png','This arch is painted in a neutral white and highlighted with a vibrant red and blue color. (Source: CKA Archives)','This arch is painted in a neutral white and highlighted with a vibrant red and blue color. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13953,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-stone-fountain-which-lies-at-the-exte_eg8q1RS.jpg','The stone fountain which lies at the exterior courtyard of the wada. Notice the circular masonry structure and the central ornamental pedestal which itself has many motifs within it. In many ways, this element alongside others showcase the craftsmanship of the artists of a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)','The stone fountain which lies at the exterior courtyard of the wada. Notice the circular masonry structure and the central ornamental pedestal which itself has many motifs within it. In many ways, this element alongside others showcase the craftsmanship of the artists of a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13956,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-mint-green-facade-of-a-house-situated_p1mjvQf.jpg','The mint green facade of a house situated in Bhagi Village. (Source: CKA Archives)','The mint green facade of a house situated in Bhagi Village. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13958,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/mud-road-that-leads-to-the-house-source-c_WVuBtwq.jpg','Mud road that leads to the house. (Source: CKA Archives)','Mud road that leads to the house. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13960,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-entrance-gate-is-constructed-of-wroug_bDQmw69.jpg','The entrance gate is constructed of wrought iron which features vertical bars and ornamental scrollwork. The compound wall itself displays intricate cement latticework, where geometric patterns and curved motifs create a rhythmic visual sequence. (Source: CKA Archives)','The entrance gate is constructed of wrought iron which features vertical bars and ornamental scrollwork. The compound wall itself displays intricate cement latticework, where geometric patterns and curved motifs create a rhythmic visual sequence. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13963,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-double-leaf-door-two-panel-door-painted_fB5YIq1.jpg','A double-leaf door (two-panel door) painted in a white color, with each leaf divided into three  panels with some shaped in arches, rectangles, and squares. (Source: CKA Archives)','A double-leaf door (two-panel door) painted in a white color, with each leaf divided into three  panels with some shaped in arches, rectangles, and squares. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13964,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-single-leaf-door-with-six-panels-arrang_EMUxdD7.jpg','A single-leaf door with six panels arranged in the configuration of two small panels at the top, two elongated panels in the middle, and two smaller panels at the bottom. (Source: CKA Archives)','A single-leaf door with six panels arranged in the configuration of two small panels at the top, two elongated panels in the middle, and two smaller panels at the bottom. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13966,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-windows-of-the-house-are-compact-in-s_CzCWYZd.jpg','The windows of the house are compact in size. They are protected by metal grills with a distinctive floral pattern; which were likely added during the renovations. (Source: CKA Archives)','The windows of the house are compact in size. They are protected by metal grills with a distinctive floral pattern; which were likely added during the renovations. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13968,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-double-layered-roofing-system-which-i_AeRNUO2.jpg','The double-layered roofing system which is separated by a traditional ventilation window (jali). (Source: CKA Archives)','The double-layered roofing system which is separated by a traditional ventilation window (jali). (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13969,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-traditional-jali-ventilation-design-wit_eVCU199.jpg','A traditional jali ventilation design with decorative corbels and a protective sunshade, which lies in between the double layered roofing system. (Source: CKA Archives)','A traditional jali ventilation design with decorative corbels and a protective sunshade, which lies in between the double layered roofing system. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13973,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/a-bungalow-at-deori-which-was-constructed_R22vxoa.jpg','A Bungalow at Deori which was constructed in 2020. (Source: CKA Archives)','A Bungalow at Deori which was constructed in 2020. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13975,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/stone-cladding-on-the-exterior-which-adds_XIt8p5D.jpg','Stone cladding on the exterior which adds a visual contrast and character to the facade of the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)','Stone cladding on the exterior which adds a visual contrast and character to the facade of the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13977,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-window-at-the-facade-of-the-house-whi_zGmGIoN.jpg','The window at the facade of the house which functions as a skylight, allowing natural light to enter. (Source: CKA Archives)','The window at the facade of the house which functions as a skylight, allowing natural light to enter. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13978,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/metal-grills-on-windows-with-a-webbed-des_lpFNKWF.jpg','Metal grills on windows with a webbed design. Notice the stone cladding within which this window is placed. (Source: CKA Archives)','Metal grills on windows with a webbed design. Notice the stone cladding within which this window is placed. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13980,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-wooden-entrance-door-with-glass-panel_ihuOsmo.jpg','The wooden entrance door with glass panels which adds to both its functionality and design appeal. (Source: CKA Archives)','The wooden entrance door with glass panels which adds to both its functionality and design appeal. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13981,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/architecture/the-balcony-of-the-house-which-features-a_vCTeP7q.jpg','The balcony of the house which features a sloping roof and metal railings. (Source: CKA Archives)','The balcony of the house which features a sloping roof and metal railings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(13991,'culture/images/maharashtra/gondia/artforms/the-men-and-women-perform-the-gondi-dance-wit_47z1RO4.png','The men and women perform th