ir-_pAI1CvL.jpg','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15222,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-splendid-architecture-of-the-mandir-_GkLH2jH.jpg','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15223,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-splendid-architecture-of-the-mandir-_Wh9GLdq.jpg','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)','The splendid architecture of the mandir, though it lacks a Shikhar, the mandir has stood the test of time. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15225,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/an-outside-view-of-the-mahaganpati-mandi_jB2IE9H.jpg','An Outside View of the Mahaganpati Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','An Outside View of the Mahaganpati Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15227,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-swayambhu-ganpati-source-cka-archive_Uolpk3L.jpg','The Swayambhu Ganpati (Source: CKA Archives)','The Swayambhu Ganpati (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15228,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/devangiri-inscription-that-is-on-the-man_FA9OmXh.jpg','Devangiri inscription that is on the mansion’s fence (Source: CKA Archives)','Devangiri inscription that is on the mansion’s fence (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15232,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-two-cannons-that-are-on-the-fort-sou_GnOGnud.jpg','The Two Cannons that are on the fort (Source: CKA Archives)','The Two Cannons that are on the fort (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15233,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/a41ed565ace942938b416ca78177d8ee-18356ae3.jpg','','',''),(15235,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-ruins-and-remnants-of-the-old-fort-w_dIzFXPC.jpg','The Ruins and remnants of the old fort walls and bastions are visible (Source: CKA Archives)','The Ruins and remnants of the old fort walls and bastions are visible (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15236,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-ruins-and-remnants-of-the-old-fort-w_nYJRMWl.jpg','The Ruins and remnants of the old fort walls and bastions are visible (Source: CKA Archives)','The Ruins and remnants of the old fort walls and bastions are visible (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15238,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/an-outside-view-of-the-matsyodari-mandir_WuXAeKQ.jpg','An Outside View of the Matsyodari Mandir at Ambad (Source: CKA Archives)','An Outside View of the Matsyodari Mandir at Ambad (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15240,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/fish-motif-embedded-in-the-mandirs-walls_EdCcYf4.jpg','Fish motif embedded in the mandir’s walls (Source: CKA Archives)','Fish motif embedded in the mandir’s walls (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15241,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/entrance-to-the-garbhagriha-source-cka-a_NhgP3dC.jpg','Entrance to the garbhagriha (Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance to the garbhagriha (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15244,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/a-view-of-the-mazar-e-maulai-noorudin-sa_EXEDGV0.png','A view of the Mazar-E-Maulai Noorudin Saheb in Dongagon[1]','A view of the Mazar-E-Maulai Noorudin Saheb in Dongagon[1]','https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=385995896144257&set=pcb.385995949477585'),(15247,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-nangartas-mandir-in-mantha-taluka2-fb5e8ae7.png','The Nangartas Mandir in Mantha Taluka[2]','The Nangartas Mandir in Mantha Taluka[2]','https://www.shriramvanyatra.org/2-148-nagartas-mandir/'),(15250,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-pokhrani-step-well-in-ambad-taluka-s_n4vJ8s5.jpg','The Pokhrani Step Well in Ambad Taluka (Source: CKA Archives)','The Pokhrani Step Well in Ambad Taluka (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15252,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-seemingly-simple-looking-structure-o_FNyWyMu.jpg','The seemingly simple-looking structure of a Step Well (Source: CKA Archives)','The seemingly simple-looking structure of a Step Well (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15254,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-interior-of-the-mandir-source-cka-ar_4OXZ9lF.jpg','The interior of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','The interior of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15256,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-carvings-of-two-ducks-source-cka-arc_HrxBmHa.jpg','The carvings of two Ducks (Source: CKA Archive)','The carvings of two Ducks (Source: CKA Archive)',''),(15258,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-ceiling-with-carvings-of-elephants-a_SIaR0h8.jpg','The ceiling with carvings of elephants arranged in a line depicts a scene of war. (Source: CKA Archives)','The ceiling with carvings of elephants arranged in a line depicts a scene of war. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15259,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/notice-the-intricate-carvings-on-the-sta_NX8U8H4.jpg','Notice the Intricate carvings on the Stambhs of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','Notice the Intricate carvings on the Stambhs of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15260,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/notice-the-intricate-carvings-on-the-sta_KL44IBA.jpg','Notice the Intricate carvings on the Stambhs of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','Notice the Intricate carvings on the Stambhs of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15262,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/an-outside-view-of-the-rajur-ganpati-man_GJk3Amo.jpg','An Outside view of the Rajur Ganpati Mandir at Jalna City (Source: CKA Archives)','An Outside view of the Rajur Ganpati Mandir at Jalna City (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15264,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-bell-sent-by-the-peshwas-in-1722-is-_OEOVJYZ.jpg','The Bell sent by the Peshwas in 1722 is still kept in the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Bell sent by the Peshwas in 1722 is still kept in the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15266,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-bell-sent-by-the-peshwas-in-1722-is-_ldeVKRG.jpg','The Bell sent by the Peshwas in 1722 is still kept in the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Bell sent by the Peshwas in 1722 is still kept in the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15268,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-samarth-mandir-in-jambsamarth-is-the_vwuydxI.jpg','The Samarth Mandir in Jambsamarth is the birthplace of Ramdas Swami (c. 1608 – c. 1682) (Source: CKA Archives)','The Samarth Mandir in Jambsamarth is the birthplace of Ramdas Swami (c. 1608 – c. 1682) (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15270,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-murti-oframdas-swami-source-cka-arch_paMtCTJ.jpg','The Murti ofRamdas Swami (Source: CKA Archives)','The Murti ofRamdas Swami (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15272,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-gaushala-that-is-attached-to-the-man_QgJemDm.jpg','The Gaushala that is attached to the mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','The Gaushala that is attached to the mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15275,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-sriram-mandir-is-the-birthplace-of-s_sG4wCkl.jpg','The Sriram Mandir is the birthplace of Sant Ramdas in Jamb Samrath Gaon (Source: CKA Archives)','The Sriram Mandir is the birthplace of Sant Ramdas in Jamb Samrath Gaon (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15277,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-murtis-of-ram-sita-and-laxman-are-cr_aMcD1k4.jpg','The Murtis of Ram, Sita, and Laxman are crafted from five sacred metals (Source: CKA Archives)','The Murtis of Ram, Sita, and Laxman are crafted from five sacred metals (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15279,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-shikhar-of-the-mandir-source-cka-arc_53FEmQ3.jpg','The Shikhar of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','The Shikhar of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15282,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-mahanubhav-priest-of-the-mandir-is-s_g7TU059.jpg','The Mahanubhav priest of the mandir is standing in front of the Garbagruha of the Mandir, Ambad (Source: CKA Archives)','The Mahanubhav priest of the mandir is standing in front of the Garbagruha of the Mandir, Ambad (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15284,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/inside-the-garbagruha-of-the-mandir-sour_kQzN4sx.jpg','Inside the Garbagruha of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','Inside the Garbagruha of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15287,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/outside-the-jain-mandir-in-jalna-city-so_u7QCBfS.png','Outside the  Jain Mandir in Jalna City (Source: CKA Archives)','Outside the  Jain Mandir in Jalna City (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15290,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/a-view-of-the-vitthal-mahadev-mandir-in-_7jSi96w.jpg','A view of the Vitthal Mahadev Mandir in Rajur Village (Source: CKA Archives)','A view of the Vitthal Mahadev Mandir in Rajur Village (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15292,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-intricately-carved-pillars-of-the-ma_Hi9bS8h.jpg','The intricately carved pillars of the Mandir (Sources: CKA Archives)','The intricately carved pillars of the Mandir (Sources: CKA Archives)',''),(15293,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/the-intricately-carved-pillars-of-the-ma_jjboxyk.jpg','The intricately carved pillars of the Mandir (Sources: CKA Archives)','The intricately carved pillars of the Mandir (Sources: CKA Archives)',''),(15295,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/inside-the-mandir-one-can-find-various-s_Y0MSzE7.jpg','Inside the Mandir, one can find various such examples of intricate carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)','Inside the Mandir, one can find various such examples of intricate carvings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15296,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/cultural-sites/possibly-a-pillar-of-the-now-broken-sabh_4LExgMb.jpg','Possibly a pillar of the now broken Sabha mandap of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','Possibly a pillar of the now broken Sabha mandap of the Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15303,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/festivals-fairs/women-performing-bhajan-in-the-anand-sw_zNWEV9d.jpg','Women performing bhajan in the Anand Swami Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','Women performing bhajan in the Anand Swami Mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15307,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/festivals-fairs/panchamukhi-mahadev1-89bb9a41.png','Panchamukhi Mahadev[1]','Panchamukhi Mahadev[1]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AzcYZJ_EdSw'),(15310,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/festivals-fairs/one-of-the-stalls-at-the-jatra2-05be5951.png','One of the stalls at the jatra[2]','One of the stalls at the jatra[2]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5pL3sY_qFTg'),(15329,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/shri-dattashram-jalna-city1-79eb71f1.png','Shri Dattashram, Jalna City[1]','Shri Dattashram, Jalna City[1]','https://www.justdial.com/Jalna/Shri-Datta-Ashram-Devmurthi-Satguru-Nagar-Jalna-City/9999P2482-2482-170208193601-G9Z8_BZDET'),(15333,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/apart-from-commercial-alcohol-there-are-local-vari_zZ9qoaC.jpg','Apart from commercial alcohol, there are local varieties that are prepared in the district. In Jalna district, near the boundary of Parbhani district, there are villages where Lamhan (Banjara) people live; these basti,  or villages, are called Tanda. They produce their local alcohol from mahua trees; the consumption of the local alcohol in this area is very high. Many people from this community produce alcohol in their own homes, and some of them sell it locally (Source: CKA Archives).','Apart from commercial alcohol, there are local varieties that are prepared in the district. In Jalna district, near the boundary of Parbhani district, there are villages where Lamhan (Banjara) people live; these basti,  or villages, are called Tanda. They produce their local alcohol from mahua trees; the consumption of the local alcohol in this area is very high. Many people from this community produce alcohol in their own homes, and some of them sell it locally (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15336,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/rajana-plant-source-cka-archives-f59e23b2.jpg','Rajana Plant  (Source: CKA Archives).','Rajana Plant  (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15337,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/phang-source-cka-archives-be04c91a.jpg','Phang (Source: CKA Archives).','Phang (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15338,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/tandulja-source-cka-archives-9c067c39.png','Tandulja  (Source: CKA Archives).','Tandulja  (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15339,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/vagote-source-cka-archives-e4f25e6e.jpg','Vagote (Source: CKA Archives).','Vagote (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15342,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/moong-puri-consists-of-a-thick-creamy-moong-dal-ye_29VcC6q.jpg','Moong Puri consists of a thick, creamy moong dal (yellow lentil) curry and puris (deep-fried puffed bread). The dal is typically prepared with a blend of spices, often including cumin, coriander, and red chili powder. This combination of flavorful dal and puris is a popular choice for breakfast or a light meal (Source: CKA Archives).','Moong Puri consists of a thick, creamy moong dal (yellow lentil) curry and puris (deep-fried puffed bread). The dal is typically prepared with a blend of spices, often including cumin, coriander, and red chili powder. This combination of flavorful dal and puris is a popular choice for breakfast or a light meal (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15344,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/sindhi-malpua-is-a-sweet-dish-that-holds-a-special_inPmmSv.jpg','Sindhi Malpua is a sweet dish that holds a special place in Sindhi cuisine. These golden-brown pancakes are made with a batter of flour, milk, and sugar, and then deep-fried to perfection. They are often served with a sweet syrup infused with cardamom and saffron, elevating their flavor to heavenly heights. It is enjoyed on special occasions and festivals, and it\'s a popular breakfast or dessert option (Source: CKA Archives).','Sindhi Malpua is a sweet dish that holds a special place in Sindhi cuisine. These golden-brown pancakes are made with a batter of flour, milk, and sugar, and then deep-fried to perfection. They are often served with a sweet syrup infused with cardamom and saffron, elevating their flavor to heavenly heights. It is enjoyed on special occasions and festivals, and it\'s a popular breakfast or dessert option (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15346,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/this-dish-originated-in-rajasthan-and-due-to-migra_6bAF5wH.jpg','This dish originated in Rajasthan and, due to migration, it has become popular in the Khandesh and Marathwada regions. In Rajasthan, dal bati is circular in shape, but in Jalna, it is toast-like and rectangular. Additionally, the dal in Jalna is spicier than in Rajasthan. First, they mix soybean and wheat flour to make the bhatti, then they boil it. When serving, they deep fry it in oil, resulting in a dish that is crunchier on the outside and softer on the inside  (Source: CKA Archives).','This dish originated in Rajasthan and, due to migration, it has become popular in the Khandesh and Marathwada regions. In Rajasthan, dal bati is circular in shape, but in Jalna, it is toast-like and rectangular. Additionally, the dal in Jalna is spicier than in Rajasthan. First, they mix soybean and wheat flour to make the bhatti, then they boil it. When serving, they deep fry it in oil, resulting in a dish that is crunchier on the outside and softer on the inside  (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15348,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/67e5dc3abaf84097b15e7ad6c5c91e3d-27123c33.jpg','','',''),(15351,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/mathura-lassi-has-been-serving-customers-for-45-ye_3sCKwX7.jpg','Mathura lassi has been serving customers for 45 years. It is located near Phool Bazaar in New Jalna. Their unique selling point is the usage of lots of cream in sweet lassi. They also serve other snacks like sabudana vada, samosa, and bhajis (Source: CKA Archives).','Mathura lassi has been serving customers for 45 years. It is located near Phool Bazaar in New Jalna. Their unique selling point is the usage of lots of cream in sweet lassi. They also serve other snacks like sabudana vada, samosa, and bhajis (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15353,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/food/it-is-located-in-new-jalna-and-was-started-by-the-_NnfoL3B.jpg','It is located in New Jalna and was started by the Lareja family. They migrated to Samrath in Uttar Pradesh from Sindh, Pakistan, in 1947 during the partition. Later, they moved to Jalna with the help of relatives. Initially, they tried the hotel business but gained popularity with their unique Sindhi dish, moong puri. Sindhi people consume more moong dal due to its health benefits; the dal is boiled, and the puri is fried in sunflower oil. Their specialty is hot and fresh puri and malpua served with moong dal and some masala on top, which gives it a unique taste. The texture of their malpua is also unique, very soft on the inside and made from wheat flour (Source: CKA Archives).','It is located in New Jalna and was started by the Lareja family. They migrated to Samrath in Uttar Pradesh from Sindh, Pakistan, in 1947 during the partition. Later, they moved to Jalna with the help of relatives. Initially, they tried the hotel business but gained popularity with their unique Sindhi dish, moong puri. Sindhi people consume more moong dal due to its health benefits; the dal is boiled, and the puri is fried in sunflower oil. Their specialty is hot and fresh puri and malpua served with moong dal and some masala on top, which gives it a unique taste. The texture of their malpua is also unique, very soft on the inside and made from wheat flour (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15372,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/markets/krushi-utpanna-bazaar-source-cka-archives-0300078e.png','Krushi Utpanna Bazaar (Source: CKA Archives)','Krushi Utpanna Bazaar (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(15377,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/markets/mangal-bazaar-may-2024-source-cka-archives-ca8bb6e9.png','Mangal Bazaar, May 2024 (Source: CKA Archives)','Mangal Bazaar, May 2024 (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(15402,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/sports-games/district-sports-stadium-source-cka-archive_tHJubIY.png','District Sports Stadium (Source: CKA Archives).','District Sports Stadium (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(15404,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/sports-games/inside-the-guru-ram-charan-ustad-bhakt-akh_U7HFCVO.jpg','Inside the Guru Ram Charan Ustad Bhakt Akhada, (Source: CKA Archives).','Inside the Guru Ram Charan Ustad Bhakt Akhada, (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(15407,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/sports-games/samarth-hanuman-akhada-jalna-source-cka-ar_Z56KRUL.jpg','Samarth Hanuman Akhada, Jalna (Source: CKA Archives).','Samarth Hanuman Akhada, Jalna (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(15420,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/stories/parner-located-in-the-rajakar-kingdom-and-gover_eWpumO2.png','Parner, located in the Rajakar kingdom and governed by the just but strict Governor Tanaji Deshmukh, was peaceful. The people admired his wisdom and impartiality in justice. Tanaji was noted for his devotion to the Mahalaxmi Devi, from whom he sought aashirwad at the Matsyodari Mandir in Ambad.','Parner, located in the Rajakar kingdom and governed by the just but strict Governor Tanaji Deshmukh, was peaceful. The people admired his wisdom and impartiality in justice. Tanaji was noted for his devotion to the Mahalaxmi Devi, from whom he sought aashirwad at the Matsyodari Mandir in Ambad.',''),(15428,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/stories/shindi-tree1-d633e05d.png','Shindi Tree[1]','Shindi Tree[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sendhi_%28Hindi-_%E0%A4%B8%E0%A5%87%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%A7%E0%A5%80%29_%283167537184%29.jpg'),(15433,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/stories/the-warrior-mahadji-shinde-was-a-devotee-of-ana_YZipRWV.png','The warrior Mahadji Shinde was a devotee of Anandi Swami from Jalna. When he struggled to win a prolonged battle, a Brahmin from his army heard about Anandi Swami and visited Jalna to explain the situation regarding the war. Anandi Swami instructed him that the entire army should chant \"Jai Shree Anandi\" before going into battle. The Brahmin conveyed this message to Mahadji Shinde, and the next day, after following these instructions, they won the war. As a result, the king became a devotee and traveled to Jalna to seek Anandi Swami\'s aashirwad. After waiting for several days, Swami did not grant blessings to Mahadji but instead blessed his son, indicating a shift in power within the kingdom (Source: CKA Archives).','The warrior Mahadji Shinde was a devotee of Anandi Swami from Jalna. When he struggled to win a prolonged battle, a Brahmin from his army heard about Anandi Swami and visited Jalna to explain the situation regarding the war. Anandi Swami instructed him that the entire army should chant \"Jai Shree Anandi\" before going into battle. The Brahmin conveyed this message to Mahadji Shinde, and the next day, after following these instructions, they won the war. As a result, the king became a devotee and traveled to Jalna to seek Anandi Swami\'s aashirwad. After waiting for several days, Swami did not grant blessings to Mahadji but instead blessed his son, indicating a shift in power within the kingdom (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15435,'culture/images/maharashtra/jalna/stories/sandip-ade-hails-from-pangri-village-in-the-man_DnHXgvt.jpg','Sandip Ade hails from Pangri village in the Mantha taluka of Jalna district and belongs to the Banjara community. He recounts a childhood experience that led him to leave school due to the fear of being punished by his teacher. After completing the third standard, Sandip decided to stop attending school because of a teacher who frequently beat the students. He reflects that, even if he had not secured a job after his education, he would have had a better understanding of the world. Following his departure from school, he began working on a farm and started grazing cattle (Source: CKA Archives).','Sandip Ade hails from Pangri village in the Mantha taluka of Jalna district and belongs to the Banjara community. He recounts a childhood experience that led him to leave school due to the fear of being punished by his teacher. After completing the third standard, Sandip decided to stop attending school because of a teacher who frequently beat the students. He reflects that, even if he had not secured a job after his education, he would have had a better understanding of the world. Following his departure from school, he began working on a farm and started grazing cattle (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(15444,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-mahalakshmi-mandir-is-an-example-of_70UsYDY.png','The Mahalakshmi Mandir is an example of Hemadpanthi architecture, constructed from black basalt without the use of mortar, showcasing the precision and durability of medieval Indian stone craftsmanship.[1]','The Mahalakshmi Mandir is an example of Hemadpanthi architecture, constructed from black basalt without the use of mortar, showcasing the precision and durability of medieval Indian stone craftsmanship.[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahalaxmi_Temple,_Kolhapur.jpg'),(15446,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-exterior-of-the-mahalakshmi-mandir-_bd5oxgp.png','The exterior of the Mahalakshmi Mandir features detailed carvings and sculptures. Notably, the sculpture of Bhagwan Krishna is painted in vibrant colors.[2]','The exterior of the Mahalakshmi Mandir features detailed carvings and sculptures. Notably, the sculpture of Bhagwan Krishna is painted in vibrant colors.[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exterior_wall_carvings_at_Shree_Mahalaxmi_temple,_kolhapur.jpg'),(15450,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-kopeshwar-mandir-in-khidrapur-built_p3IUAx4.png','The Kopeshwar Mandir in Khidrapur, built in the Bhumija style, is constructed entirely from black basalt stone and features finely cut masonry and sculptural bands.[3]','The Kopeshwar Mandir in Khidrapur, built in the Bhumija style, is constructed entirely from black basalt stone and features finely cut masonry and sculptural bands.[3]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kopeshwar_Temple-Khidrapur-Maharashtra-IMG_0737.jpg'),(15452,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-sabhamandap-of-kopeshwar-mandir-is-_UY7mQSf.png','The Sabhamandap of Kopeshwar Mandir is supported by 60 intricately carved pillars.[4]','The Sabhamandap of Kopeshwar Mandir is supported by 60 intricately carved pillars.[4]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sabha_mandap_khidrapur.jpg'),(15454,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-adhisthana-of-the-kopeshwar-mandir-_nxDUGBc.png','The Adhisthana of the Kopeshwar Mandir featuring the Gaja Patta, a frieze of 92 carved elephants, symbolizing strength and spirituality.[5]','The Adhisthana of the Kopeshwar Mandir featuring the Gaja Patta, a frieze of 92 carved elephants, symbolizing strength and spirituality.[5]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plinth_at_Khidrapur.jpg'),(15458,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/panhala-fort-is-an-example-of-medieval-_4Rzdak8.png','Panhala Fort is an example of medieval military architecture, blending Bijapuri style with Maratha military engineering.[6]','Panhala Fort is an example of medieval military architecture, blending Bijapuri style with Maratha military engineering.[6]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panhala_fort.JPG'),(15460,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-view-of-the-teen-darwaza-konkani-darw_NGOe2O9.png','A view of the Teen Darwaza (Konkani Darwaza) from the inner fort side, showcasing its imposing black stone structure and strategic military design.[7]','A view of the Teen Darwaza (Konkani Darwaza) from the inner fort side, showcasing its imposing black stone structure and strategic military design.[7]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panhala_Fort#Teen_Darwaza'),(15462,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-exterior-of-sajjakoti-showcases-its_QiAWbMs.png','The exterior of Sajjakoti showcases its balcony section, with arched openings, designed for strategic observation and ventilation.[8]','The exterior of Sajjakoti showcases its balcony section, with arched openings, designed for strategic observation and ventilation.[8]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sajja_Kothi_of_Panhala_Fort.jpg'),(15464,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/constructed-in-the-bijapuri-style-ambar_NmFD7O5.png','Constructed in the Bijapuri style, Ambarkhana is built with thick stone walls, featuring large vaulted openings that serve as granaries to store provisions.[9]','Constructed in the Bijapuri style, Ambarkhana is built with thick stone walls, featuring large vaulted openings that serve as granaries to store provisions.[9]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ambarkhana_of_Fort_Panhala.jpg'),(15468,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/bhavani-mandap-features-thick-stone-wal_7PDEvOM.png','Bhavani Mandap features thick stone walls, arched openings, and fine carvings that reflect traditional architectural practices of its time.[10]','Bhavani Mandap features thick stone walls, arched openings, and fine carvings that reflect traditional architectural practices of its time.[10]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhavani_Mandap'),(15472,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-town-hall-museum-displays-neo-gothi_gIrwE65.png','The Town Hall Museum displays neo-Gothic architecture with pointed arches, tall windows, and stone masonry that reflect colonial-era design.[11]','The Town Hall Museum displays neo-Gothic architecture with pointed arches, tall windows, and stone masonry that reflect colonial-era design.[11]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Town_Hall_Museum,_Kolhapur.jpg'),(15475,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-new-palace-blends-indo-saracenic-an_wIncmOZ.png','The New Palace blends Indo-Saracenic and Renaissance styles with regional influences, constructed in basalt and sandstone with detailed architectural features.[12]','The New Palace blends Indo-Saracenic and Renaissance styles with regional influences, constructed in basalt and sandstone with detailed architectural features.[12]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kolhapur_New_Palace.jpg#:~:text=The%20Kolhapur%20New%20Palace.,Shri%20Chhatrapati%20Shahu%20Maharaj%20himself'),(15477,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-new-palaces-85-foot-high-clock-towe_5kjKlhH.png','The New Palace’s 85-foot-high clock tower features a Char-Bangla style canopy and a domed chhatri, housing one of India’s largest mechanical clocks, crafted in England in 1877.[13]','The New Palace’s 85-foot-high clock tower features a Char-Bangla style canopy and a domed chhatri, housing one of India’s largest mechanical clocks, crafted in England in 1877.[13]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Palace_clock_tower_(Kolhapur)_(2066168180).jpg'),(15478,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-facade-of-the-new-palace-showcases-_vM3vzRH.png','The façade of the New Palace showcases Indo-Saracenic arches, mandir-style columns, and carved stone detailing.[14]','The façade of the New Palace showcases Indo-Saracenic arches, mandir-style columns, and carved stone detailing.[14]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carved_arches_of_the_New_Palace.jpg'),(15482,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/shalini-palaces-black-basalt-and-italia_r7ZeTGt.png','Shalini Palace’s black basalt and Italian marble facade features wide stone arches, a regal porch, and a central clock tower, reflecting Indo-Saracenic and Renaissance styles.[15]','Shalini Palace’s black basalt and Italian marble facade features wide stone arches, a regal porch, and a central clock tower, reflecting Indo-Saracenic and Renaissance styles.[15]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shalini_Palace,_Kolhapur,_Southern_Maharashtra,_India_.IMG_20190113_080800.jpg'),(15488,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-beautiful-19th-century-residence-wh_6PD6spS.jpg','The beautiful 19th century residence which has been home to generations of the Sarnaik family. (Source: CKA Archives)','The beautiful 19th century residence which has been home to generations of the Sarnaik family. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15490,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/street-view-of-sarnaik-galli-showcasing_S01CVZs.jpg','Street view of Sarnaik Galli showcasing the closely packed houses and intimate neighborhood setting.(Source: CKA Archives)','Street view of Sarnaik Galli showcasing the closely packed houses and intimate neighborhood setting.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15492,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/notice-how-the-plinth-of-the-house-is-l_iHzMNvR.jpg','Notice how the plinth of the house is lower compared to the others in the lane, possibly meant for easy entry. Also see the way the residence shares its walls with the adjoining houses in the galli without leaving any space, showcasing how intimate the character of the street is. (Source: CKA Archives)','Notice how the plinth of the house is lower compared to the others in the lane, possibly meant for easy entry. Also see the way the residence shares its walls with the adjoining houses in the galli without leaving any space, showcasing how intimate the character of the street is. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15494,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/stone-is-a-fundamental-material-which-f_KRctTqk.jpg','Stone is a fundamental material which forms the composite structure of the house. From the plinth to the exterior walls of the second floor and the balcony flooring, the meticulous stone masonry work is evident. (Source: CKA Archives)','Stone is a fundamental material which forms the composite structure of the house. From the plinth to the exterior walls of the second floor and the balcony flooring, the meticulous stone masonry work is evident. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15495,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/wood-is-another-material-which-makes-up_6L57zAX.jpg','Wood is another material which makes up the composite structure of the house. One can usually spot the material on the stairs or columns which all have a stone base. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wood is another material which makes up the composite structure of the house. One can usually spot the material on the stairs or columns which all have a stone base. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15496,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-close-up-of-a-wooden-column-in-the-re_YeSP8zW.jpg','A close-up of a wooden column in the residence, set atop a stone base. (Source: CKA Archives)','A close-up of a wooden column in the residence, set atop a stone base. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15498,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-house-features-traditional-cow-dung_rPyXvh0.jpg','The house features traditional cow dung spread flooring, a method no longer used in modern constructions.(Source: CKA Archives)','The house features traditional cow dung spread flooring, a method no longer used in modern constructions.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15500,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-entrance-door-of-the-residence-is-a_TKTSfga.jpg','The entrance door of the residence is adorned with a toran, a traditional cultural element. Notice the stone walls on either side, as well as the construction of the door alongside details like wooden planks and visible screws. (Source: CKA Archives)','The entrance door of the residence is adorned with a toran, a traditional cultural element. Notice the stone walls on either side, as well as the construction of the door alongside details like wooden planks and visible screws. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15502,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-floral-carving-at-the-choukat-top-o_U3TU53S.jpg','The floral carving at the choukat (top) of the entrance door.(Source: CKA Archives)','The floral carving at the choukat (top) of the entrance door.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15504,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-devlis-positioned-beside-the-entran_mlqURvK.jpg','The devlis positioned beside the entrance door, traditionally used for placing oil lamps. Notice the overall color scheme of the house remains neutral, except for the balcony walls, which stand out in a distinct shade of green. (Source: CKA Archives)','The devlis positioned beside the entrance door, traditionally used for placing oil lamps. Notice the overall color scheme of the house remains neutral, except for the balcony walls, which stand out in a distinct shade of green. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15506,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-first-floor-has-a-door-leading-to-t_XDmPMsw.jpg','The first floor has a door leading to the balcony, with frames that are without glass. (Source: CKA Archives)','The first floor has a door leading to the balcony, with frames that are without glass. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15507,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-double-leaf-door-that-leads-to-the-_VzVa2Nn.jpg','The double-leaf door that leads to the kitchen has a locking system that is colloquially referred to as the ‘kadi koynda.’ (Source: CKA Archives)','The double-leaf door that leads to the kitchen has a locking system that is colloquially referred to as the ‘kadi koynda.’ (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15508,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-peculiar-stone-which-has-been-traditi_BXu4aXj.jpg','A peculiar stone which has been traditionally used as a door stopper across many olden homes. (Source: CKA Archives)','A peculiar stone which has been traditionally used as a door stopper across many olden homes. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15510,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/windows-with-traditional-railing-gaj-so_wXzV0Si.jpg','Windows with traditional railing (gaj). (Source: CKA Archives)','Windows with traditional railing (gaj). (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15511,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-window-door-and-frame-is-made-of-wo_Agr6DaV.jpg','The window door and frame is made of wood. (Source: CKA Archives)','The window door and frame is made of wood. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15513,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-balcony-of-the-residence-has-a-rail_pSfu0Hz.jpg','The balcony of the residence has a railing with a very peculiar geometric design. This design, locals say, is common and can often be spotted in the neighborhood as if it were a trend. (Source: CKA Archives)','The balcony of the residence has a railing with a very peculiar geometric design. This design, locals say, is common and can often be spotted in the neighborhood as if it were a trend. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15514,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-few-motifs-can-be-spotted-within-the-_JrM2BMo.jpg','A few motifs can be spotted within the structure with one of them being below the railing. Notice the intricate carvings that may resemble the shape of leaves. (Source: CKA Archives)','A few motifs can be spotted within the structure with one of them being below the railing. Notice the intricate carvings that may resemble the shape of leaves. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15516,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-saana-or-the-small-space-which-is-c_NOImuxP.jpg','The Saana or the small space which is carved into the ‘tuli’ (wooden slab) of the first storey of the house.Notably, when guests of high regard showed up uninvited, the space was used by women to go up to the upper storey of the house.(Source: CKA Archives)','The Saana or the small space which is carved into the ‘tuli’ (wooden slab) of the first storey of the house.Notably, when guests of high regard showed up uninvited, the space was used by women to go up to the upper storey of the house.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15518,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-vintage-lampshade-hanging-from-the-ce_JaXTSOf.jpg','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15520,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-vintage-lampshade-hanging-from-the-ce_tuM0geb.jpg','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15522,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-vintage-lampshade-hanging-from-the-ce_6QUYgiM.jpg','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)','A vintage lampshade hanging from the ceiling, showcasing traditional lighting solutions used before electricity became commonplace. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15524,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/large-handis-that-served-as-essential-s_2oioGGH.jpg','Large handis that served as essential storage containers for grains and other food provisions in earlier times. (Source: CKA Archives)','Large handis that served as essential storage containers for grains and other food provisions in earlier times. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15525,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-wooden-cupboard-embedded-directly-int_qOcPJDp.jpg','A wooden cupboard embedded directly into the wall structure, showcasing a built-in furniture design from a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)','A wooden cupboard embedded directly into the wall structure, showcasing a built-in furniture design from a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15527,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-wooden-cupboard-embedded-directly-int_lpwGsbZ.jpg','A wooden cupboard embedded directly into the wall structure, showcasing a built-in furniture design from a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)','A wooden cupboard embedded directly into the wall structure, showcasing a built-in furniture design from a bygone era. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15530,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-single-storey-residence-with-a-well-m_sGWdpXu.jpg','A single-storey residence with a well-maintained front lawn at Datta Galli. (Source: CKA Archives)','A single-storey residence with a well-maintained front lawn at Datta Galli. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15532,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-street-next-to-the-house-shows-the-_9rABSQ2.jpg','The street next to the house shows the quiet residential nature of the neighborhood with its tree-lined pathways. (Source: CKA Archives)','The street next to the house shows the quiet residential nature of the neighborhood with its tree-lined pathways. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15534,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-view-from-above-shows-how-the-streets_QDMnKpu.jpg','A view from above shows how the streets branch into smaller lanes, forming the unique layout of this established neighborhood. (Source: CKA Archives)','A view from above shows how the streets branch into smaller lanes, forming the unique layout of this established neighborhood. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15536,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-homes-layout-features-a-centrally-p_CAjSVbS.jpg','The home’s layout features a centrally positioned main building, complemented by a front lawn, a garage or parking area, and utility spaces arranged along the sides. (Source: CKA Archives)','The home’s layout features a centrally positioned main building, complemented by a front lawn, a garage or parking area, and utility spaces arranged along the sides. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15538,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-main-wooden-entrance-door-includes-_ksr1EzX.jpg','The main wooden entrance door includes a peephole for security and has an artificial toran above it. The torans here, in many ways, reflect a continuity in the practice adding cultural elements to personalize one’s home. (Source: CKA Archives)','The main wooden entrance door includes a peephole for security and has an artificial toran above it. The torans here, in many ways, reflect a continuity in the practice adding cultural elements to personalize one’s home. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15540,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/an-old-wooden-door-has-been-kept-in-the_VHJ34qe.jpg','An old wooden door has been kept in the storeroom, offering a glimpse of the home\'s original features. (Source: CKA Archives)','An old wooden door has been kept in the storeroom, offering a glimpse of the home\'s original features. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15542,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-functional-iron-door-adjacent-to-the-_JUYebPW.jpg','A functional iron door adjacent to the kitchen provides access to utility spaces, demonstrating the practical material choices made for service-oriented areas of the home. (Source: CKA Archives)','A functional iron door adjacent to the kitchen provides access to utility spaces, demonstrating the practical material choices made for service-oriented areas of the home. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15543,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-gate-at-the-entrance-of-the-residen_Wsbkik8.jpg','The gate at the entrance of the residence is made up of iron. It has decorative elements at the top, which add both visual appeal and create a functional boundary marking. (Source: CKA Archives)','The gate at the entrance of the residence is made up of iron. It has decorative elements at the top, which add both visual appeal and create a functional boundary marking. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15545,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-decorative-door-knocker-on-the-kitche_oWs3j4S.jpg','A decorative door knocker on the kitchen door that opens to the backyard shows attention to small functional details. (Source: CKA Archives)','A decorative door knocker on the kitchen door that opens to the backyard shows attention to small functional details. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15547,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/windows-on-either-side-of-the-main-entr_CdDttxa.jpg','Windows on either side of the main entrance have modern protective railings while keeping the balanced design of the house front. (Source: CKA Archives)','Windows on either side of the main entrance have modern protective railings while keeping the balanced design of the house front. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15549,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/window-chajja-overhang-with-distinctive_C8qYokS.jpg','Window chajja (overhang) with distinctive roof-like design painted yellow and adorned with traditional motifs, illustrating the many decorative approaches that are tied to practical elements. (Source: CKA Archives)','Window chajja (overhang) with distinctive roof-like design painted yellow and adorned with traditional motifs, illustrating the many decorative approaches that are tied to practical elements. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15550,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-close-up-shows-the-detailed-decorativ_vCWHsUL.jpg','A close-up shows the detailed decorative work on the window overhang, revealing the craftsmanship that went into even functional parts of the home. (Source: CKA Archives)','A close-up shows the detailed decorative work on the window overhang, revealing the craftsmanship that went into even functional parts of the home. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15552,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-parapet-wall-with-a-decorative-cent_LdZbN9B.jpg','The parapet wall with a decorative central arch, partially finished in a soft peach hue. Its decorative design features a central arch, adding symmetry and visual appeal to the building’s facade. (Source: CKA Archives)','The parapet wall with a decorative central arch, partially finished in a soft peach hue. Its decorative design features a central arch, adding symmetry and visual appeal to the building’s facade. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15554,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-hall-has-no-pillars-or-columns-show_ckMw6Tr.jpg','The hall has no pillars or columns, showing a simple approach to design that emphasizes open space. (Source: CKA Archives)','The hall has no pillars or columns, showing a simple approach to design that emphasizes open space. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15556,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-recently-renovated-kitchen-features_9lRW4GI.jpg','The recently renovated kitchen features contemporary modular design elements with no structural separation from the dining area. (Source: CKA Archives)','The recently renovated kitchen features contemporary modular design elements with no structural separation from the dining area. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15558,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-hall-flooring-consists-of-mosaic-ti_z0wRNaE.jpg','The hall flooring consists of mosaic tiles, which were commonly used across semi-urban and urban areas throughout India during the late 20th century, representing typical material choices of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)','The hall flooring consists of mosaic tiles, which were commonly used across semi-urban and urban areas throughout India during the late 20th century, representing typical material choices of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15560,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-taxidermy-specimen-mounted-on-the-wal_UUGYlO2.jpg','A taxidermy specimen mounted on the wall, an artifact from an era when hunting was legal, representing a once-common decorative approach found in many residences of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)','A taxidermy specimen mounted on the wall, an artifact from an era when hunting was legal, representing a once-common decorative approach found in many residences of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15562,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-property-boundary-combines-a-railin_JsXMv8Y.jpg','The property boundary combines a railing at the top with trees planted inside that serve as a living fence, blending built and natural elements to define the home\'s perimeter. (Source: CKA Archives)','The property boundary combines a railing at the top with trees planted inside that serve as a living fence, blending built and natural elements to define the home\'s perimeter. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15564,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-secondary-gate-separates-the-garage-a_TfvTzvm.jpg','A secondary gate separates the garage and front yard from the lawn and main building, creating a thoughtful organization of the exterior spaces. (Source: CKA Archives)','A secondary gate separates the garage and front yard from the lawn and main building, creating a thoughtful organization of the exterior spaces. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15566,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-staircase-positioned-against-the-exte_A7XNNHp.jpg','A staircase positioned against the exterior wall offers access to the terrace, connecting the ground level to the upper outdoor space. (Source: CKA Archives)','A staircase positioned against the exterior wall offers access to the terrace, connecting the ground level to the upper outdoor space. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15568,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/cement-slab-roofing-covers-the-main-bui_5eDeVmT.jpg','Cement slab roofing covers the main building (excluding the storeroom), providing a durable protective layer for the primary living areas. (Source: CKA Archives)','Cement slab roofing covers the main building (excluding the storeroom), providing a durable protective layer for the primary living areas. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15569,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/corrugated-sheets-are-used-for-the-stor_C5Ms1aX.jpg','Corrugated sheets are used for the storage area’s roofing, distinguishing it from the primary structure. (Source: CKA Archives)','Corrugated sheets are used for the storage area’s roofing, distinguishing it from the primary structure. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15571,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/the-landscaped-front-yard-creates-a-gre_nWkZyEL.jpg','The landscaped front yard creates a green transition space between the street and the house. (Source: CKA Archives)','The landscaped front yard creates a green transition space between the street and the house. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15573,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/architecture/a-linear-utility-area-extends-along-the_ly8NSlE.jpg','A linear utility area extends along the length of the house adjacent to the kitchen, facilitating service activities