ives)','The entrance to Chhatrapati Tararani Rajwada, a key historical site now repurposed as a school. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15876,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-agad-at-panhala-built-by-rajarshi_1iFlS68.jpg','The अग्गड (Agad) at Panhala; built by Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj, this ground was used for the traditional game of Sathmari, where trained men faced off with tamed elephants.(Source: CKA Archives)','The अग्गड (Agad) at Panhala; built by Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj, this ground was used for the traditional game of Sathmari, where trained men faced off with tamed elephants.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15878,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/a-closer-look-at-the-agad-at-panhala-_qV7MGdP.jpg','A closer look at the Agad at Panhala, built by Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj for the traditional game of Sathmari. (Source: CKA Archives)','A closer look at the Agad at Panhala, built by Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj for the traditional game of Sathmari. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15882,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/a-murti-of-chhtrapati-ii-sambhaji-mah_TGj9sYm.jpg','A murti of Chhtrapati II Sambhaji Maharaj at the Mandir at Panhala.(Source: CKA Archives)','A murti of Chhtrapati II Sambhaji Maharaj at the Mandir at Panhala.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15884,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/d176823b2df74e2482143b43898a6825-a2ad3e74.jpg','','',''),(15885,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/one-step-leading-to-the-mandir-is-eng_yVgfzxp.jpg','One step leading to the Mandir is engraved with an inscription. (Source: CKA Archives)','One step leading to the Mandir is engraved with an inscription. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15886,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-mandir-with-intricately-designed-_DI33Gui.jpg','The Mandir with intricately designed pillars.(Source: CKA Archives)','The Mandir with intricately designed pillars.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15887,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/copper-pillars-inside-the-garbha-grih_LtqU9gg.jpg','Copper pillars inside the garbha griha, showcasing exquisite craftsmanship.(Source: CKA Archives)','Copper pillars inside the garbha griha, showcasing exquisite craftsmanship.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15890,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-majestic-facade-of-pant-amatya-ba_76B3llJ.jpg','The majestic facade of Pant Amatya Bavdekar Wada, Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)','The majestic facade of Pant Amatya Bavdekar Wada, Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15894,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-circular-structure-of-panyacha-kh_n7ccGQZ.jpg','The circular structure of Panyacha khajina which lies near the Katyayani Hill in Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)','The circular structure of Panyacha khajina which lies near the Katyayani Hill in Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15896,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/plaque-commemorating-the-key-figures-_CaqWhUs.jpg','Plaque commemorating the key figures behind the creation of Panyacha Khajina reservoir. (Source: CKA Archives)','Plaque commemorating the key figures behind the creation of Panyacha Khajina reservoir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15900,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-stream-at-pavankhind-quietly-flow_1l6Fxp2.jpg','The stream at Pavankhind, quietly flowing through the rugged terrains where brave Maratha warriors once fought. (Source: CKA Archives)','The stream at Pavankhind, quietly flowing through the rugged terrains where brave Maratha warriors once fought. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15902,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-samadhi-shaurya-sthal-built-in-ho_WMTTlsY.jpg','The Samadhi (Shaurya Sthal) built in honor of Baji Prabhu Despande and his soldiers, commemorating their sacrifice at Pavankhind.(Source: CKA Archives)','The Samadhi (Shaurya Sthal) built in honor of Baji Prabhu Despande and his soldiers, commemorating their sacrifice at Pavankhind.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15906,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/ramling-mandiris-located-near-palsamb_Abol6tn.png','Ramling Mandiris located near Palsambe in the Gaganbawda Tehsil of Kolhapur District.[2]','Ramling Mandiris located near Palsambe in the Gaganbawda Tehsil of Kolhapur District.[2]','https://www.facebook.com/kolhapurtourism24/posts/ramling-mandirthe-cave-temple-of-ramling-is-on-the-side-of-a-rocky-hill-the-chie/2038707356360486/'),(15910,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/a-glimpse-of-the-grand-architectural-_HfZe5aZ.jpg','A glimpse of the grand architectural exterior of Shalini Palace, standing as an iconic symbol of Kolhapur\'s royal history. (Source: CKA Archives)','A glimpse of the grand architectural exterior of Shalini Palace, standing as an iconic symbol of Kolhapur\'s royal history. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15913,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/shankar-mandir-which-lies-in-the-kasb_tWNQKUt.jpg','Shankar Mandir which lies in the Kasba Beed area of Kolhapur district. (Source: CKA Archives)','Shankar Mandir which lies in the Kasba Beed area of Kolhapur district. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15915,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/various-sized-bells-hang-above-the-en_V9kuPgz.jpg','Various-sized bells hang above the entrance to the inner sanctum of the mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','Various-sized bells hang above the entrance to the inner sanctum of the mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15916,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/intricate-carvings-which-seem-histori_ZEkQnOi.jpg','Intricate carvings which seem historic in their nature lie outside the Mandir premises. In many of these stone artworks, one can find many peculiar depictions involving women and battles. (Source: CKA Archives)','Intricate carvings which seem historic in their nature lie outside the Mandir premises. In many of these stone artworks, one can find many peculiar depictions involving women and battles. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15919,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-shikhara-of-the-binkhambi-mandir-_A3XMs15.jpg','The Shikhara of the Binkhambi Mandir, which lies in theShivaji Peth area of Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)','The Shikhara of the Binkhambi Mandir, which lies in theShivaji Peth area of Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15921,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-garbhagriha-of-thebinkhambi-mandi_7ymkObA.jpg','The garbhagriha of theBinkhambi Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)','The garbhagriha of theBinkhambi Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15924,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/grand-entrance-to-the-siddhagiri-muse_tKnZeMo.jpg','Grand entrance to the Siddhagiri Museum in Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)','Grand entrance to the Siddhagiri Museum in Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15926,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/directional-board-at-siddhagiri-gramj_iq5N0dh.jpg','Directional Board at Siddhagiri Gramjivan Museum.  (Source: CKA Archives)','Directional Board at Siddhagiri Gramjivan Museum.  (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15927,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/some-miniature-sculptures-displayed-a_qttL6IN.jpg','Some miniature sculptures displayed at the museum. (Source: CKA Archives)','Some miniature sculptures displayed at the museum. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15929,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/a-towering-42-foot-statue-of-bhagwan-_dY6B0Fl.jpg','A towering 42-foot statue of Bhagwan Shiv marks the entrance to the Siddhagiri Math.  (Source: CKA Archives)','A towering 42-foot statue of Bhagwan Shiv marks the entrance to the Siddhagiri Math.  (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15930,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/a-historic-mandir-within-the-museum-g_W4pWShg.jpg','A historic mandir within the museum grounds, believed to have stood for over 500 years.(Source: CKA Archives)','A historic mandir within the museum grounds, believed to have stood for over 500 years.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15933,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/tembai-devi-mandir-which-stands-atop-_jd29WDT.jpg','Tembai Devi Mandir which stands atop the Tembai Hill in Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)','Tembai Devi Mandir which stands atop the Tembai Hill in Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15935,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/tembai-devi-of-the-tembai-devi-mandir_krUQRsR.jpg','Tembai Devi of the Tembai Devi Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)','Tembai Devi of the Tembai Devi Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15939,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-town-hall-an-architectural-landma_gTX0mIb.jpg','The Town Hall, an architectural landmark in Kolhapur, has housed the City Museum since its establishment in 1945–46. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Town Hall, an architectural landmark in Kolhapur, has housed the City Museum since its establishment in 1945–46. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15941,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-grand-entrance-of-the-city-museum_mCa1AXq.jpg','The grand entrance of the City Museum, set within the Town Hall as a striking example of colonial-era Gothic architecture in the district. (Source: CKA Archives)','The grand entrance of the City Museum, set within the Town Hall as a striking example of colonial-era Gothic architecture in the district. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15943,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/the-commemorative-plaque-marking-the-_es2G0de.jpg','The commemorative plaque marking the establishment of the City Museum in 1945–46, underscoring its role in preserving Kolhapur’s cultural heritage. (Source: CKA Archives)','The commemorative plaque marking the establishment of the City Museum in 1945–46, underscoring its role in preserving Kolhapur’s cultural heritage. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15948,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/shree-kshetra-vithaal-birdev-mandir-w_1NEPJCM.jpg','Shree Kshetra Vithaal Birdev Mandir which lies in thevillage of Pattankodoli in Hatkanangale taluka, Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)','Shree Kshetra Vithaal Birdev Mandir which lies in thevillage of Pattankodoli in Hatkanangale taluka, Kolhapur.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15950,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/shree-vitthal-birdev-and-devi-bhaguba_vqUmPYH.jpg','Shree Vitthal, Birdev, and Devi Bhagubai of the Vitthal Birdev Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)','Shree Vitthal, Birdev, and Devi Bhagubai of the Vitthal Birdev Mandir.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15952,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/traditional-prasad-including-nachani-_9wAtebv.jpg','Traditional prasad, including Nachani Ambil, being distributed to devotees by the mandir committee.(Source: CKA Archives)','Traditional prasad, including Nachani Ambil, being distributed to devotees by the mandir committee.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15956,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/vitthal-rukami-mandir-which-lies-in-s_Bt4s91p.jpg','Vitthal Rukami Mandir which lies in Shendur, Kolhapur district.(Source: CKA Archives)','Vitthal Rukami Mandir which lies in Shendur, Kolhapur district.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15959,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/cultural-sites/wilder-memorial-church-shahupuri-kolh_ZOrXqRz.jpg','Wilder Memorial Church, Shahupuri, Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wilder Memorial Church, Shahupuri, Kolhapur. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(15991,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/festivals-fairs/murti-of-mahalaxmi-illuminated-by-su_LIGwP0b.png','Murti of Mahalaxmi illuminated by sunlight during Kirnotsav[1]','Murti of Mahalaxmi illuminated by sunlight during Kirnotsav[1]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A2q1UsV9JEM'),(15994,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/festivals-fairs/a-sea-of-yellow-as-bhandara-spreads-_mWR4nxr.png','A sea of yellow as bhandara spreads across streets and people[2]','A sea of yellow as bhandara spreads across streets and people[2]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nKi94bQxcgc'),(15997,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/festivals-fairs/celebrations-in-full-swing-with-pink_zaEkBHj.png','Celebrations in full swing with pink gulal everywhere[3]','Celebrations in full swing with pink gulal everywhere[3]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IWw_Epl6z9Y'),(16008,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/kolhapuri-misal-ingredients1-4abc42cb.png','Kolhapuri Misal Ingredients[1]','Kolhapuri Misal Ingredients[1]','https://dinewithgitanjali.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/WhatsApp-Image-2020-07-08-at-6.11.00-PM.jpeg'),(16011,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/kolhapuri-gul2-8b5a6a65.png','Kolhapuri Gul[2]','Kolhapuri Gul[2]','https://rukminim2.flixcart.com/image/750/900/xif0q/jaggery/e/k/s/900-block-special-kolhapuri-jaggery-1-box-patil-gul-original-imagms7xpjsvrdsn.jpeg?q=20&crop=false'),(16018,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/shree-mahalaxmi-annachatra-seva-trust3-eb901928.png','Shree Mahalaxmi Annachatra Seva Trust[3]','Shree Mahalaxmi Annachatra Seva Trust[3]','https://www.mahalaxmisevatrust.org/mahalaxmisevatrust/slider/mahalaxmi-sevatrust-img-01.jpg'),(16024,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/kolhapuri-misal-pav4-eb6b04c8.png','Kolhapuri Misal Pav[4]','Kolhapuri Misal Pav[4]','https://www.archanaskitchen.com/kolhapuri-misal-pav-recipe'),(16027,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/tambda-and-pandhra-rassa5-b5c757c1.png','Tambda and Pandhra Rassa[5]','Tambda and Pandhra Rassa[5]','https://cookpad.com/in/recipes/2615198-kolhapuri-tambda-rassa-recipe'),(16030,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/sukha-mutton6-0080e6de.png','Sukha Mutton[6]','Sukha Mutton[6]','https://www.cookwithnabeela.com/recipe/mutton-kolhapuri/'),(16033,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/bharli-vangi7-6c419a06.png','Bharli Vangi[7]','Bharli Vangi[7]','https://tummy-to-heart.com/kolhapuri-masala-vangi-kolhapuri-eggplant/'),(16036,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/4d9bc198adfa4190a065e7f6c18b0b14-c45ba34e.jpg','','',''),(16039,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/trushashanti-is-famous-for-its-creamy-and-flavo_TO9v4AT.png','Trushashanti is famous for its creamy and flavorful ice creams. Established in 1936 by Ganpat Pawar, it is located on Mahadwar Road and has become a beloved spot in Kolhapur. In addition to their ice creams, the eatery offers highly recommended doodh, lassi, and cold drinks. Trushashanti has expanded to two branches, with the second branch also gaining popularity for serving delicious Pavbhaji, Dahiwada, Pulav, and other local favorites (Source: CKA Archives).','Trushashanti is famous for its creamy and flavorful ice creams. Established in 1936 by Ganpat Pawar, it is located on Mahadwar Road and has become a beloved spot in Kolhapur. In addition to their ice creams, the eatery offers highly recommended doodh, lassi, and cold drinks. Trushashanti has expanded to two branches, with the second branch also gaining popularity for serving delicious Pavbhaji, Dahiwada, Pulav, and other local favorites (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(16041,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/food/kolhapuri-sangeet-chivda-is-a-well-known-shop-l_D2GZZwl.png','Kolhapuri Sangeet Chivda is a well-known shop located on the main road after exiting the Kolhapur Mahalaxmi temple. Established in 1892 by Govind Vinayak Marathe, the shop earned its name because it was popular among music lovers and theatergoers in Kolhapur, who enjoyed this chivda while heading home after watching plays and movies. The term \"sangeet\" reflects the cultural significance of the shop during a time when theaters were abundant in the area. The shop\'s main attraction is its chivda, which includes cashews, raisins, and currants. In addition to chivda, the menu features other treats like khavyache kunda, bundi che ladoo, dinkache ladoo, nachniche ladoo, and gulkand barfi. Notably, the shop has received commendations from both the Government of England and Pant Amatya of Baroda for the quality and durability of its khavyache kunda. Locals claim that the taste of this chivda has remained unchanged over the years, making it a beloved snack in Kolhapur (Source: CKA Archives).','Kolhapuri Sangeet Chivda is a well-known shop located on the main road after exiting the Kolhapur Mahalaxmi temple. Established in 1892 by Govind Vinayak Marathe, the shop earned its name because it was popular among music lovers and theatergoers in Kolhapur, who enjoyed this chivda while heading home after watching plays and movies. The term \"sangeet\" reflects the cultural significance of the shop during a time when theaters were abundant in the area. The shop\'s main attraction is its chivda, which includes cashews, raisins, and currants. In addition to chivda, the menu features other treats like khavyache kunda, bundi che ladoo, dinkache ladoo, nachniche ladoo, and gulkand barfi. Notably, the shop has received commendations from both the Government of England and Pant Amatya of Baroda for the quality and durability of its khavyache kunda. Locals claim that the taste of this chivda has remained unchanged over the years, making it a beloved snack in Kolhapur (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(16052,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/language/image-no-caption-20631dff.png','Image (no caption)','Image (no caption)',NULL),(16073,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/kolhapurs-chappal-galli-is-famous-for-handcr_KH5Rsw6.jpg','Kolhapur’s Chappal Galli is famous for handcrafted leather Kolhapuri Chappals, known for their durability, style, and heritage. Made from buffalo hides, these sandals range from ₹150 to over ₹10,000, with styles like Kapshi, Amdaar, and Shahu. Some designs include “vinchu” seeds that produce a distinct sound. The craft dates back to the 12th century and remains a key attraction for tourists and locals alike (Source: CKA Archives).','Kolhapur’s Chappal Galli is famous for handcrafted leather Kolhapuri Chappals, known for their durability, style, and heritage. Made from buffalo hides, these sandals range from ₹150 to over ₹10,000, with styles like Kapshi, Amdaar, and Shahu. Some designs include “vinchu” seeds that produce a distinct sound. The craft dates back to the 12th century and remains a key attraction for tourists and locals alike (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(16082,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/vendors-at-kapil-tirth-market-selling-fresh-_d2GRFpP.jpg','Vendors at Kapil-Tirth Market selling fresh vegetables, a regular shopping spot for residents of nearby areas  (Source: CKA Archives).','Vendors at Kapil-Tirth Market selling fresh vegetables, a regular shopping spot for residents of nearby areas  (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(16085,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/a-display-of-terracotta-and-earthenware-item_UyCYryq.jpg','A display of terracotta and earthenware items in Kumbhar Galli, a market known for traditional handmade pottery(Source: CKA Archives).','A display of terracotta and earthenware items in Kumbhar Galli, a market known for traditional handmade pottery(Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(16088,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/mahadwar-road-a-busy-street-in-kolhapur-know_DzRh08K.jpg','Mahadwar Road, a busy street in Kolhapur known for its shops and local businesses (Source: CKA Archives).','Mahadwar Road, a busy street in Kolhapur known for its shops and local businesses (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(16089,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/maharashtra-granth-bhandar-a-well-known-book_oZv8qDl.jpg','Maharashtra Granth Bhandar, a well-known bookstore on Mahadwar Road (Source: CKA Archives).','Maharashtra Granth Bhandar, a well-known bookstore on Mahadwar Road (Source: CKA Archives).',NULL),(16092,'culture/images/maharashtra/kolhapur/markets/a-vendor-cleans-and-prepares-crabs-for-sale-_IEXVUY0.jpg','A vendor cleans and prepares crabs for sale at K