 mandir is dedicated to Balaji (a form of Vishnu), and also includes shrines to other devtas. (Source: CKA Archives)','The vibrant exterior of the Balaji Mandir in Budhuda, established in 2001 following the relocation from the village’s former settlement. The mandir is dedicated to Balaji (a form of Vishnu), and also includes shrines to other devtas. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16321,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/carvings-and-murtis-of-ganesha-shesh-nag_j33VtFb.jpg','Carvings and murtis of Ganesha, Shesh Nag, and disciples of Bhagwan Shiv within the Balaji Mandir complex. (Source: CKA Archives)','Carvings and murtis of Ganesha, Shesh Nag, and disciples of Bhagwan Shiv within the Balaji Mandir complex. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16325,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/built-over-400-years-ago-the-hazrat-sura_RKiZpPO.png','Built over 400 years ago, the Hazrat Surat Shah Wali Dargah in Latur is built in a traditional Islamic style, with a large dome and numerous minarets visible across the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)','Built over 400 years ago, the Hazrat Surat Shah Wali Dargah in Latur is built in a traditional Islamic style, with a large dome and numerous minarets visible across the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16326,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/the-exterior-of-the-dargah-is-painted-in_sq6X7zr.png','The exterior of the Dargah is painted in a deep green shade, a color often associated with Islamic religious spaces.(Source: CKA Archives)','The exterior of the Dargah is painted in a deep green shade, a color often associated with Islamic religious spaces.(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16328,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/a-man-bowing-at-the-inner-shrine-of-the-_cPRpL2c.png','A man bowing at the inner shrine of the Hazrat Surat Shah Wali Dargah.(Source: CKA Archives)','A man bowing at the inner shrine of the Hazrat Surat Shah Wali Dargah.(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16329,