dow-embedded-in-the-o_7OjbQwJ.png','A small viewing window embedded in the outer wall of a structure that lies in the fort. (Source: CKA Archives)','A small viewing window embedded in the outer wall of a structure that lies in the fort. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16441,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/arched-passageway-at-udgir-fort-featurin_WTWTSki.png','Arched passageway at Udgir Fort, featuring a series of connected stone archways that create a framed perspective looking outward.(Source: CKA Archives)','Arched passageway at Udgir Fort, featuring a series of connected stone archways that create a framed perspective looking outward.(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16443,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/a-cavity-in-the-shape-of-an-eye-which-li_ADhQWLT.png','A cavity in the shape of an eye which lies in the fort. Interestingly, it is believed to have been used either as a mirror or a fountain in the olden days.(Source: CKA Archives)','A cavity in the shape of an eye which lies in the fort. Interestingly, it is believed to have been used either as a mirror or a fountain in the olden days.(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16445,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/cannon-placed-on-the-upper-level-of-udgi_8iwCizq.png','Cannon placed on the upper level of Udgir Fort, one of the remaining tofs used in the fort’s defense. (Source: CKA Archives)','Cannon placed on the upper level of Udgir Fort, one of the remaining tofs used in the fort’s defense. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16449,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/an-image-of-udaygiri-maharaj-at-the-uday_1Q1fIdB.png','An image of Udaygiri Maharaj at the Udaygiri Samadhi Mandir. Udaygiri Maharaj is locally regarded as the figure after whom Udgir town and fort are named. He is mentioned in the Osmanabad District Gazetteer (1972) in connection with the completion of the Udgir fort’s construction. (Source: CKA Archives)','An image of Udaygiri Maharaj at the Udaygiri Samadhi Mandir. Udaygiri Maharaj is locally regarded as the figure after whom Udgir town and fort are named. He is mentioned in the Osmanabad District Gazetteer (1972) in connection with the completion of the Udgir fort’s construction. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16451,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/the-mandir-complex-is-home-to-a-small-ku_3GumHCN.png','The mandir complex is home to a small kund (water tank) outside, where devotees drink jal (water) in the name of the sant, believing it to hold blessings. (Source: CKA Archives)','The mandir complex is home to a small kund (water tank) outside, where devotees drink jal (water) in the name of the sant, believing it to hold blessings. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16454,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/the-vitthal-rukmini-mandir-in-budhuda-vi_bSPXEUa.png','The Vitthal Rukmini Mandir in Budhuda village, with the current pujarin standing in the foreground.The mandir has been looked after by the same family for over two generations and continues to play an active role in the religious life of the village. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Vitthal Rukmini Mandir in Budhuda village, with the current pujarin standing in the foreground.The mandir has been looked after by the same family for over two generations and continues to play an active role in the religious life of the village. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16456,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/devta-vitthal-and-devi-rukmini-placed-in_XxwjaMF.jpg','Devta Vitthal and Devi Rukmini placed inside the inner chamber of the mandir.A photo of Sant Dnyaneshwar is also kept within the mandir, showcasing its association with the Bhakti movement and the Varkari tradition in Maharashtra. (Source: CKA Archives)','Devta Vitthal and Devi Rukmini placed inside the inner chamber of the mandir.A photo of Sant Dnyaneshwar is also kept within the mandir, showcasing its association with the Bhakti movement and the Varkari tradition in Maharashtra. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16458,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/cultural-sites/a-shivling-symbol-of-bhagwan-shiva-place_nWv3PFe.jpg','A shivling (symbol of Bhagwan Shiva) placed beneath an Audumbar tree, located outside the Datta shrine within the mandir complex. The tree and shivling serve as a secondary site of prayer, particularly for devotees of Dattatreya. (Source: CKA Archives)','A shivling (symbol of Bhagwan Shiva) placed beneath an Audumbar tree, located outside the Datta shrine within the mandir complex. The tree and shivling serve as a secondary site of prayer, particularly for devotees of Dattatreya. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(16480,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/ashtamod-chivda1-1db7220d.png','Ashtamod Chivda[1]','Ashtamod Chivda[1]','https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Se9HBjRSOLQ'),(16491,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/dink-ladoo2-c3daad9c.png','Dink Ladoo[2]','Dink Ladoo[2]','https://madhurasrecipe.com/sweets/healthy-dink-ladoo-marathi-ladoo/'),(16498,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/tandyachi-mohachi-daru3-18961eed.png','Tandyachi Mohachi Daru[3]','Tandyachi Mohachi Daru[3]','https://lokmat.news18.com/national/the-famous-moha-liquor-brand-in-the-tribal-areas-the-state-formulated-a-heritage-liquor-policy-up-mhmg-509874.html'),(16508,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/pithala-bhakri4-36a627cf.png','Pithala Bhakri[4]','Pithala Bhakri[4]','https://ministryofcurry.com/pithla/'),(16515,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/nilanga-rice5-824a09f4.png','Nilanga Rice[5]','Nilanga Rice[5]','https://in.pinterest.com/pin/824651381775897806/'),(16518,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/khoya-lassi6-92244002.png','Khoya, Lassi[6]','Khoya, Lassi[6]','https://cookpad.com/in/recipes/13552971-punjabi-khoya-lassi'),(16526,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/mandi7-12d8703a.png','Mandi[7]','Mandi[7]','https://www.munatycooking.com/yemeni-chicken-mandi/'),(16529,'culture/images/maharashtra/latur/food/shushila8-d84d2baf.png',