ashtra/mumbai/architecture/common-passageway-connecting-each-room-th_77Za9a5.jpg','Common passageway connecting each room. The rooms have a wooden door with a window above the door having mild metal grills for ventilation. Source: CKA Archives','Common passageway connecting each room. The rooms have a wooden door with a window above the door having mild metal grills for ventilation. Source: CKA Archives',''),(17787,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai/architecture/brick-red-tiled-passageway-that-connects-_b2yLguG.jpg','Brick-red tiled passageway that connects each room. Notice the upper clerestory windows that create a funnel effect for air circulation. Source: CKA Archives','Brick-red tiled passageway that connects each room. Notice the upper clerestory windows that create a funnel effect for air circulation. Source: CKA Archives',''),(17789,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai/architecture/the-building-has-an-interesting-and-vibra_OQZllwQ.jpg','The building has an interesting and vibrant color combination with a neutral base tone and bright brick-red balconies. The lower floor has large windows with a mild metal grill and glass panes. Source: CKA Archives','The building has an interesting and vibrant color combination with a neutral base tone and bright brick-red balconies. The lower floor has large windows with a mild metal grill and glass panes. Source: CKA Archives',''),(17791,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai/architecture/modular-balconies-attached-to-each-room-i_ovLfYun.jpg','Modular balconies attached to each room in the hostel in a brick-red color. Source: CKA Archives','Modular balconies attached to each room in the hostel in a brick-red color. Source: CKA Archives',''),(17832,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-vaulted-roof-over-the-nave-a_YYCZHIf.png','The vaulted roof over the nave and preserved stambhas in Cave No. 3 reflect early chaitya hall architecture at Kanheri.[1]','The vaulted roof over the nave and preserved stambhas in C