:Mount_Mary_Church,_Bandra'),(17848,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/at-mount-mary-church-a-central-n_VzHotqa.png','At Mount Mary Church, a central nave and cruciform plan lead to the statue of the Virgin Mary.[7]','At Mount Mary Church, a central nave and cruciform plan lead to the statue of the Virgin Mary.[7]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TheCapital_Image2.jpg'),(17852,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-capitals-west-facade-feature_Xn6eS16.png','The Capital’s west façade features a stepped glazed design with cantilevered floors for self-shading, while the east sky lobby showcases an egg-shaped structure.[8]','The Capital’s west façade features a stepped glazed design with cantilevered floors for self-shading, while the east sky lobby showcases an egg-shaped structure.[8]',''),(17856,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-paradoxical-character-of-mum_cEip7Uq.jpg','The paradoxical character of Mumbai - where the small spaces are giving way to towering buildings. (Source: CKA Archives)','The paradoxical character of Mumbai - where the small spaces are giving way to towering buildings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17862,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-street-view-of-a-residential-s_XzK8TAB.jpg','A street view of a residential structure, estimated by locals to be over 100 years old, located just outside Mulund Station (West), nestled within a narrow bylane off Mahatma Gandhi Road. The building’s façade, partially obscured by market stalls. (Source: CKA Archives)','A street view of a residential structure, estimated by locals to be over 100 years old, located just outside Mulund Station (West), nestled within a narrow bylane off Mahatma Gandhi Road. The building’s façade, partially obscured by market stalls. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17864,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-view-of-an-old-residence-near-_HKuyUA3.jpg','A view of an old residence near Mulund Station (W), partially obscured by market activity. The structure sits within a planned grid of lanes, typical of early 20th-century suburban layouts. (Source: CKA Archives)','A view of an old residence near Mulund Station (W), partially obscured by market activity. The structure sits within a planned grid of lanes, typical of early 20th-century suburban layouts. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17868,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/street-facing-view-of-the-reside_3sgHnuq.jpg','Street-facing view of the residence, partially hidden behind a market stall near Mulund Station (W), now awaiting redevelopment. (Source: CKA Archives)','Street-facing view of the residence, partially hidden behind a market stall near Mulund Station (W), now awaiting redevelopment. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17870,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-ground-floor-consists-of-sev_CfL4QNa.jpg','The ground floor consists of several independent doors and windows, likely indicating separate dwelling units. Many architectural features of a bygone era can be seen here,  for instance here, one can see the window vents that retain original glass within timber frames.(Source: CKA Archives)','The ground floor consists of several independent doors and windows, likely indicating separate dwelling units. Many architectural features of a bygone era can be seen here,  for instance here, one can see the window vents that retain original glass within timber frames.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17871,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/interior-corner-of-a-quarter-wit_80eoRxX.jpg','Interior corner of a quarter within the residence which possibly hints at its typology as a single dwelling unit. A masonry base structure can be seen within the room. Its purpose remains unknown, but it may have functioned as a base for storage or as a spatial division. It is the only structural element within the room apart from the enclosing walls.. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior corner of a quarter within the residence which possibly hints at its typology as a single dwelling unit. A masonry base structure can be seen within the room. Its purpose remains unknown, but it may have functioned as a base for storage or as a spatial division. It is the only structural element within the room apart from the enclosing walls.. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17873,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/closeup-of-the-iron-railings-wit_frAL3Oy.jpg','Closeup of the Iron railings with wooden screening panels below. (Source: CKA Archives)','Closeup of the Iron railings with wooden screening panels below. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17875,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/decorative-elements-and-iron-ven_slPR7bE.jpg','Decorative elements and iron vents reflect a past attention to symmetry and ventilation. Notice the fading patterns that are painted on the door.  (Source: CKA Archives)','Decorative elements and iron vents reflect a past attention to symmetry and ventilation. Notice the fading patterns that are painted on the door.  (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17877,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/view-of-the-wooden-staircase-tha_pYSvEdj.jpg','View of the wooden staircase that connects both floors; exposed beam structure supports the upper level.(Source: CKA Archives)','View of the wooden staircase that connects both floors; exposed beam structure supports the upper level.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17879,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-plinth-and-entrance-flooring_TQ7aMd2.jpg','The plinth and entrance flooring are constructed from cut stone blocks, forming the structural base of the building. (Source: CKA Archives)','The plinth and entrance flooring are constructed from cut stone blocks, forming the structural base of the building. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17880,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-traditional-well-bawda-located_GsuUptx.jpg','A traditional well (bawda) located in the exterior space of the house, once used for household water supply. (Source: CKA Archives)','A traditional well (bawda) located in the exterior space of the house, once used for household water supply. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17882,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/wooden-triangular-motif-below-th_m9aTJty.jpg','Wooden triangular motif below the sloping roof, possibly symbolic. This feature recurs in other homes nearby. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden triangular motif below the sloping roof, possibly symbolic. This feature recurs in other homes nearby. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17884,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-curved-brick-lintel-above-a-wi_ZWjEipG.jpg','A curved brick lintel above a window, with a decorative trim where the wall meets the opening. Notably, similar arches and trims can be seen on other houses in the area, suggesting a pattern of construction that balanced structural need with a measured visual rhythm.(Source: CKA Archives)','A curved brick lintel above a window, with a decorative trim where the wall meets the opening. Notably, similar arches and trims can be seen on other houses in the area, suggesting a pattern of construction that balanced structural need with a measured visual rhythm.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17888,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/only-three-of-the-original-twelv_85TfXcn.jpg','Only three of the original twelve curved-roof structures remain today, set tightly along a narrow bylane near Ashok Nagar, Mulund, Mumbai Suburban. (Source: CKA Archives)','Only three of the original twelve curved-roof structures remain today, set tightly along a narrow bylane near Ashok Nagar, Mulund, Mumbai Suburban. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17890,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/interior-spaces-flow-into-each-o_5vc5bOt.jpg','Interior spaces flow into each other, with corrugated roofing forming a continuous curved shell overhead, eliminating the need for a separate truss or rafter system. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior spaces flow into each other, with corrugated roofing forming a continuous curved shell overhead, eliminating the need for a separate truss or rafter system. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17892,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-middle-house-has-been-raised_pD9OD5Y.jpg','The middle house has been raised, possibly during renovation, aligning it directly with the street level. (Source: CKA Archives)','The middle house has been raised, possibly during renovation, aligning it directly with the street level. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17896,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-glimpse-at-the-original-layout_qPf2NjB.jpg','A glimpse at the original layout of block houses; houses were arranged in linear blocks, separated by narrow lanes. Only a few remain today. (Source: CKA Archives)','A glimpse at the original layout of block houses; houses were arranged in linear blocks, separated by narrow lanes. Only a few remain today. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17898,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/an-exterior-view-of-the-original_IqOPpu5.jpg','An exterior view of the original wooden windows with double shutters, featuring upper ventilation slots at a downtrodden block house at Mulund Colony. (Source: CKA Archives)','An exterior view of the original wooden windows with double shutters, featuring upper ventilation slots at a downtrodden block house at Mulund Colony. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17900,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/44a931b782df4d2b8428f159d9736c15_KenokoH.jpg','','',''),(17902,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/exposed-beams-supporting-corruga_4vug7eL.jpg','Exposed beams supporting corrugated metal sheets, roofs had no false ceilings, keeping interiors open and ventilated. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exposed beams supporting corrugated metal sheets, roofs had no false ceilings, keeping interiors open and ventilated. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17904,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/exterior-view-of-the-pitched-roo_MRTmjYd.jpg','Exterior view of the pitched roofing system made from corrugated metal sheets, aligned with the slope of the land. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior view of the pitched roofing system made from corrugated metal sheets, aligned with the slope of the land. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17905,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-contrast-between-the-older-a_dH11LPM.jpg','The contrast between the older and newer corrugated sheets; one can see that the older corrugated roofing featured long flat sections between ridges, a design now replaced by continuous wave patterns. (Source: CKA Archives)','The contrast between the older and newer corrugated sheets; one can see that the older corrugated roofing featured long flat sections between ridges, a design now replaced by continuous wave patterns. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17907,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-comparison-of-single-and-doubl_BAQRUTd.jpg','A comparison of single and double roofing systems. Double roofs, added later, became indicators of economic standing at one point of time for the residents of this colony. (Source: CKA Archives)','A comparison of single and double roofing systems. Double roofs, added later, became indicators of economic standing at one point of time for the residents of this colony. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17909,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/stone-flooring-known-as-shahabad_CUU0fbc.jpg','Stone flooring known as shahabad ladi, sourced from Karnataka, commonly used inside the block houses. (Source: CKA Archives)','Stone flooring known as shahabad ladi, sourced from Karnataka, commonly used inside the block houses. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17915,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-building-is-situated-on-a-qu_3qcsjAf.jpg','The building is situated on a quiet residential lane in Cypress, Mulund (W), with a consistent low-rise skyline. (Source: CKA Archives)','The building is situated on a quiet residential lane in Cypress, Mulund (W), with a consistent low-rise skyline. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17917,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/staircases-are-bordered-by-a-wal_bvK9CjD.jpg','Staircases are bordered by a wall with patterned openings that allow for light and airflow. (Source: CKA Archives)','Staircases are bordered by a wall with patterned openings that allow for light and airflow. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17919,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/concrete-chajjas-above-windows-p_Uorv1pC.jpg','Concrete chajjas above windows provide shade and rhythmic repetition across the facade. (Source: CKA Archives)','Concrete chajjas above windows provide shade and rhythmic repetition across the facade. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17921,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/while-the-windows-have-been-reno_8McPkhy.jpg','While the windows have been renovated, they originally featured wooden double panels with ventilation slots above such as the one that remains here. This window design was a common feature in buildings of this era. (Source: CKA Archives)','While the windows have been renovated, they originally featured wooden double panels with ventilation slots above such as the one that remains here. This window design was a common feature in buildings of this era. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17923,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-main-entrance-has-separate-p_Ttuf5Kg.jpg','The main entrance has separate pedestrian and vehicle gates, both designed with simple geometric patterns. (Source: CKA Archives)','The main entrance has separate pedestrian and vehicle gates, both designed with simple geometric patterns. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17924,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/a-concrete-and-granite-bench-sta_vWtLgGF.jpg','A concrete and granite bench stands near the gate, offering a small resting space. A fixed bench near the entrance is used by residents for casual seating.(Source: CKA Archives)','A concrete and granite bench stands near the gate, offering a small resting space. A fixed bench near the entrance is used by residents for casual seating.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17926,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-conjoined-building-is-manage_jLadLdC.jpg','The conjoined building is managed independently under a different housing society. (Source: CKA Archives)','The conjoined building is managed independently under a different housing society. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17928,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/independent-pump-houses-serve-th_q7LDB54.jpg','Independent pump houses serve the two buildings, indicating infrastructural separation.(Source: CKA Archives)','Independent pump houses serve the two buildings, indicating infrastructural separation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17930,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/trees-planted-by-residents-now-l_vyZrhIz.jpg','Trees planted by residents now line the compound’s edges in the absence of a formal garden.(Source: CKA Archives)','Trees planted by residents now line the compound’s edges in the absence of a formal garden.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17932,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/an-incomplete-staircase-at-the-r_cgYblWo.jpg','An incomplete staircase at the rear ends at a sealed, unused basement area. (Source: CKA Archives)','An incomplete staircase at the rear ends at a sealed, unused basement area. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17937,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-towers-height-stands-in-cont_FpajV34.jpg','The tower\'s height stands in contrast to the sloping terrain and low-rise surroundings of Mulund Colony, marking a shift in the area\'s built form. (Source: CKA Archives)','The tower\'s height stands in contrast to the sloping terrain and low-rise surroundings of Mulund Colony, marking a shift in the area\'s built form. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17939,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/from-above-the-buildings-footpri_vEhM10Y.jpg','From above, the building’s footprint follows the linear plan typical of apartment towers, but its facade introduces historical detailing. (Source: Vignesh Jaiswal)','From above, the building’s footprint follows the linear plan typical of apartment towers, but its facade introduces historical detailing. (Source: Vignesh Jaiswal)',''),(17941,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/the-upper-facade-features-triang_2bE6kRG.jpg','The upper facade features triangular and broken segmental pediments, a common device in classical and neo-classical buildings to mark entrances or transitions. (Source: CKA Archives)','The upper facade features triangular and broken segmental pediments, a common device in classical and neo-classical buildings to mark entrances or transitions. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17942,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/corinthian-columns-with-molded-c_0FayWZn.jpg','Corinthian columns with molded capitals are used to frame window bays and balconies, contrasting with the otherwise modern materials.(Source: CKA Archives)','Corinthian columns with molded capitals are used to frame window bays and balconies, contrasting with the otherwise modern materials.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17943,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/geometric-balustrades-and-decora_dPCuXix.jpg','Geometric balustrades and decorative moldings introduce regularity and detail to the structure’s vertical elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)','Geometric balustrades and decorative moldings introduce regularity and detail to the structure’s vertical elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17945,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/ornamental-patterns-at-the-entra_uSwjWWO.jpg','Ornamental patterns at the entrance reflect the formal design language used throughout the building.(Source: CKA Archives)','Ornamental patterns at the entrance reflect the formal design language used throughout the building.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17946,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/architecture/shops-integrated-at-the-base-of-_9PL7U3k.jpg','Shops integrated at the base of the tower reflect a growing trend in Mulund, where residential buildings incorporate commercial units as part of mixed-use development. (Source: CKA Archives)','Shops integrated at the base of the tower reflect a growing trend in Mulund, where residential buildings incorporate commercial units as part of mixed-use development. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(17968,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/artforms/mehboob-studios-was-one-of-the-filmi_4jzwRLg.png','Mehboob Studios was one of the filming locations for this iconic film, which became India’s first official nominee for the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film.[1]','Mehboob Studios was one of the filming locations for this iconic film, which became India’s first official nominee for the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film.[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mother_India'),(17970,'culture/images/maharashtra/mumbai-suburban/artforms/established-in-1977-by-the-maharasht_ooteZWw.png','Established in 1977 by the Maharashtra government in Goregaon, Film City provided the space and infrastructure needed for large-scale film and television production in Mumbai’s expanding suburbs.[2]','Established in 1977 by the Maharashtra government in Goregaon, Film City provided the space and infrastructure needed for large-scale film and television production in Mumbai’s expanding suburbs.[2]','https://mumbaitourism.co.in/film-city-mumba