arashtra%29'),(19459,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/cultural-sites/exhibits-at-the-coin-museum-near-anjane_2Fq98Ze.png','Exhibits at the Coin Museum near Anjaneri, along the Nashik-Trimbakeshwar road, showcase historical minting techniques and rare Indian coins.[2]','Exhibits at the Coin Museum near Anjaneri, along the Nashik-Trimbakeshwar road, showcase historical minting techniques and rare Indian coins.[2]','https://www.trawell.in/maharashtra/nashik/coin-museum'),(19462,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/cultural-sites/dhodap-fort-located-near-chandwad-in-na_7qOLPsV.png','Dhodap Fort, located near Chandwad in Nashik district, features rock-cut chambers, twin gateways, and a summit mazar, all perched nearly 5,000 ft. high.[3]','Dhodap Fort, located near Chandwad in Nashik district, features rock-cut chambers, twin gateways, and a summit mazar, all perched nearly 5,000 ft. high.[3]','https://www.mumbaitrekkers.com/event-page/dhodap'),(19467,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/cultural-sites/gangapur-dam-located-on-river-godavari-_crL3po9.png','Gangapur Dam, located on River Godavari in Nashik district was constructed post-1949.[4]','Gangapur Dam, located on River Godavari in Nashik district was constructed post-1949.[4]','https://www.deccanherald.com/india/gangapur-dam-in-nashik-97-full-757571.html'),(19470,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/cultural-sites/harihar-fort-located-in-the-trimbakeshw_hteMpa3.png','Harihar Fort, located in the Trimbakeshwar mountain in Nashik district is a hill fort featuring steep rock-cut steps, a Mandir, and views of the Trimbakeshwar region.[5]','Harihar Fort, located in the Trimbakeshwar mountain in Nashik district is a hill fort featuring steep rock-cut steps, a Mandir, and views of the Trimbakeshwar region.[5]','https://www.goldentriangletour.com/en/tourist-attractions/india/maharashtra/nashik/harihar-fort-trek.html'),(19477,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/cultural-sites/kalaram-mandir-located-in-panchavati-na_VzD7O5Y.png','