rashtra/nashik/stories/view-of-the-trimbakeshwar-jyotirling-mandir5-dc9b5419.png','View of the Trimbakeshwar Jyotirling Mandir[5]','View of the Trimbakeshwar Jyotirling Mandir[5]','https://www.trimbakeshwartrust.com/'),(19743,'culture/images/maharashtra/nashik/stories/people-taking-a-holy-dip-at-the-kushavart-tirt_GSTFbR6.png','People taking a holy dip at the Kushavart Tirth, Trimbakeshwar[6]','People taking a holy dip at the Kushavart Tirth, Trimbakeshwar[6]','https://nashik.gov.in/tourist-place/kushavart-tirtha-trimbakeshwar/'),(19750,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/vasai-fort-in-palghar-showcases-indo-por_rOWxmhF.png','Vasai Fort in Palghar showcases Indo-Portuguese military architecture with stone bastions and arches.[1]','Vasai Fort in Palghar showcases Indo-Portuguese military architecture with stone bastions and arches.[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Vasai_Fort'),(19752,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/detail-of-a-carved-stone-facade-at-vasai_dKoDnAQ.png','Detail of a carved stone façade at Vasai Fort, showcasing the Indo-Portuguese architectural style with Corinthian columns and ornamental motifs.[2]','Detail of a carved stone façade at Vasai Fort, showcasing the Indo-Portuguese architectural style with Corinthian columns and ornamental motifs.[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:..._Corinthian_pillars_and_intricate_designs_(50348080608).jpg'),(19756,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/exterior-view-of-the-holy-spirit-church-_SbCk3Lo.jpg','Exterior view of the Holy Spirit Church at Nandakhal, built by the Portuguese in 1573, featuring a plain facade typical of early colonial churches. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior view of the Holy Spirit Church at Nandakhal, built by the Portuguese in 1573, featuring a plain facade typical of early colonial churches. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19760,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/exterior-view-of-jai-vilas-palace-in-jaw_II5N7RI.png','Exterior view of Jai Vilas Palace in Jawhar, an early 20th-century structure blending Rajput and Gujarati architectural elements.[3]','Exterior view of Jai Vilas Palace in Jawhar, an early 20th-century structure blending Rajput and Gujarati architectural elements.[3]','https://nashiktourism.in/tourist-places/jai-vilas-palace-jawhar/'),(19766,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/street-view-of-the-structure-along-killa_IIIAiQV.jpg','Street view of the structure along Killa Road, with visible shopfronts and residential access above. (Source: CKA Archives)','Street view of the structure along Killa Road, with visible shopfronts and residential access above. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19768,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/street-view-of-dattatreya-niwas-on-killa_LHw6IIV.jpg','Street view of Dattatreya Niwas on Killa Road. Shops occupy the ground floor, with residences above. (Source: CKA Archives)','Street view of Dattatreya Niwas on Killa Road. Shops occupy the ground floor, with residences above. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19770,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/wooden-door-with-a-grill-for-ventilation_iR9kMNc.jpg','Wooden door with a grill for ventilation at the top. A window can also be seen to the right of the entrance door. This kind of a structural setup is common in residential quarters. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden door with a grill for ventilation at the top. A window can also be seen to the right of the entrance door. This kind of a structural setup is common in residential quarters. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19772,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/wooden-door-with-intricate-grill-designs_Lpz71Bo.jpg','Wooden door with intricate grill designs attached at the entrance. This appears to be the main entrance to a big shop in the complex. Note the contrast in detailing between floors, and the consistency within each level. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden door with intricate grill designs attached at the entrance. This appears to be the main entrance to a big shop in the complex. Note the contrast in detailing between floors, and the consistency within each level. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19774,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/internal-railing-along-the-staircase-wit_11hRlZu.jpg','Internal railing along the staircase with a yellow swastika design, a symbol in Hinduism which is often associated with good fortune. (Source: CKA Archives)','Internal railing along the staircase with a yellow swastika design, a symbol in Hinduism which is often associated with good fortune. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19775,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/exterior-railing-along-the-upper-corrido_MSeOdkO.jpg','Exterior railing along the upper corridor, finished in a gold tone. Likely more decorative in function, it adds visual contrast to the building’s otherwise muted material palette. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior railing along the upper corridor, finished in a gold tone. Likely more decorative in function, it adds visual contrast to the building’s otherwise muted material palette. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19777,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/one-of-the-rooms-of-the-complex-where-pe_XiBrWJX.jpg','One of the rooms of the complex where people lived. One notices the wooden structures, along with the rectangular layout of the house which is observed in Chawl- style buildings. Interestingly, the roofing here is made up of metal sheets. (Source: CKA Archives)','One of the rooms of the complex where people lived. One notices the wooden structures, along with the rectangular layout of the house which is observed in Chawl- style buildings. Interestingly, the roofing here is made up of metal sheets. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19778,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/exit-corridor-of-the-building-facing-eas_cMCHgA0.jpg','Exit corridor of the building, facing east as per Vastu Shastra principles. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exit corridor of the building, facing east as per Vastu Shastra principles. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19781,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/street-view-of-the-house-the-structure-a_0LlH6rL.jpg','Street view of the house. The structure appears abandoned but is still in use. (Source: CKA Archives)','Street view of the house. The structure appears abandoned but is still in use. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19782,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/the-weathered-two-storey-home-in-palghar_tpFDGa7.jpg','The weathered two-storey home in Palghar district. In many ways, the structure blends wada-style and colonial-era influences with local building traditions, evident in its plastered masonry walls, exposed wooden rafters, and pitched roof with extended eaves. Wooden shutters frame the windows, some intact, others worn by time. (Source: CKA Archives)','The weathered two-storey home in Palghar district. In many ways, the structure blends wada-style and colonial-era influences with local building traditions, evident in its plastered masonry walls, exposed wooden rafters, and pitched roof with extended eaves. Wooden shutters frame the windows, some intact, others worn by time. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19784,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/the-entrance-of-the-house-it-faces-north_19IrFC4.jpg','The entrance of the house, it faces north and the entrance of the property faces west. (Source: CKA Archives)','The entrance of the house, it faces north and the entrance of the property faces west. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19785,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/close-up-of-the-entrance-doors-showing-s_rhd58dp.jpg','Close-up of the entrance doors showing signs of age and everyday use. The wooden double-leaf doors are set within a plastered wall, with fading paint, weathered surfaces, and small repairs visible across the frame. (Source: CKA Archives)','Close-up of the entrance doors showing signs of age and everyday use. The wooden double-leaf doors are set within a plastered wall, with fading paint, weathered surfaces, and small repairs visible across the frame. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19786,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/stairs-to-the-entrance-of-the-house-the-_s9fqZke.jpg','Stairs to the entrance of the house. The curved balustrade (sidewalls of the staircase) echoes the gentle flair of late colonial bungalow forms. (Source: CKA Archives)','Stairs to the entrance of the house. The curved balustrade (sidewalls of the staircase) echoes the gentle flair of late colonial bungalow forms. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19788,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/the-original-roof-structurewhich-was-bui_rCsgE4x.jpg','The original roof structure,which was built using wood. (Source: CKA Archives)','The original roof structure,which was built using wood. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19790,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/abroken-pillar-at-the-entrance-of-the-ho_rc7MF7A.jpg','Abroken pillar at the entrance of the home. Remarkably, its proportions and style loosely echo the columns found in traditional wada houses. (Source: CKA Archives)','Abroken pillar at the entrance of the home. Remarkably, its proportions and style loosely echo the columns found in traditional wada houses. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19792,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/notably-on-one-of-the-pillars-one-notice_0ifm2js.jpg','Notably, on one of the pillars, one notices a board stating the property details. This board was put up by the Old Gram Panchayat. (Source: CKA Archives)','Notably, on one of the pillars, one notices a board stating the property details. This board was put up by the Old Gram Panchayat. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19794,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/construction-material-kept-at-the-back-o_NdLcmkO.jpg','Construction material kept at the back of the house. Some plants can still be seen, eventhoughthe garden was demolished. (Source: CKA Archives)','Construction material kept at the back of the house. Some plants can still be seen, eventhoughthe garden was demolished. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19795,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/once-a-well-maintained-space-this-garden_rt98aD7.jpg','Once a well-maintained space, this garden now lies in disarray, with wild growth taking over its boundaries. (Source: CKA Archives)','Once a well-maintained space, this garden now lies in disarray, with wild growth taking over its boundaries. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19798,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/front-view-of-the-three-storey-building-_5LRvnbO.jpg','Front view of the three-storey building with parking space in the foreground. The structure reflects typical residential construction from the 1980s.(Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the three-storey building with parking space in the foreground. The structure reflects typical residential construction from the 1980s.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19800,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/main-gate-of-the-rajnigandha-building-wh_VpsrNJE.jpg','Main gate of the Rajnigandha building, which is part of the larger apartment complex. A white post box is attached to the gate, alongside a sign reminding residents to close the door. (Source: CKA Archives)','Main gate of the Rajnigandha building, which is part of the larger apartment complex. A white post box is attached to the gate, alongside a sign reminding residents to close the door. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19802,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/architecture/side-view-of-the-building-variations-in-_dbSYkzw.jpg','Side view of the building. Variations in window sizes and types are visible, highlighting functional adjustments within a standard layout.(Source: CKA Archives)','Side view of the building. Variations in window sizes and types are visible, highlighting functional adjustments within a standard layout.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(19815,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/an-older-member-of-the-warli-community-paint_NyJ2zS0.jpg','An older member of the Warli community painting traditional Warli patterns.[1]','An older member of the Warli community painting traditional Warli patterns.[1]','https://merikalamurti.medium.com/warli-painting-art-made-from-geometry-9257d9570a2e'),(19819,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/participants-perform-tarpa-dance-during-an-e_om25wFJ.png','Participants perform Tarpa dance during an event.[2]','Participants perform Tarpa dance during an event.[2]','https://www.herzindagi.com/society-culture/tarpa-dance-maharashtra-palghar-tribal-dance-meaning-article-247863'),(19823,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/dahanu-festival3-f2c61813.png','Dahanu Festival[3]','Dahanu Festival[3]','https://www.hotelierindia.com/events/dahanu-festival-2022-celebrates-sustainable-tourism'),(19827,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/fabric-jewelry-produced-by-local-artisans-at_yKsCMpE.jpg','Fabric jewelry produced by local artisans at Paduka Artisans.[4]','Fabric jewelry produced by local artisans at Paduka Artisans.[4]','https://www.justdial.com/jdmart/Thane/Padukas-Artisans-Village-Nimboli-Tal-Wada-Near-Hanuman-Mandir-Kelthan/022PXX22-XX22-210803135542-P6M6_BZDET/catalogue/products'),(19832,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/jivya-soma-mashe5-bcf7f12b.jpg','Jivya Soma Mashe[5]','Jivya Soma Mashe[5]','https://www.modestiperdriolle.com/jivya-soma-mashe'),(19836,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/artforms/shanta-gokhale6-ac873f79.png','Shanta Gokhale[6]','Shanta Gokhale[6]','https://speakingtigerbooks.com/authors-name/shanta-gokhale/'),(19852,'culture/images/maharashtra/palghar/cultural-sites/the-agashi-maha-tirtha-in-virar-is-an-_MDITIeH.png','The Agashi Maha Tirtha in Virar is an intricately carved marble structure.[1]','The Agashi Maha Tirtha in Virar is an intricately carved marble structure.[1]','https://www.jainmandir.o