shed over 250 years ago, remains a central religious and social institution for the Twashta Kasar community. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Kalika Devi Mandir of Kasba Peth, established over 250 years ago, remains a central religious and social institution for the Twashta Kasar community. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20601,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/current-board-members-of-the-kalika-devi-mandir_ZxbzSZA.jpg','Current board members of the Kalika Devi Mandir, elected by the community to oversee religious, cultural, and administrative matters. (Source: CKA Archives)','Current board members of the Kalika Devi Mandir, elected by the community to oversee religious, cultural, and administrative matters. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20603,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/silver-jewellery-and-decorative-work-adorning-t_RqKlIIu.jpg','Silver jewellery and decorative work adorning the Kalika Devi murti, created using nakshikam engraving techniques passed down within the community. (Source: CKA Archives)','Silver jewellery and decorative work adorning the Kalika Devi murti, created using nakshikam engraving techniques passed down within the community. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20604,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/brass-daankoti-donation-box-placed-inside-the-k_Bp47cgZ.jpg','Brass daankoti (donation box) placed inside the Kalika Devi Mandir, made by community artisans. (Source: CKA Archives)','Brass daankoti (donation box) placed inside the Kalika Devi Mandir, made by community artisans. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20606,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/the-temporary-mandap-erected-during-ganesh-chat_zbad6ml.jpg','The temporary mandap erected during Ganesh Chaturthi, built annually behind Kalika Devi Mandir and used as a site for craft display and collective worship. (Source: CKA Archives)','The temporary mandap erected during Ganesh Chaturthi, built annually behind Kalika Devi Mandir and used as a site for craft display and collective worship. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20608,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/exterior-of-the-community-runvachanalaya-a-publ_MEsocAW.jpg','Exterior of the community-runvachanalaya, a public library established around 50 years ago and still managed voluntarily by local residents. (Source: CKA Archives)','Exterior of the community-runvachanalaya, a public library established around 50 years ago and still managed voluntarily by local residents. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20609,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/interior-view-of-the-vachanalaya-containing-boo_Yvlw0sm.jpg','Interior view of the vachanalaya, containing books on history, social reform, and literature, preserving intellectual heritage alongside material craft. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior view of the vachanalaya, containing books on history, social reform, and literature, preserving intellectual heritage alongside material craft. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20611,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/opening-board-of-the-anandi-sansar-exhibit-cura_jaQpchK.jpg','Opening board of the Anandi Sansar exhibit, curated by Girish Potphode to document and present the lived craft traditions of the Twashta Kasar community. (Source: CKA Archives)','Opening board of the Anandi Sansar exhibit, curated by Girish Potphode to document and present the lived craft traditions of the Twashta Kasar community. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20612,'culture/images/maharashtra/pune/artforms/miniature-figurines-representing-the-twelve-her_LdVtE7s.jpg','Miniature figurines representing the twelve hereditary occupations under the Bara Balutedar system, illustrating the historical division of labour in traditional Maharashtrian society at the exhibit. (Source: CKA Archives)','Miniature figurines representing the twelve hereditary occupations under the Bara Balutedar system, illustrating the historical division of labour in traditional Maharashtrian society at the exhibit. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(20613,'