r Mandir, believed to have been built in the Vedic period, follows the Hemadpanthi architectural site.[1]','Harihareshwar Mandir, believed to have been built in the Vedic period, follows the Hemadpanthi architectural site.[1]','https://www.tourmyindia.com/states/maharashtra/harihareshwar-temple-raigad.html'),(20712,'culture/images/maharashtra/raigad/architecture/elephanta-caves-carved-from-basalt-rock-o_eZKXYln.png','Elephanta Caves carved from basalt rock on Gharapuri Island, showcasing rock-cut architecture.[2]','Elephanta Caves carved from basalt rock on Gharapuri Island, showcasing rock-cut architecture.[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Elephanta_Caves'),(20714,'culture/images/maharashtra/raigad/architecture/interior-of-cave-1-featuring-a-central-ha_C05Z3gi.png','Interior of Cave 1, featuring a central hall and Shivling in the garbhagriha.[3]','Interior of Cave 1, featuring a central hall and Shivling in the garbhagriha.[3]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elephanta_Cave_1_F1.jpg'),(20718,'culture/images/maharashtra/raigad/architecture/raigad-fort-built-in-hill-fort-style-show_qVVNihV.png','Raigad Fort, built in hill fort style, showcasing its seventeenth-century architectural features.[4]','Raigad Fort, built in hill fort style, showcasing its seventeenth-century architectural features.[4]','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Nagarkhana%2C_Raigad_Fort%2C_India.jpg/500px-Nagarkhana%2C_Raigad_Fort%2C_India.jpg'),(20720,'culture/images/maharashtra/raigad/architecture/the-forts-maha-darwaja-is-flanked-by-20-m_XbKofXa.png','The fort’s Maha Darwaja is flanked by 20-metre-tall bastions, showcasing its strategic design.[5]','The fort’s Maha Darwaja is flanked by 20-metre-tall bastions, showcasing its strategic design.[5]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahadarwaja_rajgad.jpg'),(20724,'culture/images/maharashtra/raigad/architecture/murud-janjira-fort-an-island-water-fort-f_UH99qHI.png','Murud Janjira Fort: an isl