ULL),(21565,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/preparation-of-vade-battersource-cka-archives-5c3beeb5.jpg','Preparation of Vade batter(Source: CKA Archives)','Preparation of Vade batter(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21566,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/vades-getting-friedsource-cka-archives-55e14f6c.jpg','Vades getting fried(Source: CKA Archives)','Vades getting fried(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21568,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/jackfruit-seedssource-cka-archives-cdba7ec2.jpg','Jackfruit Seeds(Source: CKA Archives)','Jackfruit Seeds(Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21571,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/a-board-in-adarsh-upahar-gruh-source-cka-archi_IRTSNGy.jpg','A board in Adarsh Upahar Gruh (Source: CKA Archives)','A board in Adarsh Upahar Gruh (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21575,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/a-board-in-adarsh-upahar-gruh-source-cka-archi_6IOOsIB.jpg','A board in Adarsh Upahar Gruh (Source: CKA Archives)','A board in Adarsh Upahar Gruh (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21578,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/the-interior-of-pritam-ice-cream-parlour-sourc_f1ESYO9.jpg','The interior of Pritam Ice Cream Parlour (Source: CKA Archives)','The interior of Pritam Ice Cream Parlour (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21579,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/food/the-exterior-of-pritam-ice-cream-parlour-sourc_m9uA5bO.jpg','The exterior of Pritam Ice Cream Parlour (Source: CKA Archives)','The exterior of Pritam Ice Cream Parlour (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21608,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/language/title-cards-of-popular-tv-serials-that-con_X0LvseV.png','Title cards of popular TV serials that contained plot or characters speaking in Malwani. Gaav Gaata Gazali (Zee Marathi), a light-hearted TV serial that showcases village life, folk traditions, and daily humor, all in rich Malwani speech.[1]','Title cards of popular TV serials that contained plot or characters speaking in Malwani. Gaav Gaata Gazali (Zee Marathi), a light-hearted TV serial that showcases village life, folk traditions, and daily humor, all in rich Malwani speech.[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaav_Gata_Gajali'),(21609,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/language/ratris-khel-chale-transl-the-game-runs-at-_i01Zkxb.png','Ratris Khel Chale (transl. The Game Runs at Night) is a Marathi-Malwani supernatural thriller television series that premiered on Zee Marathi on 22 February 2016. Set in Sawantwadi, the story follows the Naik family, who speak in Malwani and encounter a series of mysterious and unexplainable events.[2]','Ratris Khel Chale (transl. The Game Runs at Night) is a Marathi-Malwani supernatural thriller television series that premiered on Zee Marathi on 22 February 2016. Set in Sawantwadi, the story follows the Naik family, who speak in Malwani and encounter a series of mysterious and unexplainable events.[2]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratris_Khel_Chale'),(21646,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/markets/chipluns-main-market-stretches-along-the-ce_8A3TZw3.jpg','Chiplun’s Main Market stretches along the central road, with open-air stalls and built-in shops offering everything from vegetables and fish to clothing and medical supplies. (Source: CKA Archives)','Chiplun’s Main Market stretches along the central road, with open-air stalls and built-in shops offering everything from vegetables and fish to clothing and medical supplies. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21650,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/markets/chipluns-fish-market-is-run-mainly-by-women_CSMDQWy.jpg','Chiplun’s fish market is run mainly by women from fishing communities. (Source: CKA Archives)','Chiplun’s fish market is run mainly by women from fishing communities. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21653,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/markets/chipluns-vegetable-market-has-fresh-produce_wRLrGhq.jpg','Chiplun’s vegetable market has fresh produce stalls, run by local farmers and nearby traders. (Source: CKA Archives)','Chiplun’s vegetable market has fresh produce stalls, run by local farmers and nearby traders. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21656,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/markets/friday-market-shukravar-bazaar-in-pirlote-i_L9lGqcE.jpg','Friday Market (Shukravar Bazaar) in Pirlote is a weekly open-air market with sections for vegetables, fruits, dry fish, hardware, clothes, and toast-khari, attracting crowds from across the district. (Source: CKA Archives)','Friday Market (Shukravar Bazaar) in Pirlote is a weekly open-air market with sections for vegetables, fruits, dry fish, hardware, clothes, and toast-khari, attracting crowds from across the district. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21706,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/sports-games/dilip-vengsarkar1-00bcc9b9.jpg','Dilip Vengsarkar[1]','Dilip Vengsarkar[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DilipVengsarkar.jpg'),(21726,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/stories/the-thibaw-wada1-05dc854a.png','The Thibaw Wada[1]','The Thibaw Wada[1]','https://www.holidify.com/collections/things-to-do-in-ratnagiri'),(21729,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/stories/shyam-chi-aai2-591834e9.png','Shyam Chi Aai[2]','Shyam Chi Aai[2]','https://www.amazon.in/Shyamchi-Aai-Pandurang-Sadashiv-Sane/dp/1974690555'),(21732,'culture/images/maharashtra/ratnagiri/stories/konkan-petroglyphs3-abc8a2ba.png','Konkan Petroglyphs[3]','Konkan Petroglyphs[3]','https://kevinstandagephotography.wordpress.com/2019/03/14/the-konkan-petroglyphs-introduction/'),(21774,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/tanpuras-displayed-at-a-workshop-in-sitarmake_1r5Robb.png','Tanpuras displayed at a workshop in Sitarmaker Galli, Miraj.[1]','Tanpuras displayed at a workshop in Sitarmaker Galli, Miraj.[1]','https://www.sahapedia.org/string-masters-sitarmakers-of-miraj'),(21776,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/craftsmen-working-together-on-a-tanpura-in-mi_QomK4xX.png','Craftsmen working together on a tanpura in Miraj, continuing a centuries-old tradition of musical instrument making.[2]','Craftsmen working together on a tanpura in Miraj, continuing a centuries-old tradition of musical instrument making.[2]','https://www.sahapedia.org/string-masters-sitarmakers-of-miraj'),(21780,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/a-group-of-women-skillfully-draw-a-beautiful-_yEXxyDp.jpg','A group of women skillfully draw a beautiful rangoli of Bhagwan Ram at the Ayodhya Nagari Festival held in Sangli at the Neeminath Nagar ground. (Source: CKA Archives)','A group of women skillfully draw a beautiful rangoli of Bhagwan Ram at the Ayodhya Nagari Festival held in Sangli at the Neeminath Nagar ground. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21781,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/the-completed-rangoli-of-bhagwan-ram-at-the-a_QPsvABX.jpg','The completed rangoli of Bhagwan Ram at the Ayodhya Nagari Festival in Sangli.(Source: CKA Archives)','The completed rangoli of Bhagwan Ram at the Ayodhya Nagari Festival in Sangli.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21786,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/entrance-of-the-sangli-state-museum-sangli-ci_7loBb0W.png','Entrance of the Sangli State Museum, Sangli City.[3]','Entrance of the Sangli State Museum, Sangli City.[3]','https://www.ixigo.com/web-stories/top-10-places-to-visit-in-sangli.html'),(21790,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/vishnudas-bhave-natya-vidyamandir-in-sangli4-dcc0d0aa.jpg','Vishnudas Bhave Natya Vidyamandir in Sangli.[4]','Vishnudas Bhave Natya Vidyamandir in Sangli.[4]','https://vishnudasbhavenatyamandirsangli.com/'),(21794,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/bal-gandharva5-6541bea8.png','Bal Gandharva[5]','Bal Gandharva[5]','https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0304152/'),(21798,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/artforms/vishnu-khandekar6-4b406a6d.png','Vishnu Khandekar[6]','Vishnu Khandekar[6]','https://te.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%B0%B5%E0%B0%BF%E0%B0%B7%E0%B1%8D%E0%B0%A3%E0%B1%81_%E0%B0%B8%E0%B0%96%E0%B0%BE%E0%B0%B0%E0%B0%BE%E0%B0%82_%E0%B0%96%E0%B0%BE%E0%B0%82%E0%B0%A1%E0%B1%87%E0%B0%95%E0%B0%B0%E0%B1%8D'),(21812,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-28-ft-monolithic-marble-statue-of-b_9TJJXWo.jpg','The 28 ft. monolithic marble statue of Bahubali at the base of Kumbhojgiri Hill, Sangli.[1]','The 28 ft. monolithic marble statue of Bahubali at the base of Kumbhojgiri Hill, Sangli.[1]','http://exploremaharashtra.blogspot.com/2011/05/bahubali-hill-temples-are-located-27-km.html'),(21816,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/entrance-to-shri-dattatraya-audumbar-ma_LFm8HOs.jpg','Entrance to Shri Dattatraya Audumbar Mandir, located on the banks of the Krishna River in Bhilawadi, Sangli district.(Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance to Shri Dattatraya Audumbar Mandir, located on the banks of the Krishna River in Bhilawadi, Sangli district.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21818,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/a-bhakt-touches-his-head-to-the-ground-_Y9oJUgm.jpg','A bhakt touches his head to the ground to seek blessings of Adi Dattatraya.(Source: CKA Archives)','A bhakt touches his head to the ground to seek blessings of Adi Dattatraya.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21820,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/a-huge-ghat-has-been-built-in-front-of-_waCHGPl.jpg','A huge ghat has been built in front of the Shri Dattatraya Audumbar Mandir. Devotees gather along the ghat to take a dip in the holy Krishna river, to cleanse themselves as they seek her blessings.(Source: CKA Archives)','A huge ghat has been built in front of the Shri Dattatraya Audumbar Mandir. Devotees gather along the ghat to take a dip in the holy Krishna river, to cleanse themselves as they seek her blessings.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21823,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/intriguing-nag-serpent-design-above-the_2Qj4KiF.jpg','Intriguing nag (serpent) design above the gateway of Girilingeshwar Mandir, located on the Girling plateau in Sangli district. (Source: CKA Archives)','Intriguing nag (serpent) design above the gateway of Girilingeshwar Mandir, located on the Girling plateau in Sangli district. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21824,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-entire-structure-blends-naturally-w_d5m2lno.jpg','The entire structure blends naturally with the plateau’s landscape. It is supported by intricately carved stone pillars, and includes a number of caves. Some of these go deep into the hillside and serve practical purposes, such as storing utensils for mahaprasad (a sacred communal meal).(Source: CKA Archives)','The entire structure blends naturally with the plateau’s landscape. It is supported by intricately carved stone pillars, and includes a number of caves. Some of these go deep into the hillside and serve practical purposes, such as storing utensils for mahaprasad (a sacred communal meal).(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21830,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/irwin-bridge-over-the-krishna-river-bui_EbywcgG.jpg','Irwin Bridge over the Krishna River, built in 1929 during British rule.(Source: CKA Archives)','Irwin Bridge over the Krishna River, built in 1929 during British rule.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21832,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/architectural-detail-on-irwin-bridge-wh_9VZaw3H.jpg','Architectural detail on Irwin Bridge which was built using brick masonry and features floral detailing along certain portions, reflecting the design aesthetics of the time.(Source: CKA Archives)','Architectural detail on Irwin Bridge which was built using brick masonry and features floral detailing along certain portions, reflecting the design aesthetics of the time.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21833,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/shri-krishnamai-mandir-seen-from-sarkar_ZtB32EL.jpg','Shri Krishnamai Mandir seen from Sarkari Ghat near the Irwin Bridge in Sangli; the structure often submerges during seasonal floods.(Source: CKA Archives)','Shri Krishnamai Mandir seen from Sarkari Ghat near the Irwin Bridge in Sangli; the structure often submerges during seasonal floods.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21839,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/main-entrance-of-the-dargah-complex-a-s_xw2HThl.jpg','Main entrance of the dargah complex, a site of pilgrimage for followers from across the region.(Source: CKA Archives)','Main entrance of the dargah complex, a site of pilgrimage for followers from across the region.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21843,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/entrance-to-the-revansiddha-mandir-in-r_9YgcmxI.png','Entrance to the Revansiddha Mandir, in Renavi, Sangli district.[2]','Entrance to the Revansiddha Mandir, in Renavi, Sangli district.[2]','https://myadhyatm.com/shri-revansiddha-mandir-renavisanglimaharashtra/'),(21847,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-sangameshwar-mandir-at-haripur-in-s_wfqHIZW.jpg','The Sangameshwar Mandir at Haripur in Sangli. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Sangameshwar Mandir at Haripur in Sangli. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21849,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-garbhagriha-sanctum-of-the-mandir-w_C76ni9J.jpg','The garbhagriha (sanctum) of the Mandir, which features very old and beautifully carved pillars. (Source: CKA Archives)','The garbhagriha (sanctum) of the Mandir, which features very old and beautifully carved pillars. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21850,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/a-deepstambh-a-column-illuminated-with-_G3SC4l1.jpg','A deepstambh (a column illuminated with oil lamps or diyas which can be commonly found in Hindu mandirs) which lies outside the entrance of the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)','A deepstambh (a column illuminated with oil lamps or diyas which can be commonly found in Hindu mandirs) which lies outside the entrance of the Mandir. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21853,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/entrance-to-sangli-fort-sangli-city-bui_uJCqQb4.jpg','Entrance to Sangli fort, Sangli city built by Shrimant Chintaman Rao Patwardhan in the early 19th century. (Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance to Sangli fort, Sangli city built by Shrimant Chintaman Rao Patwardhan in the early 19th century. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21855,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/darbar-hall-at-sangli-fort-used-for-off_sVdJ3qr.jpg','Darbar Hall at Sangli fort, used for official proceedings during the Patwardhan rule. (Source: CKA Archives)','Darbar Hall at Sangli fort, used for official proceedings during the Patwardhan rule. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21857,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/cannons-positioned-at-the-entrance-of-t_8ru9wER.jpg','Cannons positioned at the entrance of the Darbar Hall, part of the original fort complex. (Source: CKA Archives)','Cannons positioned at the entrance of the Darbar Hall, part of the original fort complex. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21860,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/view-of-the-shri-ganesh-mandir-in-centr_zD22zmm.jpg','View of the Shri Ganesh Mandir in central Sangli city. (Source: CKA Archives)','View of the Shri Ganesh Mandir in central Sangli city. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21861,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-grand-entrance-of-the-shri-ganesh-m_JgDoUhI.jpg','The grand entrance of the Shri Ganesh Mandir, which stands out from the surrounding structures due to the use of red sandstone.(Source: CKA Archives)','The grand entrance of the Shri Ganesh Mandir, which stands out from the surrounding structures due to the use of red sandstone.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21863,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/a-life-size-statue-of-shri-chintamanrao_gWbHRKP.jpg','A life size statue of Shri Chintamanrao Appasaheb-I Patwardhan (1775-1851) which lies in the garden adjacent to the mandir (Source: CKA Archives)','A life size statue of Shri Chintamanrao Appasaheb-I Patwardhan (1775-1851) which lies in the garden adjacent to the mandir (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21867,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-magnificent-entrance-to-the-tasgaon_jJxP9hJ.jpg','The magnificent entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, Tasgaon City, Sangli.  (Source: CKA Archives)','The magnificent entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, Tasgaon City, Sangli.  (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21869,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-beautiful-gopuram-of-the-tasgaon-ga_A06tBIX.jpg','The beautiful gopuram of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, it is described in the district Gazetteer (1969) to be “unrivalled in beauty and magnificence in this part of the country.” (Source: CKA Archives)','The beautiful gopuram of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, it is described in the district Gazetteer (1969) to be “unrivalled in beauty and magnificence in this part of the country.” (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21870,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/cultural-sites/the-beautiful-garbhagriha-of-the-tasgao_04Bq2Zi.jpg','The beautiful garbhagriha of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir where Rajasthani paintings adorn the ceiling walls and portraits of the famous Patwardhan family can be found. (Source: CKA Archives)','The beautiful garbhagriha of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir where Rajasthani paintings adorn the ceiling walls and portraits of the famous Patwardhan family can be found. (Source: CKA Archives)','');
INSERT INTO `culture_imageblock` VALUES (21893,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/festivals-fairs/the-mhasoba-yatra-at-banpuri-brings-to_394c0vy.png','The Mhasoba Yatra at Banpuri brings together hundreds of people in a vibrant celebration of the gramdevta, Mhasoba.[1]','The Mhasoba Yatra at Banpuri brings together hundreds of people in a vibrant celebration of the gramdevta, Mhasoba.[1]','https://utsav.gov.in/view-event/sangli-mhasoba-yatra-1'),(21903,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/festivals-fairs/the-magnificent-entrance-to-the-tasgao_v83SxPi.jpg','The magnificent entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, Tasgaon City, Sangli.  (Source: CKA Archives)','The magnificent entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, Tasgaon City, Sangli.  (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21916,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/mutton-kharda1-8c006b6a.png','Mutton Kharda[1]','Mutton Kharda[1]','https://kalimirchbysmita.com/how-to-make-mutton-kharda/'),(21920,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/turmericfingers2-9f3644b5.png','Turmericfingers[2]','Turmericfingers[2]','https://m.indiamart.com/proddetail/sangli-turmeric-finger-20901553912.html'),(21923,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/olya-haldicha-loncha3-81caada2.png','Olya Haldicha Loncha[3]','Olya Haldicha Loncha[3]','https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=0Qz4p2bYZN4'),(21929,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/traditional-makar-sankranti-thali-bhogichi-bhaji-_4ZAWQt5.png','Traditional Makar Sankranti Thali (bhogichi bhaji, bajra bhakri, methi, kharda and til sweets) (Source: CKA Archives)','Traditional Makar Sankranti Thali (bhogichi bhaji, bajra bhakri, methi, kharda and til sweets) (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21935,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/santra-desi-daarusource-cka-archives-5e8c03b8.png','Santra: Desi Daaru(Source: CKA Archives)','Santra: Desi Daaru(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21937,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/misrisource-cka-archives-b2734443.jpg','Misri(Source: CKA Archives)','Misri(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21941,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/chakolya-source-cka-archives-83e60818.jpg','Chakolya (Source: CKA Archives)','Chakolya (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21944,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/kadhi-vadasource-cka-archives-f6d9d19e.png','Kadhi Vada(Source: CKA Archives)','Kadhi Vada(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21947,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/sangli-special-bhel-source-cka-archives-cd90e829.png','Sangli Special Bhel (Source: CKA Archives)','Sangli Special Bhel (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21950,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/chapati-bhajjisource-cka-archives-39ece642.png','Chapati Bhajji(Source: CKA Archives)','Chapati Bhajji(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(21953,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/food/image-no-caption-0495307e.jpg','Image (no caption)','Image (no caption)',''),(21979,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/markets/a-vendor-selling-baskets-made-out-of-bamboo-at_16ZijVo.jpg','A vendor selling baskets made out of bamboo at Burud Galli. (Source: CKA Archives)','A vendor selling baskets made out of bamboo at Burud Galli. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21982,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/markets/vegetable-vendors-at-chhatrapati-shivaji-mahar_6CHlSxg.jpg','Vegetable vendors at Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Market, one of Sangli’s oldest and busiest retail markets. (Source: CKA Archives)','Vegetable vendors at Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Market, one of Sangli’s oldest and busiest retail markets. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(21987,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/markets/vendors-at-laxmi-market-in-miraj-continue-to-s_0Q5wjlq.jpg','Vendors at Laxmi Market in Miraj continue to sell fresh produce under the historic market’s original roofed structure, built over a century ago. (Source: CKA Archives)','Vendors at Laxmi Market in Miraj continue to sell fresh produce under the historic market’s original roofed structure, built over a century ago. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22019,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/sports-games/a-kusti-ground-in-sangli-20141-78cf2c70.jpg','A Kusti Ground in Sangli, 2014[1]','A Kusti Ground in Sangli, 2014[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kusti_maidan.jpg'),(22052,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/stories/the-patwardhan-mahal1-54fea5ae.png','The Patwardhan Mahal[1]','The Patwardhan Mahal[1]','https://in.worldorgs.com/catalog/sangli/city-government-office/patwardhan-palace-sangli-rajwada'),(22055,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/stories/parasuram-bhau2-a554091b.png','Parasuram Bhau[2]','Parasuram Bhau[2]','https://mohinik.blogspot.com/2015/02/parshuram-bahu-patwardhan.html'),(22058,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/stories/mahadevs-mandir3-c480670c.png','Mahadev’s Mandir[3]','Mahadev’s Mandir[3]','https://www.facebook.com/people/Kargani-Aatpadi-Sangali/100067224982813/?locale=fr_FR'),(22063,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/stories/chouranginath-hill-station-sonsal4-e6e37604.png','Chouranginath Hill Station, Sonsal[4]','Chouranginath Hill Station, Sonsal[4]','https://www.roaring-india.com/chouranginath-hill-station-sonsal-kadegaon/'),(22070,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/stories/yayati5-cef8c91f.png','Yayati[5]','Yayati[5]','https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/33224711-yayati'),(22079,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/entrance-to-the-tasgaon-ganpati-mandir-ne_ScpG2C0.jpg','Entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir near the Patwardhan Rajwada. (Source: CKA Archives)','Entrance to the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir near the Patwardhan Rajwada. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22081,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/seven-storeyed-gopuram-of-the-tasgaon-gan_dV64Ffq.jpg','Seven-storeyed gopuram of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, commended for its intricate carvings and exceptional design. (Source: CKA Archives)','Seven-storeyed gopuram of the Tasgaon Ganpati Mandir, commended for its intricate carvings and exceptional design. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22084,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/the-grand-entrance-of-shri-ganesh-mandir-_JNDRq45.jpg','The grand entrance of Shri Ganesh Mandir, built with red sandstone. (Source: CKA Archives)','The grand entrance of Shri Ganesh Mandir, built with red sandstone. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22086,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/main-mandir-of-shri-ganesh-constructed-in_jbaKmBh.jpg','Main Mandir of Shri Ganesh, constructed in black stone in 1843. (Source: CKA Archives)','Main Mandir of Shri Ganesh, constructed in black stone in 1843. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22089,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/irwin-bridge-over-the-krishna-river-built_dPFcMCL.jpg','Irwin Bridge over the Krishna River, built in 1929 during British rule. (Source: CKA Archives)','Irwin Bridge over the Krishna River, built in 1929 during British rule. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22091,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/architectural-detailing-on-irwin-bridge-i_Hdpa4ch.jpg','Architectural detailing on Irwin Bridge, including brick masonry and floral motifs typical of colonial design. (Source: CKA Archives)','Architectural detailing on Irwin Bridge, including brick masonry and floral motifs typical of colonial design. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22097,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/the-central-courtyard-of-sanglis-rajwada-_ykO1xck.jpg','The central courtyard of Sangli’s Rajwada, showcasing its distinctive blue wooden pillars and the many rooms that lie within it. (Source: CKA Archives)','The central courtyard of Sangli’s Rajwada, showcasing its distinctive blue wooden pillars and the many rooms that lie within it. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22099,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/the-wada-has-a-beautiful-timber-framework_WJJKgqC.jpg','The Wada has a beautiful timber framework and many joinery details which can be seen at the upper sections of the wooden columns. These are features typical of Wada architecture yet so distinctly interpreted. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Wada has a beautiful timber framework and many joinery details which can be seen at the upper sections of the wooden columns. These are features typical of Wada architecture yet so distinctly interpreted. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22100,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/the-vibrant-blue-on-the-wooden-pillars-gi_jKKNuRu.jpg','The vibrant blue on the wooden pillars give the structure an aesthetic look. Notably, the pillar’s construction, with a stone base, is a typical feature of wada architecture. Additionally, notice the unique roofing system, featuring a ‘gable end’ at the far right corner, beneath which the roof slopes. (Source: CKA Archives)','The vibrant blue on the wooden pillars give the structure an aesthetic look. Notably, the pillar’s construction, with a stone base, is a typical feature of wada architecture. Additionally, notice the unique roofing system, featuring a ‘gable end’ at the far right corner, beneath which the roof slopes. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22102,'culture/images/maharashtra/sangli/architecture/the-walls-of-the-rajwada-are-adorned-with_e7S7Vvn.jpg','The walls of the Rajwada are adorned with beautiful paintings and drawings. In frame is a drawing of Nandi alongside the pair of Bhagwan Shiv and Devi Parvati, Kartik aboard his vahan- peacock, rishis, and parrots. (Source: CKA Archives)','The walls of the Rajwada are adorned with beautiful paintings and drawings. In frame is a drawing of Nandi alongside the pair of Bhagwan Shiv and Devi Parvati, Kartik aboard his vahan- peacock, rishis, and parrots. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22116,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/main-gateway-of-ajinkyatara-fort-with-hig_gSI2pcX.jpg','Main gateway of Ajinkyatara Fort with high buttresses, located near the northwest corner of the fort.[1]','Main gateway of Ajinkyatara Fort with high buttresses, located near the northwest corner of the fort.[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Gateway,_Ajinkyatara_02.jpg'),(22117,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/shambhu-mahadev-mandir-shikhar-shingnapur_G2ON6S5.jpg','Shambhu Mahadev Mandir, Shikhar Shingnapur—stone-built Mandir with carved spire, housing twin Shivlings representing Shiv and Parvati.[3]','Shambhu Mahadev Mandir, Shikhar Shingnapur—stone-built Mandir with carved spire, housing twin Shivlings representing Shiv and Parvati.[3]','https://mr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%B0_%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%A3%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%82%E0%A4%B0#/media/%E0%A4%9A%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0:Shikhar-Shingnapur-2.jpg'),(22120,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/shambhu-mahadev-mandir-shikhar-shingnapur_yb1omaf.png','Shambhu Mahadev Mandir, Shikhar Shingnapur—stone-built Mandir with carved spire, housing twin Shivlings representing Shiv and Parvati.[3]','Shambhu Mahadev Mandir, Shikhar Shingnapur—stone-built Mandir with carved spire, housing twin Shivlings representing Shiv and Parvati.[3]','https://mr.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%96%E0%A4%B0_%E0%A4%B6%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%A3%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%AA%E0%A5%82%E0%A4%B0#/media/%E0%A4%9A%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0:Shikhar-Shingnapur-2.jpg'),(22124,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/jabareshwar-mandir-in-phaltan-a-rock-cut-_ijeOSel.png','Jabareshwar Mandir in Phaltan, a rock-cut Hemadpanti structure carved from a single stone around 1237 CE.[4]','Jabareshwar Mandir in Phaltan, a rock-cut Hemadpanti structure carved from a single stone around 1237 CE.[4]','https://hi.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E0%A4%9A%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B0:Jabreshwar_Mandir,Phaltan.jpg'),(22128,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/santoshgad-a-medieval-hill-fort-in-basalt_UUn7BEp.png','Santoshgad, a medieval hill fort in basalt stone, on the Mhasoba mountain range near Phaltan.[5]','Santoshgad, a medieval hill fort in basalt stone, on the Mhasoba mountain range near Phaltan.[5]','https://www.mtdc.co.in/forts/santoshgad-fort/'),(22132,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/vishveshwar-mandir-at-sangam-mahuli-built_66izVFn.jpg','Vishveshwar Mandir at Sangam Mahuli, built in 1735 CE by Shripatrao Pant Pratinidhi in Hemadpanthi style. (Source: CKA Archives)','Vishveshwar Mandir at Sangam Mahuli, built in 1735 CE by Shripatrao Pant Pratinidhi in Hemadpanthi style. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22136,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-view-of-the-old-palace-featuring-it_XJYwws1.png','Front view of the Old Palace featuring its multi-wing structure and carved wooden balconies.[6]','Front view of the Old Palace featuring its multi-wing structure and carved wooden balconies.[6]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_Rajwada-Satara-Maharashtra.jpg'),(22140,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-view-of-the-new-palace-showing-its-_y7rqQhK.png','Front view of the New Palace showing its solid structure and Indo-European architectural elements.[7]','Front view of the New Palace showing its solid structure and Indo-European architectural elements.[7]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Rajwada2-Satara-Maharashtra.jpg'),(22144,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/phaltan-rajwada-located-in-phaltan-town-o_k2YrWkL.png','Phaltan Rajwada, located in Phaltan town of Satara district, blends Indo-Saracenic architecture Jain and Hindu styles.[8]','Phaltan Rajwada, located in Phaltan town of Satara district, blends Indo-Saracenic architecture Jain and Hindu styles.[8]','https://www.peepultree.world/livehistoryindia/story/monuments/phaltan-rajwada'),(22150,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-elevation-of-bakulicha-wada-the-mai_GEayhGu.jpg','Front elevation of Bakulicha Wada. The main entrance is framed symmetrically with a central doorway and windows above, a layout typical of many traditional wadas.(Source: CKA Archives)','Front elevation of Bakulicha Wada. The main entrance is framed symmetrically with a central doorway and windows above, a layout typical of many traditional wadas.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22152,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/the-front-landscape-features-large-trees-_DGidFbM.jpg','The front landscape features large trees and a low stone edging. This border acts as both seat and tree guard.(Source: CKA Archives)','The front landscape features large trees and a low stone edging. This border acts as both seat and tree guard.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22154,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/view-of-the-entrance-steps-at-bakulicha-w_UxFQAdC.jpg','View of the entrance steps at Bakulicha Wada. The elevated plinth and wide stone staircase give the building a commanding presence from the street. A Tulsi Vrundavan sits at the threshold, while a marigold toran marks the main wooden doorway.(Source: CKA Archives)','View of the entrance steps at Bakulicha Wada. The elevated plinth and wide stone staircase give the building a commanding presence from the street. A Tulsi Vrundavan sits at the threshold, while a marigold toran marks the main wooden doorway.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22156,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/wooden-door-of-the-entrance-the-spikes-ac_hfg2qg7.jpg','Wooden door of the entrance. The spikes act as embellishment, while also providing protection. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden door of the entrance. The spikes act as embellishment, while also providing protection. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22157,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/there-is-also-an-iron-chain-used-to-secur_r8edE04.jpg','There is also an iron chain, used to secure the door. (Source: CKA Archives)','There is also an iron chain, used to secure the door. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22159,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/cantilevered-wooden-balcony-on-the-first-_l4mY2L3.jpg','Cantilevered wooden balcony on the first floor. Timber brackets and simple railing elements support and frame the projection.(Source: CKA Archives)','Cantilevered wooden balcony on the first floor. Timber brackets and simple railing elements support and frame the projection.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22161,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/interior-wooden-door-with-a-padlock-syste_hUXeQYA.jpg','Interior wooden door with a padlock system. (Source: CKA Archives)','Interior wooden door with a padlock system. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22163,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/the-window-at-the-exterior-is-adorned-wit_wyntQ22.jpg','The window at the exterior is adorned with stone arches. The ‘jali’ (steel grills) provide protection while showcasing the ingenuity of local artisans. (Source: CKA Archives)','The window at the exterior is adorned with stone arches. The ‘jali’ (steel grills) provide protection while showcasing the ingenuity of local artisans. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22164,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/arched-brick-framed-windows-with-iron-jal_OV0pieq.jpg','Arched brick-framed windows with iron jalis. The placement aligns with the building’s symmetrical front facade. (Source: CKA Archives)','Arched brick-framed windows with iron jalis. The placement aligns with the building’s symmetrical front facade. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22166,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/deep-window-recess-functioning-as-a-seati_E9BZXff.jpg','Deep window recess functioning as a seating niche. The depth allows for casual occupation of the space while maintaining a degree of privacy, which, in many ways, reflects the controlled visual access typical of wada interiors.(Source: CKA Archives)','Deep window recess functioning as a seating niche. The depth allows for casual occupation of the space while maintaining a degree of privacy, which, in many ways, reflects the controlled visual access typical of wada interiors.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22168,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/one-of-the-wooden-columns-of-the-wada-not_C8505Pt.jpg','One of the wooden columns of the Wada. Notice the decorative carvings present on the top half of the pilaster. This style of embellishing was common during the olden eras and can also be seen in mandirs today. (Source: CKA Archives)','One of the wooden columns of the Wada. Notice the decorative carvings present on the top half of the pilaster. This style of embellishing was common during the olden eras and can also be seen in mandirs today. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22169,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/timber-column-with-carved-detailing-at-th_MpbgZzg.jpg','Timber column with carved detailing at the top. The carving reflects ornamentation styles typical of regional domestic architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)','Timber column with carved detailing at the top. The carving reflects ornamentation styles typical of regional domestic architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22171,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/a-niche-with-a-ganpati-murti-inside-the-w_Bd5CNCJ.jpg','A niche with a Ganpati Murti inside the Wada. Red flowers are placed as offerings here which are tied to a cultural element. Notably, it is believed that red flowers are Ganpati’s favourite. One can notice red hibiscus flowers offered to the Devata. (Source: CKA Archives)','A niche with a Ganpati Murti inside the Wada. Red flowers are placed as offerings here which are tied to a cultural element. Notably, it is believed that red flowers are Ganpati’s favourite. One can notice red hibiscus flowers offered to the Devata. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22174,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/a-changing-skyline-along-khalcha-rasta-wh_VEWDonq.jpg','A changing skyline along Khalcha Rasta, where older forms remain alongside newer ones. (Source: CKA Archives)','A changing skyline along Khalcha Rasta, where older forms remain alongside newer ones. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22176,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/side-view-of-the-two-storey-wada-built-in_0zx1fcA.jpg','Side view of the two-storey wada, built in Shaka 1861 (1939 CE) and currently owned by the Shete Brothers.(Source: CKA Archives)','Side view of the two-storey wada, built in Shaka 1861 (1939 CE) and currently owned by the Shete Brothers.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22178,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-view-of-the-interesting-curved-stru_etdGRYK.jpg','Front view of the interesting curved structure of the Khalsa Wada where shops and residences occupy different storeys. (Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the interesting curved structure of the Khalsa Wada where shops and residences occupy different storeys. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22180,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/ground-floor-shop-front-with-wooden-panel_AVG21dT.jpg','Ground-floor shop front with wooden panel doors. Above, the metal-sheet roof is supported by a distinct framework.(Source: CKA Archives)','Ground-floor shop front with wooden panel doors. Above, the metal-sheet roof is supported by a distinct framework.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22181,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/a-wider-view-of-a-ground-floor-shop-front_32Zxta4.jpg','A wider view of a ground floor shop front which has a distinct design language that distinguishes it from the upper floors of the Wada.(Source: CKA Archives)','A wider view of a ground floor shop front which has a distinct design language that distinguishes it from the upper floors of the Wada.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22182,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/rear-access-stairway-leading-to-the-resid_cr1S7wK.jpg','Rear access stairway leading to the residential level. The area is used informally for drying and storage.(Source: CKA Archives)','Rear access stairway leading to the residential level. The area is used informally for drying and storage.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22184,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/balcony-doors-with-timber-arches-and-deta_3xo9mRn.jpg','Balcony doors with timber arches and detailed woodwork, distinct from the design of the doors of the ground floor.(Source: CKA Archives)','Balcony doors with timber arches and detailed woodwork, distinct from the design of the doors of the ground floor.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22185,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/detail-of-the-balcony-arch-timber-is-used_Hmu1sFH.jpg','Detail of the balcony arch. Timber is used to frame and highlight the curve, adding an ornamental layer to the elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)','Detail of the balcony arch. Timber is used to frame and highlight the curve, adding an ornamental layer to the elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22187,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/balcony-with-decorative-cast-iron-railing_Jbb06B4.jpg','Balcony with decorative cast iron railings and timber supports. Modern advertisement boards occupy part of the upper railing. Notice the uniformity in the design language here, indicating that this area is a shared space.(Source: CKA Archives)','Balcony with decorative cast iron railings and timber supports. Modern advertisement boards occupy part of the upper railing. Notice the uniformity in the design language here, indicating that this area is a shared space.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22189,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/a-closeup-of-the-cast-iron-railingsource-_WWiTmXp.jpg','A closeup of the cast iron railing(Source: CKA Archives)','A closeup of the cast iron railing(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22191,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-facing-windows-with-brick-arches-an_xoplbrA.jpg','Front-facing windows with brick arches and timber panels. The symmetry and alignment define the elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)','Front-facing windows with brick arches and timber panels. The symmetry and alignment define the elevation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22192,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/arched-brick-framed-windows-with-timber-s_kMo3akz.jpg','Arched brick-framed windows with timber shutters on the front façade. The repetition of form and proportion contributes to the overall symmetry of the building. (Source: CKA Archives)','Arched brick-framed windows with timber shutters on the front façade. The repetition of form and proportion contributes to the overall symmetry of the building. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22193,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/close-view-of-arched-brick-window-and-woo_kejShJl.jpg','Close view of arched brick window and wooden shutters. Notice the intricate brick masonry within which the windows are set.(Source: CKA Archives)','Close view of arched brick window and wooden shutters. Notice the intricate brick masonry within which the windows are set.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22195,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/high-set-rear-windows-with-iron-grills-th_WPvBXY3.jpg','High-set rear windows with iron grills. Their placement reflects functional needs rather than ornamentation.(Source: CKA Archives)','High-set rear windows with iron grills. Their placement reflects functional needs rather than ornamentation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22197,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/in-the-corners-of-the-building-inscriptio_awGsAD6.jpg','In the corners of the building, Inscriptions noting the name of the wada and its date of construction are carved into the surface—features typical of buildings constructed in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. A clock is also mounted on the upper corner of the façade, visible from the street below. (Source: CKA Archives)','In the corners of the building, Inscriptions noting the name of the wada and its date of construction are carved into the surface—features typical of buildings constructed in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. A clock is also mounted on the upper corner of the façade, visible from the street below. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22198,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/two-sculpted-figures-flank-a-carved-date-_H2iB65F.jpg','Two sculpted figures flank a carved date panel at the building’s corner. The exaggerated features and expressions suggest a protective or symbolic role, though their specific meaning is uncertain. The inscription carved here reads “Shake 1861”, corresponding to the year 1939 CE in the Gregorian calendar. This likely indicates the date of construction. Note: The Shaka calendar begins in 78 CE. To convert a Shaka year to the Gregorian calendar, 78 years are added. (Source: CKA Archives)','Two sculpted figures flank a carved date panel at the building’s corner. The exaggerated features and expressions suggest a protective or symbolic role, though their specific meaning is uncertain. The inscription carved here reads “Shake 1861”, corresponding to the year 1939 CE in the Gregorian calendar. This likely indicates the date of construction. Note: The Shaka calendar begins in 78 CE. To convert a Shaka year to the Gregorian calendar, 78 years are added. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22201,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/front-view-of-the-residential-building-on_zdbmXKk.jpg','Front view of the residential building. One notices a shop on the ground floor, which seems to be frequented by locals. An advertisement hoarding of Patanjali is hung up on the first floor balcony. (Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the residential building. One notices a shop on the ground floor, which seems to be frequented by locals. An advertisement hoarding of Patanjali is hung up on the first floor balcony. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22203,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/tall-floor-length-windows-on-the-ground-f_ZGGkZPk.jpg','Tall, floor-length windows on the ground floor with balusters. Wooden arches above the doors show craftsmanship. Inside, a tile mosaic is visible.(Source: CKA Archives)','Tall, floor-length windows on the ground floor with balusters. Wooden arches above the doors show craftsmanship. Inside, a tile mosaic is visible.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22205,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/the-windows-on-the-upper-floor-with-slant_YIJg96U.jpg','The windows on the upper floor, with slanted construction allowing for maximum sunlight. The design on the windows is simpler than the grand windows on the ground floor.(Source: CKA Archives)','The windows on the upper floor, with slanted construction allowing for maximum sunlight. The design on the windows is simpler than the grand windows on the ground floor.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22207,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/main-entrance-to-the-residence-beside-the_ltS0Nna.jpg','Main entrance to the residence beside the shop. Decorative woodwork frames the door, and a torans hangs above.(Source: CKA Archives)','Main entrance to the residence beside the shop. Decorative woodwork frames the door, and a torans hangs above.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22209,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/a-devli-which-is-used-to-place-murtis-of-_t87ALtQ.jpg','A devli which is used to place Murtis of Devtas and Devis. As they hold their murtis, notice how these Devlis are constructed higher up than other Devlis. It is said that they are structured in this way to denote importance to the Murti placed inside. (Source: CKA Archives)','A devli which is used to place Murtis of Devtas and Devis. As they hold their murtis, notice how these Devlis are constructed higher up than other Devlis. It is said that they are structured in this way to denote importance to the Murti placed inside. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22210,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/another-devli-constructed-at-an-elevated-_1DS7T1Z.jpg','Another devli constructed at an elevated height, which is typically used for housing murtis of Devis & Devtas.(Source: CKA Archives)','Another devli constructed at an elevated height, which is typically used for housing murtis of Devis & Devtas.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22211,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/smaller-devli-to-the-side-of-a-doorway-co_DVV6UqF.jpg','Smaller Devli to the side of a doorway. Commonly used for placing diyas during religious or festive occasions.(Source: CKA Archives)','Smaller Devli to the side of a doorway. Commonly used for placing diyas during religious or festive occasions.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22213,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/interior-wooden-doors-each-is-constructed_Zf5ekmS.jpg','Interior wooden doors. Each is constructed in a similar structure, with slight differences based on function and room type.(Source: CKA Archives)','Interior wooden doors. Each is constructed in a similar structure, with slight differences based on function and room type.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22214,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/the-door-features-a-pale-yellow-and-white_ACnglPV.jpg','The door features a pale yellow and white color palette, accented by an orange border. (Source: CKA Archives)','The door features a pale yellow and white color palette, accented by an orange border. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22216,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/wooden-railing-of-the-ground-floor-shop-p_KWAXtBq.jpg','Wooden railing of the ground floor shop. Primarily functional in its purpose.(Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden railing of the ground floor shop. Primarily functional in its purpose.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22218,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/cast-iron-balcony-railing-with-timber-fra_WxiK2YY.jpg','Cast iron balcony railing with timber framing. Much of the railing is concealed behind a shop hoarding.(Source: CKA Archives)','Cast iron balcony railing with timber framing. Much of the railing is concealed behind a shop hoarding.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22220,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/cast-iron-pattern-framed-within-wooden-co_AIsXEWf.jpg','Cast iron pattern framed within wooden column elements. The motif continues along the vertical axis of the façade.(Source: CKA Archives)','Cast iron pattern framed within wooden column elements. The motif continues along the vertical axis of the façade.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22221,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/architecture/simpler-railing-designs-were-constructed-_GtNvTS9.jpg','Simpler railing designs were constructed on the upper floor, offering basic protection while maintaining visual continuity with the rest of the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)','Simpler railing designs were constructed on the upper floor, offering basic protection while maintaining visual continuity with the rest of the structure. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22232,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/shivam-ingale-a-male-lavani-performer-from-sa_X3Ju2Mh.png','Shivam Ingale, a male Lavani performer from Satara.[1]','Shivam Ingale, a male Lavani performer from Satara.[1]','https://www.news18.com/viral/he-didnt-accept-defeat-despite-being-discouraged-by-people-the-story-of-lavani-king-shivam-7748215.html'),(22236,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/the-inaugural-rock-dhokra-piece-crafted-at-de_8mkOWxT.png','The inaugural Rock Dhokra piece crafted at Devrai Art Village, depicting a Nature Devi. The artwork integrates brass casting with natural stone, which is said to mark the introduction of this technique.[2]','The inaugural Rock Dhokra piece crafted at Devrai Art Village, depicting a Nature Devi. The artwork integrates brass casting with natural stone, which is said to mark the introduction of this technique.[2]','https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/60c6f7db9866bd2e2163b4ff/a3ae2500-eaba-4e8e-8b01-46db3da3fd90/14.jpg?format=750w'),(22237,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/the-dancing-girl-of-mohenjodaro-a-figurine-fr_Mgbaw74.png','The Dancing Girl of Mohenjodaro, a figurine from around 2500 BCE, often cited as an early example of metal casting techniques similar to Dhokra.[3]','The Dancing Girl of Mohenjodaro, a figurine from around 2500 BCE, often cited as an early example of metal casting techniques similar to Dhokra.[3]','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg/300px-Dancing_girl_of_Mohenjo-daro.jpg'),(22241,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/shri-bhavani-museum-in-aundh-satara4-b6600c2e.jpg','Shri Bhavani Museum in Aundh, Satara.[4]','Shri Bhavani Museum in Aundh, Satara.[4]','https://x.com/micnewdelhi/status/1078134205580746758'),(22245,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/shri-chhatrapati-shivaji-maharaj-museum-satar_Gi2jGty.jpg','Shri Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Museum, Satara.[5]','Shri Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Museum, Satara.[5]','https://www.justdial.com/Satara/Shri-Chhatrapati-Shivaji-Museum-Near-St-Stand-Satara-HO/9999P2162-2162-130731161227-X3M7_BZDET'),(22249,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/shri-shahu-kala-mandir6-d28815e1.jpg','Shri Shahu Kala Mandir[6]','Shri Shahu Kala Mandir[6]','https://www.justdial.com/Satara/Shahu-Kala-Mandir-Near-Rajwada-Rajwada/9999P2162-2162-141122132538-H4S7_BZDET'),(22252,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/the-devrai-art-village-an-art-centre-at-panch_sE3g8lk.png','The Devrai Art Village, an art centre at Panchgani.[7]','The Devrai Art Village, an art centre at Panchgani.[7]','https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/60c6f7db9866bd2e2163b4ff/0c40633e-0ba8-4e52-958d-df8ec5da51c7/DSC06138-01.jpeg'),(22257,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/musicians-such-as-vocalist-venkatesh-kumar-an_4mtzrVc.png','Musicians such as vocalist Venkatesh Kumar and tabla player Praveen Karkare performing at the Aundh Sangeet Mahotsav, held in 2020.[8]','Musicians such as vocalist Venkatesh Kumar and tabla player Praveen Karkare performing at the Aundh Sangeet Mahotsav, held in 2020.[8]','https://caravanmagazine.in/arts/rural-classical-music-festival-unites-aficionados'),(22262,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/yamunabai-waikar-at-the-1999-gunijan-gaurav-s_hfiPPJj.png','Yamunabai Waikar at the 1999 Gunijan Gaurav Sohala in Vile Parle, an event held to honour 75 distinguished personalities from diverse fields.[9]','Yamunabai Waikar at the 1999 Gunijan Gaurav Sohala in Vile Parle, an event held to honour 75 distinguished personalities from diverse fields.[9]','https://www.uttungtrust.org/photo-archive-2022/photo-archive-1999/'),(22266,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/dr-shriram-lagoo10-fbde4852.jpg','Dr. Shriram Lagoo[10]','Dr. Shriram Lagoo[10]','https://www.rangabhoomi.com/news/dr-shriram-lagoo-death-anniversary/'),(22270,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/artforms/vasant-bapat11-c52fcefe.png','Vasant Bapat[11]','Vasant Bapat[11]','https://sadhanaprakashan.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Vasant-Bapat1.jpg'),(22283,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/cultural-sites/image-no-caption-00cbc023.png','Image (no caption)','Image (no caption)',NULL),(22285,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/cultural-sites/image-no-caption-7b5cf898.png','Image (no caption)','Image (no caption)',NULL),(22292,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/festivals-fairs/musicians-such-as-vocalist-venkatesh-k_CcQA0sL.png','Musicians such as vocalist Venkatesh Kumar and tabla player Praveen Karkare performing at the Aundh Sangeet Mahotsav, held in 2020.[1]','Musicians such as vocalist Venkatesh Kumar and tabla player Praveen Karkare performing at the Aundh Sangeet Mahotsav, held in 2020.[1]','https://caravanmagazine.in/arts/rural-classical-music-festival-unites-aficionados'),(22296,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/festivals-fairs/the-towering-bagad-pole-with-the-bagad_1O0PZlV.png','The towering Bagad pole with the ‘Bagadswar’ suspended by hooks, fulfilling a centuries-old vow during the Bhairavnath Bagad Yatra at Bavdhan, Satara.[2]','The towering Bagad pole with the ‘Bagadswar’ suspended by hooks, fulfilling a centuries-old vow during the Bhairavnath Bagad Yatra at Bavdhan, Satara.[2]','https://utsav.gov.in/view-event/bagad-yatra-of-bavdhan-1'),(22306,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/festivals-fairs/jalmandir-palace-satarathe-present-res_GaQka7A.png','Jalmandir Palace, Satara—the present residence of Chhatrapati Udayanraje Bhosale, with gardens and Jagdamba Mata Mandir within the complex.[3]','Jalmandir Palace, Satara—the present residence of Chhatrapati Udayanraje Bhosale, with gardens and Jagdamba Mata Mandir within the complex.[3]','https://yappe.in/maharashtra/satara/jalmandir-palace/125208'),(22361,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/koyana-dairy1-de33bce1.png','Koyana Dairy[1]','Koyana Dairy[1]','https://www.koyanadudh.com/products.html'),(22366,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/kurdai2-2ec6f19e.png','Kurdai[2]','Kurdai[2]','https://india.neelamfoodland.in/products/wheat-kurdai-150-gm'),(22372,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/sugarcane-pulled-by-ox-in-satara3-b431ff73.png','Sugarcane pulled by Ox in Satara[3]','Sugarcane pulled by Ox in Satara[3]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Migratory_sugarcane_cutter_communities_struggling_for_livelihood_-_carrying_sugarcane_factory,_Koregaon-Satara,_Maharashtra,_December_2018.jpg'),(22374,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/strawberries-being-plucked-by-tourists-in-a-farm-_QgaxMol.png','Strawberries being plucked by tourists in a farm in Mahabaleshwar[4]','Strawberries being plucked by tourists in a farm in Mahabaleshwar[4]','https://revolvingcompass.com/strawberry-picking-at-a-strawberry-farm-in-mahabaleshwar/'),(22391,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/kandi-pedhe5-9dae956b.png','Kandi Pedhe[5]','Kandi Pedhe[5]','https://www.amazon.in/NSatvik-Satari-Kandi-Pedhe-Peda/dp/B09Z7Y6FYT'),(22394,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/strawberry-cream6-850dc8d5.png','Strawberry Cream[6]','Strawberry Cream[6]','https://zeezest.com/food/top-9-famous-foods-from-mahabaleshwar-you-have-to-try-3465#strawberry-cream'),(22396,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/mapro-factory7-f6a6e0d7.jpg','Mapro Factory[7]','Mapro Factory[7]','https://mahabaleshwartourism.in/mapro-garden-mahabaleshwar#google_vignette'),(22400,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/food/mapro-factory7-940b3d8a.png','Mapro Factory[7]','Mapro Factory[7]','https://mahabaleshwartourism.in/mapro-garden-mahabaleshwar#google_vignette'),(22438,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/sports-games/mallakhamb-ground-in-satara-source-cka-ar_ywfWmy5.jpg','Mallakhamb Ground in Satara (Source: CKA Archives)','Mallakhamb Ground in Satara (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22442,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/sports-games/cricket-being-played-on-the-koteshwar-mai_pZkXVaN.png','Cricket being played on the Koteshwar Maidan (Source: CKA Archives)','Cricket being played on the Koteshwar Maidan (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22446,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/sports-games/football-being-played-at-the-talim-sangh-_IYXijlp.png','Football being played at the Talim Sangh Maidan Satara (Source: CKA Archives)','Football being played at the Talim Sangh Maidan Satara (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22481,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/stories/pratapgad1-a7f3238a.png','Pratapgad[1]','Pratapgad[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pratapgarh'),(22483,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/stories/afzal-khan-and-shivaji-maharaj2-fe5023a9.png','Afzal Khan and Shivaji Maharaj[2]','Afzal Khan and Shivaji Maharaj[2]','https://navbharattimes.indiatimes.com/navbharatgold/thumb/msid-103517952,width-1200,height-630,imgsize-127084,resizemode-6/we-the-people/why-and-how-chhatrapati-shivaji-killed-afzal-khan.jpg'),(22486,'culture/images/maharashtra/satara/stories/banganga-river-near-phaltan3-7c2c8b57.png','Banganga river near Phaltan.[3]','Banganga river near Phaltan.[3]','https://mr-m-wikipedia-org.translate.goog/wiki/%E0%A4%AC%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A3%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%82%E0%A4%97%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%A8%E0%A4%A6%E0%A5%80_(%E0%A4%B8%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A4%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%B0%E0%A4%BE_%E0%A4%9C%E0%A4%BF%E0%A4%B2%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE)?_x_tr_sl=mr&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp'),(22493,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/kunkeshwar-mandir-in-sindhudurg-built_rlkVre6.jpg','Kunkeshwar Mandir in Sindhudurg, built in Dravidian style, overlooking the Arabian Sea. (Source: CKA Archives)','Kunkeshwar Mandir in Sindhudurg, built in Dravidian style, overlooking the Arabian Sea. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22497,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/vijaydurg-fort-a-key-stronghold-of-th_duilElR.png','Vijaydurg Fort, a key stronghold of the Maratha navy along the Konkan coast, with laterite walls rising from the Vaghotan Creek.[1]','Vijaydurg Fort, a key stronghold of the Maratha navy along the Konkan coast, with laterite walls rising from the Vaghotan Creek.[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vijaydurg_Fort'),(22501,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/lakshminarayan-mandir-in-walaval-sind_tyve43p.jpg','Lakshminarayan Mandir in Walaval, Sindhudurg, built in the 14th century in Hemadpanthi style with teakwood construction. (Source: CKA Archives)','Lakshminarayan Mandir in Walaval, Sindhudurg, built in the 14th century in Hemadpanthi style with teakwood construction. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22505,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/sindhudurg-fort-built-by-shivaji-maha_bXO3viy.png','Sindhudurg Fort, built by Shivaji Maharaj in the 17th century, showcases coastal military architecture on Kurte Island in the Arabian Sea.[2]','Sindhudurg Fort, built by Shivaji Maharaj in the 17th century, showcases coastal military architecture on Kurte Island in the Arabian Sea.[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sindhudurg_Fort,_Maharashtra,_India_%282017%29.jpg'),(22511,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-sawantwadi-palace-framed-by-cocon_lPvEIAR.jpg','The Sawantwadi Palace, framed by coconut groves and set against a backdrop of Narendra Hill. (Source: CKA Archives)','The Sawantwadi Palace, framed by coconut groves and set against a backdrop of Narendra Hill. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22513,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/side-elevation-of-the-facade-of-sawan_535Zfdw.jpg','Side elevation of the facade of Sawantwadi Palace showcasing a blend of traditional wada-style planning with English-style arches. The use of locally sourced laterite stone (chira) reflects adaptation to regional materials and climate. (Source: CKA Archives)','Side elevation of the facade of Sawantwadi Palace showcasing a blend of traditional wada-style planning with English-style arches. The use of locally sourced laterite stone (chira) reflects adaptation to regional materials and climate. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22515,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-impressive-main-gateway-pravesadv_3aXaxYM.jpg','The impressive main gateway (pravesadvara) to the Sawantwadi Palace complex in Sindhudurg. The structure showcases influence from both European and Maharashtrian architectural elements, characteristic of coastal Maharashtra\'s historical buildings. (Source: CKA Archives)','The impressive main gateway (pravesadvara) to the Sawantwadi Palace complex in Sindhudurg. The structure showcases influence from both European and Maharashtrian architectural elements, characteristic of coastal Maharashtra\'s historical buildings. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22517,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-central-tower-features-a-pointed-_KBUU3bp.jpg','The central tower features a pointed archway, a round oculus window, and a small balcony inspired by traditional jharokhas. These elements, combined with the symmetrical layout and use of red laterite stone, reflect a blend of local building practices and colonial-era design influences. (Source: CKA Archives)','The central tower features a pointed archway, a round oculus window, and a small balcony inspired by traditional jharokhas. These elements, combined with the symmetrical layout and use of red laterite stone, reflect a blend of local building practices and colonial-era design influences. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22519,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-main-gate-combines-practical-secu_Uj4hu0v.jpg','The main gate combines practical security with formal architectural detailing, including a smaller pedestrian panel within a larger arched frame. (Source: CKA Archives)','The main gate combines practical security with formal architectural detailing, including a smaller pedestrian panel within a larger arched frame. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22520,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/this-door-shows-typical-features-of-d_x1cXXhn.jpg','This door shows typical features of domestic design, with a solid wood frame and subtle decorative elements. (Source: CKA Archives)','This door shows typical features of domestic design, with a solid wood frame and subtle decorative elements. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22521,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/wooden-door-with-iron-grills-combines_4gieNaF.jpg','Wooden door with iron grills. Combines ventilation and safety, with a latch-and-bolt system and minimalist detailing. (Source: CKA Archives)','Wooden door with iron grills. Combines ventilation and safety, with a latch-and-bolt system and minimalist detailing. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22522,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/painted-in-pastel-green-the-door-is-s_2XcSYRl.jpg','Painted in pastel green, the door is shaded by an umbrella-style overhang, featuring coloured glass and ornamental detailing. (Source: CKA Archives)','Painted in pastel green, the door is shaded by an umbrella-style overhang, featuring coloured glass and ornamental detailing. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22524,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/a-series-of-palace-windows-featuring-_zlUa4yi.jpg','A series of palace windows featuring protectivechajjas. These small overhanging canopies, commonly found in traditional architecture, provide shade and rain protection while adding a layer of detail to the façades. (Source: CKA Archives)','A series of palace windows featuring protectivechajjas. These small overhanging canopies, commonly found in traditional architecture, provide shade and rain protection while adding a layer of detail to the façades. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22525,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/white-brickwork-frames-this-inset-arc_n15JZD6.jpg','White brickwork frames this inset arched window, adding contrast to the red laterite wall. (Source: CKA Archives)','White brickwork frames this inset arched window, adding contrast to the red laterite wall. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22526,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/modern-wooden-window-recessed-into-th_QTeRbB9.jpg','Modern wooden window recessed into the wall. Notice the minimal design and simplistic design. (Source: CKA Archives)','Modern wooden window recessed into the wall. Notice the minimal design and simplistic design. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22527,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/traditional-window-with-wooden-panels_HRVpF0w.jpg','Traditional window with wooden panels on the outside. This provides security, while also maintaining the wooden, brown appearance of the palace. (Source: CKA Archives)','Traditional window with wooden panels on the outside. This provides security, while also maintaining the wooden, brown appearance of the palace. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22529,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/front-view-of-the-clay-tiled-roof-the_tuO0cX2.jpg','Front view of the clay-tiled roof. The overlapping curved tiles create a textured pattern, typical of roofing systems used in coastal Konkan architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the clay-tiled roof. The overlapping curved tiles create a textured pattern, typical of roofing systems used in coastal Konkan architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22530,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/side-view-of-the-sloped-roof-the-roof_rJGZ3IS.jpg','Side view of the sloped roof. The roof’s angled design efficiently handles monsoon rains, with wide eaves offering shade and protection. (Source: CKA Archives)','Side view of the sloped roof. The roof’s angled design efficiently handles monsoon rains, with wide eaves offering shade and protection. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22532,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/zinc-plated-ceiling-of-the-darbar-hal_B3lFq1f.jpg','Zinc-plated ceiling of the Darbar Hall with intricate geometric motifs and a chandelier from the 1880s. (Source: CKA Archives)','Zinc-plated ceiling of the Darbar Hall with intricate geometric motifs and a chandelier from the 1880s. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22533,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/portraits-of-royal-ancestors-in-the-b_hdJUk2J.jpg','Portraits of royal ancestors in the background of the Darbar Hall chandelier. (Source: CKA Archives)','Portraits of royal ancestors in the background of the Darbar Hall chandelier. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22535,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/indoor-staircase-of-the-palace-notice_YkWBh74.jpg','Indoor staircase of the Palace. Notice the intricate iron designs of the grills. The steps are made of stone, which is said to be a common feature of old construction. (Source: CKA Archives)','Indoor staircase of the Palace. Notice the intricate iron designs of the grills. The steps are made of stone, which is said to be a common feature of old construction. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22539,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-house-follows-a-linear-plan-with-_VegxMWg.jpg','The house follows a linear plan with a sloped clay tile roof and sits along an internal village road. Its quiet form reflects traditional construction practices of the region. (Source: CKA Archives)','The house follows a linear plan with a sloped clay tile roof and sits along an internal village road. Its quiet form reflects traditional construction practices of the region. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22541,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/thick-layers-of-mud-form-the-exterior_wOzADh1.jpg','Thick layers of mud form the exterior walls, offering insulation and climate responsiveness. (Source: CKA Archives)','Thick layers of mud form the exterior walls, offering insulation and climate responsiveness. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22542,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/built-from-local-stone-the-compound-w_i1tY6jd.jpg','Built from local stone, the compound wall defines the house’s edge and anchors it to the site. (Source: CKA Archives)','Built from local stone, the compound wall defines the house’s edge and anchors it to the site. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22544,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/overlapping-tiles-and-extended-eaves-_pcUMrya.jpg','Overlapping tiles and extended eaves help manage rainfall and protect the walls below. (Source: CKA Archives)','Overlapping tiles and extended eaves help manage rainfall and protect the walls below. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22545,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/the-roofing-system-is-held-up-by-a-co_NT3P4l6.jpg','The roofing system is held up by a combination of bamboo and timber members, with no added ceiling, which is said to be a typical feature in traditional rural houses that allows heat to rise and escape naturally. (Source: CKA Archives)','The roofing system is held up by a combination of bamboo and timber members, with no added ceiling, which is said to be a typical feature in traditional rural houses that allows heat to rise and escape naturally. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22547,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/a-raised-tulsi-planter-marks-the-fron_vOPfemt.jpg','A raised Tulsi planter marks the front courtyard, whose placement and presence has become something that is tied to a cultural practice and can be commonly found across homes in Maharashtra. (Source: CKA Archives)','A raised Tulsi planter marks the front courtyard, whose placement and presence has become something that is tied to a cultural practice and can be commonly found across homes in Maharashtra. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22549,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/open-courtyard-space-in-front-of-the-_ccWjFHe.jpg','Open courtyard space in front of the house. Used for growing herbs, drying grains, and daily outdoor activities. (Source: CKA Archives)','Open courtyard space in front of the house. Used for growing herbs, drying grains, and daily outdoor activities. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22551,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/double-leafed-wooden-door-a-simple-fr_jOEF2TT.jpg','Double-leafed wooden door. A simple frame with recessed panels and a traditional locking system. (Source: CKA Archives)','Double-leafed wooden door. A simple frame with recessed panels and a traditional locking system. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22553,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/architecture/small-louvered-window-with-wooden-fra_U2zlUX7.jpg','Small louvered window with wooden frame. The angled wooden slats allow ventilation while offering shade and privacy. (Source: CKA Archives)','Small louvered window with wooden frame. The angled wooden slats allow ventilation while offering shade and privacy. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22569,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-traditional-dashavatar-performance-bein_zEWaeoo.jpg','A traditional Dashavatar performance being staged at night in Sindhudurg, as a large audience gathers to watch the vibrant retelling of epic stories. (Source: CKA Archives)','A traditional Dashavatar performance being staged at night in Sindhudurg, as a large audience gathers to watch the vibrant retelling of epic stories. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22575,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/some-chitrakathi-paintings-originally-mad_2dtKu8D.jpg','Some Chitrakathi paintings, originally made on teak leaves, are now created on handmade paper using red, green, and blue. Over 350-year-old examples are displayed at the TAKA Museum, Sindhudurg. (Source: CKA Archives)','Some Chitrakathi paintings, originally made on teak leaves, are now created on handmade paper using red, green, and blue. Over 350-year-old examples are displayed at the TAKA Museum, Sindhudurg. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22579,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-display-of-pangul-bail-art-featuring-de_U4VlyKz.jpg','A display of Pangul Bail art, featuring decorative cloths, ornaments, and models of bulls used by theThakarcommunityduring performances. (Source: CKA Archives)','A display of Pangul Bail art, featuring decorative cloths, ornaments, and models of bulls used by theThakarcommunityduring performances. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22582,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-display-of-tools-instruments-and-househ_igOOxcp.jpg','A display of tools, instruments, and household items used by the Pingali (Vasudev) performers in Pinguli village. (Source: CKA Archives)','A display of tools, instruments, and household items used by the Pingali (Vasudev) performers in Pinguli village. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22585,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-curated-display-of-instruments-and-ritu_K0Pkg5h.jpg','A curated display of instruments and ritual objects used in Gondhal. Visible here are the sambal drums, devi diwati (ritual lamp), tuntune (stringed percussion), zanja (cymbals), and gungaroo (ankle bells), arranged around the Gondhalacha Maand. (Source: CKA Archives).','A curated display of instruments and ritual objects used in Gondhal. Visible here are the sambal drums, devi diwati (ritual lamp), tuntune (stringed percussion), zanja (cymbals), and gungaroo (ankle bells), arranged around the Gondhalacha Maand. (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(22588,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-display-of-costumes-and-instruments-use_FyAniYJ.jpg','A display of costumes and instruments used in Radha Nritya, a folk dance performed in the Konkan region. Featured here are traditional jewellery pieces like bashing and bangadya, accessories like ambada (hair bun with flowers), and the vibrant Radha costume. Musical instruments such as the huduk drum and zanja (cymbals) accompany the performance, while a sketch illustrates a typical dance scene. (Source: CKA Archives)','A display of costumes and instruments used in Radha Nritya, a folk dance performed in the Konkan region. Featured here are traditional jewellery pieces like bashing and bangadya, accessories like ambada (hair bun with flowers), and the vibrant Radha costume. Musical instruments such as the huduk drum and zanja (cymbals) accompany the performance, while a sketch illustrates a typical dance scene. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22592,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/instruments-used-in-powada-performances-f_pHRcQzq.jpg','Instruments used in Powada performances from Sindhudurg—huduk (drum), tambora (string instrument), and taal(cymbals)—are displayed here alongside a traditional Ganesh painting and an illustration of performers. (Source: CKA Archives)','Instruments used in Powada performances from Sindhudurg—huduk (drum), tambora (string instrument), and taal(cymbals)—are displayed here alongside a traditional Ganesh painting and an illustration of performers. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22595,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/an-exhibit-showcasing-the-craft-ofkalsutr_SkghqM7.jpg','An exhibit showcasing the craft ofKalsutri Bahulya(string puppetry) from Pinguli, highlighting both puppet body parts and complete figures. On the left are carved components like heads, hands, legs, masks, and tools used by the Thakar community to create wooden puppets. On the right are finished puppets of characters likeRam,Laxman, andGanpati, dressed in vibrant costumes. Unlike Rajasthan’s cloth-basedkathputali, Pinguli puppets are made of wood—demonstrating the unique craftsmanship of the Thakar artists. (Source: CKA Archives)','An exhibit showcasing the craft ofKalsutri Bahulya(string puppetry) from Pinguli, highlighting both puppet body parts and complete figures. On the left are carved components like heads, hands, legs, masks, and tools used by the Thakar community to create wooden puppets. On the right are finished puppets of characters likeRam,Laxman, andGanpati, dressed in vibrant costumes. Unlike Rajasthan’s cloth-basedkathputali, Pinguli puppets are made of wood—demonstrating the unique craftsmanship of the Thakar artists. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22598,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/shadow-puppets-used-by-the-thakar-communi_U5IrKwf.jpg','Shadow puppets used by the Thakar community to tell stories throughKalsutri Bahulya. These leather puppets, painted in vibrant colours, are brought to life with songs and dialogues during performances. (Source: CKA Archive)','Shadow puppets used by the Thakar community to tell stories throughKalsutri Bahulya. These leather puppets, painted in vibrant colours, are brought to life with songs and dialogues during performances. (Source: CKA Archive)',''),(22603,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-colourful-collection-of-traditional-woo_nzCj6sH.jpg','A colourful collection of traditional wooden toys and figurines, often seen in local markets across Maharashtra. These handcrafted pieces, painted in bright natural dyes, depict everyday village life, occupations, and characters (Source: CKA Archives).','A colourful collection of traditional wooden toys and figurines, often seen in local markets across Maharashtra. These handcrafted pieces, painted in bright natural dyes, depict everyday village life, occupations, and characters (Source: CKA Archives).',''),(22607,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a-hand-paintedganjifacard-from-sawantwadi_YWDPj05.jpg','A hand-paintedGanjifacard from Sawantwadi, made on wood and decorated with fine detailing. Though originally used for playing, these cards are now valued for their artistic craftsmanship.(Source: CKA Archives)','A hand-paintedGanjifacard from Sawantwadi, made on wood and decorated with fine detailing. Though originally used for playing, these cards are now valued for their artistic craftsmanship.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22612,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/f3368ff1fcf34b21a097039a95520474-89a044d9.png','','',''),(22618,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/the-wata-a-traditional-wax-based-instrume_lVUg4Mh.jpg','The Wata, a traditional wax-based instrument and dining plate, on display at the Thakar Adivasi Kala Angan (TAKA) Museum, Pinguli.(Source: CKA Archives).','The Wata, a traditional wax-based instrument and dining plate, on display at the Thakar Adivasi Kala Angan (TAKA) Museum, Pinguli.(Source: CKA Archives).',''),(22622,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/a7224715883949feb3255a8fd5ec757d-67f72ca1.jpg','','',''),(22625,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/e10849da344c4480b2cee65c6ba7edc4-22fc41d4.jpg','','',''),(22628,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/f9671cfeae2f4d20aed0027f3d86067a-c04dd696.png','','',''),(22632,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/89580d9a86fd4fd18759353a5af8b52f-5813a1b6.png','','',''),(22636,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/abefca5dce854d7687593b4517d6d239-7b392965.jpg','','',''),(22640,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/jayawant-dalvi5-fd22fccf.png','Jayawant Dalvi[5]','Jayawant Dalvi[5]','https://dnyangangabooks.com/collections/jaywant-dalvi'),(22645,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/artforms/f5abebee26c640db86a24cf73c7328dc-c2c46864.jpg','','',''),(22660,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/the-exterior-of-sri-bandeshwar-mand_W1o0VZi.jpg','The exterior of Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, Banda village, Sindhudurg. (Source: CKA Archives)','The exterior of Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, Banda village, Sindhudurg. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22662,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/intricately-designed-pillars-inside_fT984lT.jpg','Intricately designed pillars inside the Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, which are likely indicative of the skilled craftsmanship seen in mandir architecture of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)','Intricately designed pillars inside the Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, which are likely indicative of the skilled craftsmanship seen in mandir architecture of the period. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22664,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/the-ornately-carved-ceiling-of-the-_Xenb08R.jpg','The ornately carved ceiling of the Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, showcasing traditional stonework techniques found in regional mandir architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)','The ornately carved ceiling of the Sri Bandeshwar Mandir, showcasing traditional stonework techniques found in regional mandir architecture. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22665,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/an-interesting-motif-on-the-walls-o_g6PqhSC.jpg','An interesting motif on the walls of Shri Bandeshwar Mandir, Banda, Sindhudurg district(Source: CKA Archives)','An interesting motif on the walls of Shri Bandeshwar Mandir, Banda, Sindhudurg district(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22668,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/the-exterior-view-of-bhagwati-mandi_DeFzVvH.jpg','The exterior view of Bhagwati Mandir, Dhamapur, Sindhudurg district (Source: CKA Archives)','The exterior view of Bhagwati Mandir, Dhamapur, Sindhudurg district (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22669,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/cultural-sites/bhagwati-devi-inside-the-mandir-dha_PIRFk5q.png','Bhagwati Devi inside the Mandir, Dhamapur, Sindhudurg district (Source: CKA Archives)','Bhagwati Devi inside the Mandir, Dhamapur, Sindhudurg district (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(22673,'culture/image