LJt.jpg','Steamed Nevarya filled with sweet coconut and jaggery saran, a festive delicacy of the region. (Source: CKA Archives)','Steamed Nevarya filled with sweet coconut and jaggery saran, a festive delicacy of the region. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22809,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/food/soft-and-spongy-amboli-a-konkan-favourite-mad_P6dmGKB.jpg','Soft and spongy Amboli, a Konkan favourite made from fermented rice and dal batter. (Source: CKA Archives)','Soft and spongy Amboli, a Konkan favourite made from fermented rice and dal batter. (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22812,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/food/shirwale-ani-naralacha-ras-source-cka-archive_jGvFfx2.jpg','Shirwale ani Naralacha Ras (Source: CKA Archives)','Shirwale ani Naralacha Ras (Source: CKA Archives)',NULL),(22814,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/food/image-no-caption-64948510.jpg','Image (no caption)','Image (no caption)',NULL),(22832,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/language/title-cards-of-popular-tv-serials-that-co_sV8AaO1.png','Title cards of popular TV serials that contained plot or characters speaking in Malwani. Gaav Gaata Gazali (Zee Marathi), a light-hearted TV serial that showcases village life, folk traditions, and daily humor, all in rich Malwani speech.[1]','Title cards of popular TV serials that contained plot or characters speaking in Malwani. Gaav Gaata Gazali (Zee Marathi), a light-hearted TV serial that showcases village life, folk traditions, and daily humor, all in rich Malwani speech.[1]','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaav_Gata_Gajali'),(22833,'culture/images/maharashtra/sindhudurg/language/ratris-khel-chale-translthe-game-runs-at-_oiAgRwZ.png','Ratris Khel Chale (transl.The Game Runs at Night) is a Marathi-Malwani supernatural thriller television series that premiered on Zee Marathi on 22 February 2016. Set in Sawantwadi, the story follows the Naik family, who speak in Malwani and encounter a series of mysterious and unexplainable events.[2]