ir is a Vesara-styleMandirbuilt in black basalt, blending Nagara and Dravidian architectural features.[1]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shiv_Mandir,_Ambernath.jpg'),(23427,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/intricate-carvings-and-sculptures-adorn-th_n2cFtwM.png','Intricate carvings and sculptures adorn the outer walls of Ambarnath Shiv Mandir.[2]','Intricate carvings and sculptures adorn the outer walls of Ambarnath Shiv Mandir.[2]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20180928172926_IMG_1753.jpg'),(23431,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/bastions-and-stone-fortification-walls-of-_Ri9j0bn.png','Bastions and stone fortification walls of Ghodbunder Fort, built in the hill fort (Giri Durg) architectural style using locally quarried stone.[3]','Bastions and stone fortification walls of Ghodbunder Fort, built in the hill fort (Giri Durg) architectural style using locally quarried stone.[3]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghodbunder_Fort.jpg'),(23435,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/entrance-of-shri-kopineshwar-mandir-reflec_aF2xmHi.png','Entrance of Shri Kopineshwar Mandir, reflecting the simple, functional construction typical of Maratha architectural style.[4]','Entrance of Shri Kopineshwar Mandir, reflecting the simple, functional construction typical of Maratha architectural style.[4]','https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shri_Kopineshwar_Mandir.jpg'),(23441,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/the-street-character-of-naupada-whereshops_Hy54qAT.jpg','The street character of Naupada whereshops open directly onto the footpath, with a continuous residential floor above, a common mixed-use typology in B-Cabin area of Naupada. (Source: CKA Archives)','The street character of Naupada whereshops open directly onto the footpath, with a continuous residential floor above, a common mixed-use typology in B-Cabin area of Naupada. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23443,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/front-elevation-of-the-rajput-building-sho_aqpYHTg.jpg','Front elevation of the Rajput Building showing ground-floor shops with a continuous balcony above, framed by cast iron railings. An interesting extended wall section above the balcony contains a row of clerestory vents just below the roofline. Notice how this element supports ventilation while also shaping the overall street-facing character of the building.(Source: CKA Archives)','Front elevation of the Rajput Building showing ground-floor shops with a continuous balcony above, framed by cast iron railings. An interesting extended wall section above the balcony contains a row of clerestory vents just below the roofline. Notice how this element supports ventilation while also shaping the overall street-facing character of the building.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23445,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/close-up-of-the-cast-iron-railing-along-th_3m1lU1U.jpg','Close-up of the cast iron railing along the balcony, with a repeating geometric pattern. Notice the level of detail in the design.(Source: CKA Archives)','Close-up of the cast iron railing along the balcony, with a repeating geometric pattern. Notice the level of detail in the design.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23447,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/timber-doors-with-a-raised-panel-design-an_fpiCDFh.jpg','Timber doors with a raised panel design and integrated ventilation openings open onto the balcony. Positioned just beneath the sloped metal roof, the doors and overhang together support airflow and provide protection from sun and rain.(Source: CKA Archives)','Timber doors with a raised panel design and integrated ventilation openings open onto the balcony. Positioned just beneath the sloped metal roof, the doors and overhang together support airflow and provide protection from sun and rain.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23451,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/view-of-the-old-house-at-the-junction-of-g_UEScjal.jpg','View of the old house at the junction of Gokhale Road and Vinayak Thakur Road. Painted in a bold yellow, the upper portion of the house stands out from behind the shops, hinting at its original character despite being partially concealed. (Source: CKA Archives)','View of the old house at the junction of Gokhale Road and Vinayak Thakur Road. Painted in a bold yellow, the upper portion of the house stands out from behind the shops, hinting at its original character despite being partially concealed. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23452,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/load-bearing-brick-walls-and-wooden-framed_6nAg0Xr.jpg','Load-bearing brick walls and wooden framed windows with ventilation panels of the structure suggest construction techniques that were common from the late 19th to early 20th century.(Source: CKA Archives)','Load-bearing brick walls and wooden framed windows with ventilation panels of the structure suggest construction techniques that were common from the late 19th to early 20th century.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23454,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/thebuildingsextended-roofline-creates-a-vi_7fJPCjX.jpg','Thebuilding’sextended roofline creates a visible edge along the upper portion of the facade. The bold yellow finish further accentuates the form, contrasting with the muted tones of the newer commercial layer in front.(Source: CKA Archives)','Thebuilding’sextended roofline creates a visible edge along the upper portion of the facade. The bold yellow finish further accentuates the form, contrasting with the muted tones of the newer commercial layer in front.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23457,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/view-of-the-residential-building-near-kopr_aBhTsRI.jpg','View of the residential building near Kopri Railway Bridge, with pastel green facade and street-facing commercial frontage. (Source: CKA Archives)','View of the residential building near Kopri Railway Bridge, with pastel green facade and street-facing commercial frontage. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23459,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/this-mid-century-building-reflects-quiet-b_i52SJU0.jpg','This mid-century building reflects quiet Bombay charm with its many geometric motifs. Shallow chajjas provide rain protection and rhythm to the design.(Source: CKA Archives)','This mid-century building reflects quiet Bombay charm with its many geometric motifs. Shallow chajjas provide rain protection and rhythm to the design.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23461,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/the-windows-now-enclosed-with-custom-box-g_1eAlXFB.jpg','The windows, now enclosed with custom box grills, serve as semi-private indoor spaces, a common adaptation in buildings facing busy streets. It’s a practical design, in many ways, shaped by climate, culture, and the need to make space in a growing city. (Source: CKA Archives)','The windows, now enclosed with custom box grills, serve as semi-private indoor spaces, a common adaptation in buildings facing busy streets. It’s a practical design, in many ways, shaped by climate, culture, and the need to make space in a growing city. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23462,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/old-wooden-windows-with-glass-panels-which_WQX8lxU.jpg','Old wooden windows with glass panels, which are double-doored and have vents are still visible, alongside later additions such as AC units and extended grills. (Source: CKA Archives)','Old wooden windows with glass panels, which are double-doored and have vents are still visible, alongside later additions such as AC units and extended grills. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23466,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/front-view-of-the-monalisa-building-showin_PlNeuld.jpg','Front view of the Monalisa Building, showing the central lift core and red water tank above. (Source: CKA Archives)','Front view of the Monalisa Building, showing the central lift core and red water tank above. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23468,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/commercial-units-along-the-main-road-form-_mETeQ9R.jpg','Commercial units along the main road form a continuous street-facing base for the building, reinforcing the plot boundary and supporting mixed-use activity. (Source: CKA Archives)','Commercial units along the main road form a continuous street-facing base for the building, reinforcing the plot boundary and supporting mixed-use activity. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23470,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/the-residential-entry-is-placed-along-a-qu_feD1ePx.jpg','The residential entry is placed along a quieter side lane, offering privacy and separating it from the building’s commercial frontage. (Source: CKA Archives)','The residential entry is placed along a quieter side lane, offering privacy and separating it from the building’s commercial frontage. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23472,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/capsule-shaped-window-embedded-in-the-lift_lJR56Jf.jpg','Capsule-shaped window embedded in the lift core.Possibly the most recognisable feature of the building, this window introduces a curved geometry that is carried forward in other elements. (Source: CKA Archives)','Capsule-shaped window embedded in the lift core.Possibly the most recognisable feature of the building, this window introduces a curved geometry that is carried forward in other elements. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23473,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/a-closer-view-of-the-capsule-shaped-window_uYVSpQ3.jpg','A closer view of the capsule-shaped window embedded in the lift core where one can see a curved motif, repeated across grills and other architectural features. (Source: CKA Archives)','A closer view of the capsule-shaped window embedded in the lift core where one can see a curved motif, repeated across grills and other architectural features. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23474,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/the-entrances-to-each-building-within-the-_B4td8OY.jpg','The entrances to each building within the complex repeat a capsule-shaped motif. This repetition contributes to a cohesive retro-futuristic aesthetic, setting the complex apart from the predominantly rectilinear residential forms of its time.(Source: CKA Archives)','The entrances to each building within the complex repeat a capsule-shaped motif. This repetition contributes to a cohesive retro-futuristic aesthetic, setting the complex apart from the predominantly rectilinear residential forms of its time.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23475,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/window-grills-differ-in-design-and-scale-a_0BhHDFY.jpg','Window grills differ in design and scale, added individually by flat owners over time, resulting in a patchwork of metalwork styles.(Source: CKA Archives)','Window grills differ in design and scale, added individually by flat owners over time, resulting in a patchwork of metalwork styles.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23476,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/shallow-concrete-chajjas-and-subtle-surfac_4nhzztp.jpg','Shallow concrete chajjas and subtle surface reliefs contribute to the building’s layered elevation and geometric variation.(Source: CKA Archives)','Shallow concrete chajjas and subtle surface reliefs contribute to the building’s layered elevation and geometric variation.(Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23480,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/apartment-towers-at-neelkanth-greens-with-_5DsOUK4.jpg','Apartment towers at Neelkanth Greens, with repetitive façades and a neutral colour palette. (Source: CKA Archives)','Apartment towers at Neelkanth Greens, with repetitive façades and a neutral colour palette. (Source: CKA Archives)',''),(23482,'culture/images/maharashtra/thane/architecture/with-multiple-towers-organized-within-a-si_0AEz3wO.jpg','With multiple towers organized within a single gated layout,Neelkan