ing a southward course. The Wainganga is characterized by its perennial nature and broad valley, creating fertile alluvial plains along its course. During the monsoon season, the river significantly swells, contributing to the groundwater recharge of the region.','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wainganga_River'),(22397,'statistic/images/maharashtra/gondia/environment/the-wainganga-river-dominates-the-draina_YCOkCNZ.png','The Wainganga River dominates the drainage system of the Gondia district, flowing through its central and western regions. This major river originates in the Mahadeo Hills of Madhya Pradesh and enters the district from the north, following a southward course. The Wainganga is characterized by its perennial nature and broad valley, creating fertile alluvial plains along its course. During the monsoon season, the river significantly swells, contributing to the groundwater recharge of the region.','The Wainganga River dominates the drainage system of the Gondia district, flowing through its central and western regions. This major river originates in the Mahadeo Hills of Madhya Pradesh and enters the district from the north, following a southward course. The Wainganga is characterized by its perennial nature and broad valley, creating fertile alluvial plains along its course. During the monsoon season, the river significantly swells, contributing to the groundwater recharge of the region.','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wainganga_River'),(22399,'statistic/images/maharashtra/gondia/environment/the-chulband-river-system-forms-another-_CoLRuAg.png','The Chulband River system forms another important tributary network in the district. This river flows through the northeastern sections, draining substantial agricultural areas. The Chulband is characterized by its seasonal flow pattern, with maximum discharge during the monsoon months. Its valley contains rich alluvial deposits that support intensive farming, particularly rice cultivation.','The Chulband River system forms another important tributary network in the district. This river flows through the northeastern sections, draining substantial agricultural areas. The Chulband is characterized by its seasonal flow pattern, with maximum discharge during the monsoon months. Its valley contains rich alluvial deposits that support intensive farming, particularly rice cultivation.','https://www.tourmyindia.com/states/maharashtra/chulbandh-dam-gondia.html'),(22403,'statistic/images/maharashtra/gondia/environment/bamboo-forests-form-a-significant-compon_Ch4alpD.png','Bamboo forests form a significant component of the district\'s vegetation, with Dendrocalamus strictus being the predominant bamboo species.','Bamboo forests form a significant component of the district\'s vegetation, with Dendrocalamus strictus being the predominant bamboo species.','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendrocalamus_strictus'),(22406,'statistic/images/maharashtra/gondia/environment/gondia-district-in-maharashtra-is-home-t_If1Yi51.png','Gondia district in Maharashtra is home to a variety of wildlife, with the tiger (Panthera tigris) being the top predator in the area. The Navegaon-Nagzira Tiger Reserve and nearby protected areas serve as vital habitats for these majestic cats. The tigers here are part of a larger population found throughout central India, using forest corridors to travel between different reserves. Their presence is a good sign of healthy forest ecosystems that can support large carnivores.','Gondia district in Maharashtra is home to a variety of wildlife, with the tiger (Panthera tigris) being the top predator in the area. The Navegaon-Nagzira Tiger Reserve and nearby protected areas serve as vital habitats for these majestic cats. The tigers here are part of a larger population found throughout central India, using forest corridors to travel between different reserves. Their presence is a good sign of healthy forest ecosystems that can support large carnivores.','https://www.millenniu